//! Loan conflicts and moved places in one typed body: native borrow checking for loans and moves.
//!
//! # When to use
//! Call [`check`] on a successfully typed, unselected body before it is published. A
//! [`Outcome.Conflict`] rejects the body with `LoanConflict` (the bootstrap's `OWN0010`),
//! `AccessDuringLoan` (`OWN0011`), `UseAfterMove` (`OWN0001`), `OverlappingAssignment` (`OWN0004`)
//! or `IncompatibleLoopHeader` (`OWN0005`), relating the earlier loan or move when there is one.
//!
//! # Details
//! The proof runs on the typed body. It numbers evaluation points in evaluation order and links
//! them into a control-flow graph. A loan
//! comes from a written borrow, a shared or mutable receiver pass, or a borrowed capture of a
//! constructed callable or section, which carries it like any value. A place behind a reference
//! names the referent's storage, so a reborrow is a loan of that place and carries the parent
//! reference's loans (BORROW-005). A loan carried by a value
//! stays live until the node that consumes that value, so a call argument's loan lasts for the
//! whole call (BORROW-004). A loan bound by `let` to a reference local stays live while that local
//! is live, by backward liveness over the graph, so loans end at their last use. An access that
//! overlaps a live loan conflicts as in the bootstrap: a shared borrow conflicts with an exclusive
//! loan, an exclusive borrow with any loan, a read with an exclusive loan, and a write or move with
//! any loan. Moves reach forward along the same graph until a binding or a covering replacement;
//! each loop compares the moved places of its outer locals at entry and on every back edge. A match
//! accesses its subject once as its form declares and branches to its arms in order; its bindings
//! are places of the subject (MATCH-001, MATCH-002).
//!
//! # Gotchas
//! Scope storage ends and observing cleanup run on every normal, return, failure, break and
//! continue path. Mutable holders have reaching per-assignment definitions, so an overwritten
//! value releases its old loans. A match subject owns a dense holder slot; a destructuring let
//! keeps that slot until its enclosing block, while match and if-let end it with the selected arm.
//! A required local loan beyond its storage end is `ExpiredLifetime` (OWN0019).
//!
//! A borrow of a value with no place lends its hidden owner (BORROW-006), a root the walk ends
//! where lowering drops it: with the innermost statement or match arm that evaluates it, or with
//! the condition, guard or short-circuit operand that does. A view of a temporary used past its
//! statement is OWN0019 at the use (CALL-003). Lowering keeps every temporary of a viewing
//! binding's initializer, or of a borrowing destructuring `let`'s subject, for the binding's scope,
//! so their storage and cleanup end there; only a viewing binding's borrowed array stays valid that
//! long, and any other temporary's loans expire with its statement. A binding typed by a type
//! parameter may view at an instance, so its temporaries are kept and expire that way too.
//!
//! A retaining write through a referent, replacing an exact callable environment with new capture
//! loans, or cleanup with unknown retained contents leaves the supported slice as `StoredLoans`. A projected replacement conservatively retains sibling
//! loans. Conflicts with approximate retention answer `Imprecise`, except that a loan a field store
//! gave a retaining local holder, which flows exactly, is still OWN0019 once required past its storage
//! end; a runtime index overlapping an exact element loan still rejects. A referent loan which
//! crosses a scope boundary leaves its external
//! validity relation to the region proof. Call results and projections retain precisely the
//! regions their types can name; parameters chosen outside the body cannot retain a fresh body
//! region, nor can a call result retain a body loan whose regions cannot outlive one it names. The
//! proof trusts callee contracts and never reads a callee body or MIR.

//! An invoked closure whose own body is not `Checked` may store any loan it carries where it can
//! write (CAPTURE-002, ANON-OWN-001): each body-local holder the invocation lends exclusively, and
//! whose type can retain a region, holds those loans from the invocation on, as do the holders a
//! call lends beside any argument that carries such a closure's loans, by value, by reference or
//! within a holder. A holder reached through a local reference that
//! holds loans may be body storage the walk cannot place, which leaves the slice as `StoredLoans`; a
//! reference parameter lent that way may receive a loan of body storage, so the body is never Checked.

//! Immediate execution drives, notifications, current-execution queries, relinquishing and package
//! construction, whose stored inputs typing proves detached, are calls to their catalog contracts.
//! Stored drives remain `StoredLoans`: their capture retention is not represented, and lowering
//! never emits one. A raw slot address consumes its slot and holds no loan.
//! Replacement is a write to its place; supported primitives are calls to their contracts.

import semantic.Types {TypeTable, Types}
import hir.Hir {Access, CallableMode, InfixOperator, OwnerKind}
import semantic.SourceLocations {Location}
import semantic.DeclarationId {DeclarationId, OwnerStep}
import semantic.ModuleId {InvalidModulePath, ModuleId}
import semantic.Lifetime {Lifetime}
import semantic.Rejection {RejectionCode}
import semantic.StorageOperation {StorageOperation}
import semantic.Type {Argument, Binding, KeptRegions, KeptSlot, KeptStep, KeptStepKind, Type}
import semantic.TypedBody {
  SectionRetention,
  AggregateField,
  ResultBorrow,
  BorrowStatus,
  CaptureHold,
  ConsumedPlace,
  Expression,
  BindingAccess,
  ImpliedOutlives,
  Local,
  MatchArm,
  MatchSyntax,
  Node,
  NodeId,
  NodeKind,
  Origin,
  PlaceStep,
  ReceiverPass,
  ReferentCapture,
  RunAccess,
  SafetyObligation,
  SubjectAccess,
  TypedBody,
}
import silk.allocator {Allocator, OutOfMemoryError}
import silk.bytes {Bytes}
import silk.effect {Effect}
import silk.testing {AssertionError, Testing}
import silk.option {Option}
import silk.ownership {Copy}
import silk.shared {Shared}
import silk.u64
import silk.usize
import silk.list {List}

/// What checking one body's loans and moves established.
pub enum Outcome {
  /// Every loan in the body is free of conflicts, and no moved place is used.
  Clear,
  /// An access conflicts with a live loan or uses a moved place, or a loop repeats with different
  /// moved places.
  Conflict,
  /// The body uses a form outside this slice; nothing is proved or rejected.
  NotChecked,
}

/// The outcome of checking one body. For a conflict, `access` is the rejected access or loop and
/// `earlier` the borrow or move it conflicts with, if any; otherwise `code` and `access` are unused.
///
/// Its spans count from the checked body's anchor, like the body's origins.
pub struct Verdict {
  pub outcome: Outcome
  /// For a clear body, `Checked` when [`regionClosed`] and nothing is pending, `Regions` otherwise;
  /// for an unchecked one, the reason.
  pub status: BorrowStatus
  pub code: RejectionCode
  pub access: Location
  pub earlier: Option<Location>
  /// Every loan conflict the body reports, the one above included, ordered by span as the
  /// bootstrap lists them; empty for a verdict that is not a loan conflict.
  pub reports: List<Report>
}

/// One reported conflict: the rejected access and, when `related`, the borrow or move it conflicts
/// with at `earlier`.
pub struct Report {
  pub code: RejectionCode
  pub access: Location
  pub related: bool
  pub earlier: Location
  /// For a conflicting borrow (OWN0010), whether the rejected borrow is exclusive.
  pub requestedExclusive: bool
  /// For a conflicting borrow (OWN0010), whether the active loan it conflicts with is exclusive.
  pub existingExclusive: bool
}

impl Copy for Report {}

// Records a conflict unless one with the same code and span was already found.
effect fn addReport(reports: &mut List<Report>, report: Report) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let found = List<Report>.asSlice(&reports.*)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < found.length {
    if found[at].code == report.code && found[at].access.start == report.access.start && found[at].access.end == report.access.end {
      return ()
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  run List<Report>.append(&mut reports.*, report)
  return ()
}

// The reports ordered by span, earlier first; reports with one span keep the order they were found.
effect fn bySpan(reports: &[Report]) -> List<Report> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut sorted = List<Report>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < reports.length {
    run List<Report>.append(&mut sorted, reports[at])
    let mut slot = List<Report>.length(&sorted) - usize.ONE
    while slot > usize.ZERO {
      let mut items = List<Report>.asMutSlice(&mut sorted)
      let previous = items[slot - usize.ONE]
      let current = items[slot]
      let later = previous.access.start > current.access.start
        || (previous.access.start == current.access.start && previous.access.end > current.access.end)
      if !later { break }
      items[slot - usize.ONE] = current
      items[slot] = previous
      slot = slot - usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move sorted
}

/// A declared/header premise, supplied separately from the body's retained goals.
pub struct RegionBound {
  pub longer: Shared<Lifetime>
  pub shorter: Shared<Lifetime>
}

fn verdict(outcome: Outcome, status: BorrowStatus) -> Verdict {
  return Verdict {outcome: outcome, status: status, code: RejectionCode.Unsupported, access: Location.make(usize.ZERO, usize.ZERO),
    earlier: Option<Location>.none(), reports: List<Report>.make()}
}

// The kind of one place step. Each kind numbers its own steps, so no field, element or member
// ordinal can stand for another kind of step.
enum StepKind {
  Field,
  Element,
  // A union member or variant payload; distinct members of one union are disjoint places.
  Member,
  // The step from a reference to its referent. A place through a reference names the referent's
  // storage, so a reborrow is a loan of that place (BORROW-005).
  Referent,
  // An index step whose value is unknown; it overlaps every element step.
  AnyElement,
  // A held loan replicated into every array element, never a source access path.
  RepeatedElement,
}

struct Step {
  kind: StepKind
  ordinal: usize
}

impl Copy for Step {}

fn fieldStep(index: usize) -> Step {
  return Step {kind: StepKind.Field, ordinal: index}
}

fn elementStep(index: usize) -> Step {
  return Step {kind: StepKind.Element, ordinal: index}
}

fn memberStep(tag: usize) -> Step {
  return Step {kind: StepKind.Member, ordinal: tag}
}

fn referent() -> Step {
  return Step {kind: StepKind.Referent, ordinal: usize.ZERO}
}

fn anyElement() -> Step {
  return Step {kind: StepKind.AnyElement, ordinal: usize.ZERO}
}

fn sameStep(left: Step, right: Step) -> bool {
  return left.kind == right.kind && left.ordinal == right.ordinal
}

// Whether `inner` lies behind a reference stored at `outer`: `outer`'s steps are a strict prefix of
// `inner`'s and the next step dereferences. Replacing the reference leaves its old referent alone.
fn behind(outer: &Place, inner: &Place) -> bool {
  if outer.root != inner.root {
    return false
  }
  let first = List<Step>.asSlice(&outer.steps)
  let second = List<Step>.asSlice(&inner.steps)
  if first.length >= second.length || second[first.length].kind != StepKind.Referent {
    return false
  }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < first.length {
    if !sameStep(first[at], second[at]) {
      return false
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Only a whole local whose actual type is a shared reference proves that consuming this
// descriptor cannot consume its referent. Projected, hidden and opaque places need their own
// type evidence; a shared loan alone says nothing about the descriptor's access.
fn sharedLocalDescriptor(locals: &[Local], place: &Place) -> bool {
  if place.root >= locals.length || List<Step>.length(&place.steps) != usize.ZERO { return false }
  return Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&locals[place.root].ty, fn(ty: &Type) -> bool {
    return match &ty.* {
      Type.Reference {access, ..} => access == Access.Shared
      _ => false
    }
  })
}

// A body local and its static projection path: field ordinals, or `anyElement` for an index.
struct Place {
  root: usize
  steps: List<Step>
}

struct Interval {
  from: usize
  to: usize
  definition: usize
  read: usize
  cleanup: bool
}

impl Copy for Interval {}

// How exactly the walk knows which values carry this loan. A conflict with an inexact loan leaves
// the body imprecise instead of rejecting it, except a `Stored` one.
// - `Stored`: a retaining local holder took the loan by a field store. The loan itself flows exactly,
//   so it is still rejected once required past its storage end, and its region proof is typing's
//   relation from the stored loan's region into the field's: the holder's region keeps every loan it
//   ever held, which over-approximates, and a requirement before the store is vacuous for this loan,
//   whose creation does not reach it. A call that cannot map it exactly leaves it `Unknown`.
// - `Alternatives`: the loan is one of a complete union of possible source loans. Every source must
//   satisfy a region proof, but a conflict with one possible source cannot establish a definite rejection.
// - `Unknown`: no complete mapping, so the loan cannot participate in region proofs.
enum LoanPrecision { Exact, Stored, Alternatives, Unknown }

// Whether region proofs may use a loan: its sources are exact, held by a field store, or a complete
// union of alternatives.
fn provable(precision: LoanPrecision) -> bool {
  return precision == LoanPrecision.Exact || precision == LoanPrecision.Stored || precision == LoanPrecision.Alternatives
}

struct Loan {
  place: Place
  exclusive: bool
  origin: Location
  // Evaluation-point ranges in which a value carrying this loan is in flight.
  intervals: List<Interval>
  // How exactly the walk knows which values carry this loan.
  precision: LoanPrecision
  // The regions typing gave the borrow, or none when the borrow has no typed node of its own.
  regions: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
  // Whether the loan borrows a place rooted in a body local, so its region is a body region even
  // when typing recorded none.
  local: bool
  // Storage provenance is separate from inner lifetime atoms retained by the borrowed type.
  borrowed: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>
  parent: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>
  crossed: bool
  created: usize
  // Whether the loan's value reached a call or callable that can keep it in a universal region, one
  // chosen before the body runs; it must then outlive the body wherever its creation reaches (R3
  // amendment 4).
  escapes: bool
  // The match subject node whose borrowed arm bindings hold this loan, or `usize.MAX`: accesses
  // through those bindings reach the subject place without conflicting with it (MATCH-002).
  binder: usize
  // The local an `effect` block binds when this loan is one of the block's own captures, taken by
  // the block's initializer, or `usize.MAX`.
  block: usize
  // A point the loan stays live to whether or not a holder uses it there, or `usize.MAX`: an unrun
  // `effect` block keeps its own captures to its scope end (EFFECT-OWN-001).
  until: usize
  // The referent of the reference the borrow is typed as, or none, and a call then judges a carried
  // loan by its whole operand.
  referent: Option<Shared<Type>>
  // Whether a result keeps the loan only because typing requires its region to outlive a caller
  // region the result names (`outlivesResult`): where the return-slot refutation decides that
  // relation, the walk leaves the loan's conflicts to it.
  bound: bool
}

enum Kind {
  Read,
  // A complete or projected replacement: it reinitializes the place.
  Write,
  // A transfer of ownership out of the place: it leaves the place without an owner.
  Move,
  // An explicit `drop`: it ends the place's remaining parts, so a part moved earlier is no use.
  Drop,
  SharedBorrow,
  ExclusiveBorrow,
  // A `match &mut` scrutinee: like a write it conflicts with every loan, but it replaces nothing.
  Update,
  // A `match place` scrutinee reads the tag of an owner whose payload parts may have moved: it
  // conflicts with every loan, and only a move of the owner or an ancestor is a use after move.
  Inspect,
  // Ends the remaining storage of one scope owner after its observing cleanup.
  End,
  // Ends the validity of a hidden owner's loans while its storage lives on: a temporary a viewing
  // binding keeps beyond its statement (BORROW-006).
  Expire,
}

struct Event {
  point: usize
  place: Place
  kind: Kind
  span: Location
  // The accessed place itself, which a loan conflict reports (OWN0011): the operand of a `move`,
  // otherwise `span`.
  target: Location
  // The loan this access creates, or `usize.MAX`.
  loan: usize
  // For a replacement, whether its right-hand side moves out of the target: 0 no, 1 yes, 2 only
  // through an unknown index.
  consumesTarget: usize
  // The place match whose binding this access goes through, or `usize.MAX` (see `Path`).
  refiner: usize
  refinedDepth: usize
  // The subjects of the borrowing matches whose bindings this access goes through.
  binders: List<usize>
}

struct Point {
  next: List<usize>
  // A holder local read here, or `usize.MAX`.
  uses: usize
  // The path within `uses` this read reaches, or `usize.MAX` when it may reach all of it.
  read: usize
  // The exact path within `uses` whose old value this point overwrites, or `usize.MAX`: what was
  // held within it is not read here.
  written: usize
  // A holder local bound here, or `usize.MAX`.
  defines: usize
  // A local whose binding initializes it here, or `usize.MAX`.
  initializes: usize
  // The access recorded here, or `usize.MAX`.
  event: usize
  span: Location
}

struct Frame {
  exit: usize
  // The index of the frame's loop in `Walker.loops`.
  repeat: usize
  scopes: usize
}

// A loop: the point before it, its header, the sources of its back edges, the end of its points,
// and the span the bootstrap reports for an incompatible header.
struct Loop {
  before: usize
  header: usize
  sources: List<usize>
  end: usize
  span: Location
}

impl Copy for Frame {}

// A loan carried by a value, and the point from which it is in flight.
struct Carry {
  loan: usize
  since: usize
  // The operand of the consuming node that carried the loan to it, or `usize.MAX`.
  operand: usize
  // A read carries only definitions reaching that read, even after a later join or call.
  definition: usize
  read: usize
  // Where in the carrying value the loan is held: a `Walker.paths` entry naming the sub-place the
  // loan lies somewhere within (entry 0 is the whole value), or `usize.MAX` when that is unknown.
  field: usize
  // Whether the sub-place `field` names is the loan's own reference, only moved, copied or placed
  // since the borrow: no projection, call or read through it, so it is still typed as the borrow.
  direct: bool
}

impl Copy for Carry {}

struct Flow {
  at: usize
  carried: List<Carry>
}

// The written place a node names: its root local, whether it is reached through a reference, its
// projection path with a `referent` step per dereference, and the index operands to evaluate
// first, in order.
struct Path {
  root: usize
  through: bool
  steps: List<Step>
  indexes: List<NodeId>
  // The subject node of the innermost `match place` whose binding names this place, or
  // `usize.MAX`, and how many leading steps name that subject. The binding denotes the payload
  // the match selected only until the subject place is written or moved (MATCH-001).
  refiner: usize
  refinedDepth: usize
  // The subjects of the borrowing matches whose bindings name this place, outermost first.
  binders: List<usize>
}

// A holding exists when any recorded source definition reaches its corresponding read.
struct HoldingSource {
  definition: usize
  read: usize
}
impl Copy for HoldingSource {}

struct Holding {
  loan: usize
  holder: usize
  point: usize
  // Range in Walker.holdingSources; an empty range denotes an unconditional fresh loan.
  sources: usize
  sourceCount: usize
  // Where in the holder's value the loan is held, as `Carry.field` and `Carry.direct`.
  field: usize
  direct: bool
  // Whether the place that held the loan was overwritten: no later read of the holder reaches the
  // loan, yet a value read from that place still carries it, as typing relates the holder's whole
  // region to every loan it ever held there.
  shadowed: bool
  // Whether the loan reached this holder only through a value read from a shadowed place. The
  // holder's later reads need it only when that value was read after the loan's storage ended.
  inherited: bool
}

impl Copy for Holding {}

// The roots a lexical scope releases on every path out of it. A statement scope holds only the
// hidden owners of the temporaries its statement, condition, guard or short-circuit operand
// borrows (BORROW-006); bindings belong to the nearest enclosing ordinary scope. `expiring` roots
// stop being valid here while their storage and cleanup stay with an enclosing scope.
struct Scope {
  roots: List<usize>
  expiring: List<usize>
  statement: bool
}

/// The borrowed regions an initialized owner can observe during cleanup. Structural cleanup
/// observes only hook-bearing components, rather than every field of an aggregate.
pub struct LoanCleanup {
  pub regions: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
  pub unknown: bool
}

// Cleanup seen before a later definition in the same loop cannot observe that definition with
// the walk's forward-only interval recording. Keep that body unchecked until this is modeled.
struct LoopCleanup {
  holder: usize
  repeat: usize
}

impl Copy for LoopCleanup {}

// These are pending local validity requirements. They may keep a carried source live; they
// cannot prove their own validity and are never actual-parent or universal-premise edges.
struct RetentionEdge {
  source: usize
  extent: usize
}
impl Copy for RetentionEdge {}

fn retentionOrdinal(region: &Shared<Lifetime>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> usize {
  return Shared<Lifetime>.with<usize>(region, fn(value: &Lifetime) -> usize {
    if let Lifetime.Local {declaration, ordinal} = &value.* {
      if DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner) { return ordinal }
    }
    return usize.MAX
  })
}

effect fn localRetentionEdges(owner: &DeclarationId, obligations: &[SafetyObligation]) -> List<RetentionEdge>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut edges = List<RetentionEdge>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < obligations.length {
    if let SafetyObligation.RegionRelation {offered, wanted, inferredStatic, ..} = &obligations[at] {
      let pending = match &inferredStatic { Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {..} => true _ => false }
      if !pending {
        let source = retentionOrdinal(&offered, owner)
        let extent = retentionOrdinal(&wanted, owner)
        if source != usize.MAX && extent != usize.MAX && source != extent {
          run List<RetentionEdge>.append(&mut edges, RetentionEdge {source: source, extent: extent})
        }
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move edges
}

fn retentionListed(values: &[usize], value: usize) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < values.length {
    if values[at] == value { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// A retained inner atom does not name this loan's own borrowed storage. Require both the actual
// outer borrow identity and its recorded region, and leave empty/unknown mappings untouched.
fn requiredLoan(loan: &Loan, owner: &DeclarationId, required: &[usize]) -> bool {
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
    let ordinal = retentionOrdinal(&borrowed, owner)
    if ordinal != usize.MAX && retentionListed(required, ordinal) {
      let regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
      let mut at = usize.ZERO
      while at < regions.length {
        if Lifetime.equalsShared(&regions[at], &borrowed) { return true }
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
    }
  }
  return false
}

// Only retaining results with an unmatched actual local source need this closure. The finite
// goals are still separately checked against availability by localRelationsProved.
effect fn requiredRetainedRegions(loans: &[Loan], carried: &[Carry], named: &[Shared<Lifetime>],
  owner: &DeclarationId, edges: &[RetentionEdge]) -> List<usize> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut required = List<usize>.make()
  if edges.length == usize.ZERO { return move required }
  let mut missing = false
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carried.length {
    let loan = &loans[carried[at].loan]
    if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
      if retentionOrdinal(&borrowed, owner) != usize.MAX
        && !sharesAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions), named) { missing = true }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if !missing { return move required }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < named.length {
    let count = Lifetime.atomCount(&named[at])
    let mut part = usize.ZERO
    while part < count {
      let atom = Lifetime.atomAt(&named[at], part)
      let ordinal = retentionOrdinal(&atom, owner)
      if ordinal != usize.MAX && !retentionListed(List<usize>.asSlice(&required), ordinal) {
        run List<usize>.append(&mut required, ordinal)
      }
      part = part + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&required) {
    let entries = List<usize>.asSlice(&required)
    let extent = entries[at]
    let mut edge = usize.ZERO
    while edge < edges.length {
      if edges[edge].extent == extent && !retentionListed(List<usize>.asSlice(&required), edges[edge].source) {
        run List<usize>.append(&mut required, edges[edge].source)
      }
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move required
}

// A write through a reference into storage the caller holds, or into a local, and the lifetime
// parameters of the body or a named enclosing declaration that its target's type names.
struct StoreWindow {
  span: Location
  regions: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
  // The local written, or `usize.MAX` for a write through a reference.
  holder: usize
}

// A whole-value hold `finish` gave a result: the loan and the result node. Only a call its
// signature `described` bounds where in the result the loan can lie.
struct WholeHold {
  loan: usize
  result: NodeId
  described: bool
}

// A signature-retained source after a concrete call/construction point. The source predicate is
// the actual paired definition/read of that carry, not a union of unrelated reaching alternatives.
enum CallerSource { Absent, Actual, Unknown }

struct CallerRetention {
  loan: usize
  point: usize
  definition: usize
  read: usize
}

struct Walker {
  callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>
  // The Supplied atoms this body's own selected application binds its region parameters to.
  // They name caller regions valid for the whole invocation; every other Supplied atom stays open.
  supplied: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
  // Per local, whether it is an `effect` block's value not yet used: one never run or used keeps
  // the loans of its captures until its scope ends (EFFECT-OWN-001), as the bootstrap's fallback
  // end does. An unrun `effect fn` call's argument loans end at the call, as they do there.
  unrun: List<bool>
  points: List<Point>
  loans: List<Loan>
  events: List<Event>
  frames: List<Frame>
  loops: List<Loop>
  // Per local, the loans it holds; empty for a local that holds none.
  held: List<List<usize>>
  definitions: List<Holding>
  holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>
  scopes: List<Scope>
  localCount: usize
  cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>
  loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>
  exit: usize
  // The point before the body's first evaluation, where no place is moved and no loan is live.
  entry: usize
  outside: bool
  // Why the walk left the checked slice, once `outside` is set.
  reason: BorrowStatus
  // The binding roots of the consuming matches whose guards are being walked, innermost last.
  guarded: List<usize>
  // The first move or drop of a guarded binding root: a guard consumed a provisional binding.
  guardConsumed: Option<Location>
  // How lowering keeps the temporaries of the binding initializer or `let` subject being walked.
  retention: Retention
  // Pending finite requirements used only to retain carried sources, never to prove ancestry.
  requirements: List<RetentionEdge>
  // Whether typing retained no capture contents, so body loan regions are related only by
  // equality, the facts the body's types imply, and `retentionRelations`.
  settled: bool
  // Open relations used only to conservatively retain possible source loans, never proof premises.
  retentionRelations: List<ImpliedGroup>
  // Every whole-value hold of a loan a result took, for narrowing a later read within it.
  wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>
  // Atoms of the local regions a retained open contents bound names: values of unknown regions
  // enter them, so no symbolic proof relates them to a universal target.
  openContents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
  // Loans a call result dropped because it names only caller regions, which a body region cannot
  // outlive. A proof that such a loan's region outlives a universal region contradicts the drop:
  // the walk no longer sees where the loan goes, so it must be free of conflicts wherever its
  // creation reaches, as an escaping loan is.
  unretained: List<usize>
  // Whether a captured loan with no typed region reached a callable that can store through a type
  // parameter this walk cannot see. The walk continues, so a definite conflict among exact loans
  // still rejects, but the body is never Checked: where the callable stores it is unknown.
  storing: bool
  // The status of the first anonymous body this one constructs that the borrow check did not close,
  // or `Checked`. Nothing reports an anonymous body on its own, so this body claims no more.
  inherited: BorrowStatus
  // The loans a constructed callable carries whose body may store them where it can write.
  storable: List<usize>
  // Atoms of the regions an unretained loan's proof walks, once an access conflicts with a loan
  // that proof grounds on after the drop: none of them outlives a universal region.
  contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
  // Each `match place` and the point after its subject access, where it selects its arm.
  refinements: List<Refinement>
  // The binding slots of borrowed destructuring `let`s: each keeps its loan until its scope ends.
  lexicalHolders: List<usize>
  // The field paths `Carry.field` names; entry 0 is the empty path of a whole value.
  paths: List<List<Step>>
  // The writes through a reference and into locals: each statement's span and the universal
  // lifetime parameters its target's type names (`escapingOwnedLoan`).
  stores: List<StoreWindow>
  // The `return` statements whose value's type names a universal lifetime parameter: the caller's
  // result slot, which `escapingOwnedLoan` reads only when no other conflict decides the body.
  returns: List<StoreWindow>
  // The calls whose result can retain no region: a returned value never holds what reaches them.
  sealed: List<Location>
  // The operands of direct calls whose result can hold nothing they carry (typing's `retained`): a
  // region goal admitted inside one relates the operand to the call's binder, which the callee's
  // signature keeps apart from its result, so no requirement on the result reaches the operand.
  unheld: List<Location>
  // The locals whose value a write through a reference stores.
  escaping: List<usize>
}

// A `match place` at `subject` selects the variant its bindings refine at point `test`.
struct Refinement {
  subject: usize
  test: usize
}

impl Copy for Refinement {}

// How lowering keeps a binding's temporaries (BORROW-006). It keeps every temporary of a viewing
// binding's initializer, and of a borrowing destructuring `let`'s subject, for the binding's scope;
// only a borrowed array of a viewing binding stays valid that long.
enum Retention {
  // The temporaries end with their statement, arm or operand.
  None,
  // Storage and cleanup end with the scope; every temporary but a borrowed array expires with its
  // statement.
  Arrays,
  // Storage and cleanup end with the scope; every temporary expires with its statement. A binding
  // typed by a type parameter may view at an instance, so its temporaries are kept this way too.
  Storage,
}

fn flowAt(at: usize) -> Flow {
  return Flow {at: at, carried: List<Carry>.make()}
}

effect fn copyBinders(binders: &[usize]) -> List<usize> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut copied = List<usize>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < binders.length {
    run List<usize>.append(&mut copied, binders[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move copied
}

effect fn copySteps(steps: &[Step]) -> List<Step> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut copied = List<Step>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < steps.length {
    run List<Step>.append(&mut copied, steps[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move copied
}

effect fn newPoint(walker: &mut Walker, from: usize) -> usize ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let created = List<Point>.length(&walker.points)
  run List<Point>.append(&mut walker.points, Point {next: List<usize>.make(), uses: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, written: usize.MAX, defines: usize.MAX, initializes: usize.MAX, event: usize.MAX, span: Location.make(usize.ZERO, usize.ZERO)})
  run edge(&mut walker.*, from, created)
  return created
}

effect fn backEdge(walker: &mut Walker, repeat: usize, from: usize) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if from == usize.MAX {
    return ()
  }
  let mut loops = List<Loop>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loops)
  run List<usize>.append(&mut loops[repeat].sources, from)
  let header = loops[repeat].header
  run edge(&mut walker.*, from, header)
  return ()
}

effect fn edge(walker: &mut Walker, from: usize, to: usize) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if from == usize.MAX || to == usize.MAX {
    return ()
  }
  let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  run List<usize>.append(&mut points[from].next, to)
  return ()
}

// Ends the flight of carried loans at `at`, where their value is consumed.
effect fn consume(walker: &mut Walker, carried: &[Carry], at: usize) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < carried.length {
    let carry = carried[index]
    let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
    run List<Interval>.append(&mut loans[carry.loan].intervals, Interval {from: carry.since, to: at, definition: carry.definition, read: carry.read, cleanup: false})
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

effect fn appendCarried(target: &mut List<Carry>, source: &[Carry]) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < source.length {
    run List<Carry>.append(&mut target.*, source[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// Whether a carried loan borrows storage this body owns.
fn carriesLocal(walker: &Walker, carried: &[Carry]) -> bool {
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carried.length {
    if loans[carried[at].loan].local { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// The steps of the path `field` names.
effect fn copyPath(walker: &Walker, field: usize) -> List<Step> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let paths = List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths)
  return run copySteps(List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[field]))
}

// Names `steps` as a field path; the empty path is entry 0.
effect fn internPath(walker: &mut Walker, steps: List<Step>) -> usize ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if List<Step>.length(&steps) == usize.ZERO { return usize.ZERO }
  let index = List<List<Step>>.length(&walker.paths)
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, move steps)
  return index
}

// The path within its holder a read of `path` reaches: a read through a reference reaches the
// reference, which may lead anywhere its loans do.
effect fn readPath(walker: &mut Walker, path: &Path) -> usize ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let steps = List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps)
  let mut reached = List<Step>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < steps.length && steps[at].kind != StepKind.Referent {
    run List<Step>.append(&mut reached, steps[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return run internPath(&mut walker.*, move reached)
}

// Whether `steps` names one exact place: no computed index and no step through a reference.
fn exactPath(steps: &[Step]) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < steps.length {
    if steps[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || steps[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement
      || steps[at].kind == StepKind.Referent { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Whether two sub-places of one value may overlap: one contains the other. A computed index may
// name any element, and an unknown path may be anywhere.
fn pathsOverlap(walker: &Walker, left: usize, right: usize) -> bool {
  if left == usize.MAX || right == usize.MAX { return true }
  let paths = List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths)
  let first = List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[left])
  let second = List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[right])
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < first.length && at < second.length {
    let indexed = (first[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || second[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement
      || first[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement || second[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement)
      && (first[at].kind == StepKind.Element || first[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || first[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement)
      && (second[at].kind == StepKind.Element || second[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || second[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement)
    if !indexed && (first[at].kind != second[at].kind || first[at].ordinal != second[at].ordinal) { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Whether overwriting the exact sub-place `written` discards a loan held at `field`: the loan lies
// within that place, so it left with the old value. A computed index may name another element, so
// a write through one discards nothing.
effect fn discards(walker: &Walker, written: &[Step], field: usize) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if field == usize.MAX || !exactPath(written) { return false }
  let held = run copyPath(walker, field)
  return pathContains(written, List<Step>.asSlice(&held))
}

// The path of `prefix` followed by the path `field` names: where a loan held somewhere within
// `field` lies once its value is stored at `prefix`. A loan whose field is unknown lies somewhere
// within `prefix`, so a read that contains `prefix` forwards it, and a narrower read that may reach
// it still carries it, unattributed: an unknown field errs toward rejection. A computed index
// leaves the element unknown, so the path is unknown too.
effect fn prefixedPath(walker: &mut Walker, prefix: &[Step], field: usize) -> usize ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if field == usize.MAX && prefix.length == usize.ZERO { return usize.MAX }
  let mut steps = List<Step>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < prefix.length {
    if prefix[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || prefix[at].kind == StepKind.Referent { return usize.MAX }
    run List<Step>.append(&mut steps, prefix[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if field != usize.MAX {
    let tail = run copyPath(&walker.*, field)
    let listed = List<Step>.asSlice(&tail)
    at = usize.ZERO
    while at < listed.length {
      run List<Step>.append(&mut steps, listed[at])
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return run internPath(&mut walker.*, move steps)
}

// The path `field` names without its first `count` steps.
effect fn strippedPath(walker: &mut Walker, field: usize, count: usize) -> usize ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let held = run copyPath(&walker.*, field)
  let listed = List<Step>.asSlice(&held)
  let mut steps = List<Step>.make()
  let mut at = count
  while at < listed.length {
    run List<Step>.append(&mut steps, listed[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return run internPath(&mut walker.*, move steps)
}

// Whether a read of the sub-place `read` contains the sub-place `held` a loan lies somewhere within,
// so the value read holds the loan. Elements are one place to a computed index.
fn pathContains(read: &[Step], held: &[Step]) -> bool {
  if read.length > held.length { return false }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < read.length {
    let left = read[at]
    let right = held[at]
    if right.kind == StepKind.AnyElement { return false }
    let anyElement = left.kind == StepKind.AnyElement && right.kind == StepKind.Element
    if !anyElement && (left.kind != right.kind || left.ordinal != right.ordinal) { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Selecting any element of a repeated value carries the same nested loans. Unlike
// pathContains (also used by writes), this does not claim the selection replaces every copy.
fn readContains(read: &[Step], held: &[Step]) -> bool {
  if read.length > held.length { return false }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < read.length {
    let left = read[at]
    let right = held[at]
    if right.kind == StepKind.AnyElement { return false }
    let selectedRepeat = right.kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement
      && (left.kind == StepKind.Element || left.kind == StepKind.AnyElement)
    let anyElement = left.kind == StepKind.AnyElement && right.kind == StepKind.Element
    if !selectedRepeat && !anyElement && !sameStep(left, right) { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Record each crossing; its proof later follows the actual storage parent.
fn cross(walker: &mut Walker, carried: &[Carry]) -> () {
  let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carried.length {
    if !loans[carried[at].loan].local { loans[carried[at].loan].crossed = true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// Ends the loans one path carries at its end `end` and restarts them at the join `joined`. Points
// are numbered in creation order, not by path, so a joined value's carries restart at the join. A
// path that ends at `usize.MAX` never reaches the join.
effect fn rejoin(walker: &mut Walker, carried: &[Carry], end: usize, joined: usize, onward: &mut List<Carry>) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if end == usize.MAX {
    return ()
  }
  cross(&mut walker.*, carried)
  run consume(&mut walker.*, carried, end)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carried.length {
    run List<Carry>.append(&mut onward.*, Carry {loan: carried[at].loan, since: joined, operand: usize.MAX, definition: carried[at].definition, read: carried[at].read, field: carried[at].field, direct: carried[at].direct})
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// Appends the loans one operand carries, marked with that operand's position.
effect fn appendOperand(target: &mut List<Carry>, source: &[Carry], operand: usize) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < source.length {
    run List<Carry>.append(&mut target.*, Carry {loan: source[at].loan, since: source[at].since, operand: operand, definition: source[at].definition, read: source[at].read, field: source[at].field, direct: source[at].direct})
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// Whether a value of `ty` can retain an alias loan, including static regions; unknown counts as retained.
effect fn retains(ty: &Shared<Type>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let known = run bodyRetainedRegions(ty, owner, &mut regions)
  return !known || List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(&regions) > usize.ZERO
}

// Appends the regions a value of `ty` can retain; `false` when they are unknown.
effect fn retainedBy(ty: &Shared<Type>, owner: &DeclarationId, regions: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let representations = List<Option<Shared<Type>>>.make()
  return run Type.retainedRegions(ty, owner, List<Option<Shared<Type>>>.asSlice(&representations), &mut regions.*, true)
}

fn expressionType(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> Option<Shared<Type>> {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {ty, ..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
    return Option<Shared<Type>>.some(Shared<Type>.clone(&ty))
  }
  return Option<Shared<Type>>.none()
}

// Whether `id`'s value can retain a non-static region; a statement node retains nothing. A callable
// value may hold capture loans its type does not name, so it always counts as retaining.
effect fn nodeRetains(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let found = expressionType(nodes, id)
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move found {
    if Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&value, callableValue) {
      return true
    }
    let retained = run retains(&value, owner)
    return retained
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a type is a fixed array, whose aggregate operands are its elements.
fn arrayType(node: &Type) -> bool {
  return match &node.* {
    Type.Array {..} => true
    _ => false
  }
}

// Whether `id` is a slice view, whose elements lie behind it rather than in its own storage.
fn sliceValue(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> bool {
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, id) {
    return Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&value, fn(node: &Type) -> bool {
      return match &node.* {
        Type.Slice {..} => true
        _ => false
      }
    })
  }
  return false
}

// Reads the written place of `id`, or a path with root `usize.MAX` when it names no place.
effect fn pathOf(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> Path ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut path = Path {root: usize.MAX, through: false, steps: List<Step>.make(), indexes: List<NodeId>.make(), refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: usize.ZERO, binders: List<usize>.make()}
  run extendPath(nodes, id, usize.MAX, &mut path)
  return move path
}

// Reads the place `id` names when the value of `base`, which names no place, is held by its hidden
// owner (BORROW-006): `base`'s projections, indexes and dereferences extend that owner's root.
effect fn temporaryPath(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId, base: NodeId) -> Path ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut path = Path {root: usize.MAX, through: false, steps: List<Step>.make(), indexes: List<NodeId>.make(), refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: usize.ZERO, binders: List<usize>.make()}
  run extendPath(nodes, id, base.index, &mut path)
  return move path
}

// The innermost operand of a place expression's projections, indexes and dereferences.
fn projectedBase(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> NodeId {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form, ..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
    return match &form {
      Expression.Field {value, ..} => projectedBase(nodes, value)
      Expression.Index {value, ..} => projectedBase(nodes, value)
      Expression.Dereference {value} => projectedBase(nodes, value)
      _ => id
    }
  }
  return id
}

// The root of a temporary's hidden owner, keyed by the node that produces the temporary. It
// follows the match subject roots, so it overlaps no local or subject.
fn temporaryRoot(nodes: &[Node], base: usize) -> usize {
  return usize.MAX / 4 + nodes.length + base
}

// The holder of the loan a borrowing match at `subject` lends its arm bindings: a slot after the
// temporaries' with no storage of its own, so only uses of the bindings keep its loan live.
fn bindingsRoot(nodes: &[Node], subject: usize) -> usize {
  return usize.MAX / 4 + nodes.length + nodes.length + subject
}

// Whether `root` is a temporary's hidden owner.
fn temporary(nodes: &[Node], root: usize) -> bool {
  return root >= usize.MAX / 4 + nodes.length && root < usize.MAX / 4 + nodes.length + nodes.length
}

/// Which storage the loan walk ends beside the locals, by holder slot: slot `n` is the subject of a
/// match at node `n`, and slot `nodes.length + n` the hidden owner of the temporary node `n` a
/// borrow lends or a projection reads (BORROW-006). Their cleanup is observed like a local's.
pub effect fn storageNodes(nodes: &[Node]) -> List<bool> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut owning = List<bool>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < nodes.length + nodes.length {
    run List<bool>.append(&mut owning, false)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < nodes.length {
    let mut owned = usize.MAX
    if let NodeKind.Expression {form, ..} = &nodes[at].kind {
      match &form {
        Expression.Match {subject, ..} => { owned = subject.index }
        Expression.Borrow {value, ..} => {
          let path = run pathOf(nodes, value)
          if path.root == usize.MAX { owned = nodes.length + projectedBase(nodes, value).index }
        }
        // A projection out of a value with no place may read it through its hidden owner.
        Expression.Field {..} => {
          let path = run pathOf(nodes, NodeId {index: at})
          if path.root == usize.MAX { owned = nodes.length + projectedBase(nodes, NodeId {index: at}).index }
        }
        Expression.Index {..} => {
          let path = run pathOf(nodes, NodeId {index: at})
          if path.root == usize.MAX { owned = nodes.length + projectedBase(nodes, NodeId {index: at}).index }
        }
        _ => {}
      }
    }
    if owned != usize.MAX {
      let mut marked = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut owning)
      marked[owned] = true
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move owning
}

effect fn extendPath(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId, temporary: usize, path: &mut Path) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if id.index == temporary {
    path.root = temporaryRoot(nodes, temporary)
    return ()
  }
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form, ..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
    match &form {
      Expression.Local {local} => {
        path.root = local.index
        return ()
      }
      Expression.Field {value, index, ..} => {
        run extendPath(nodes, value, temporary, &mut path.*)
        if path.root != usize.MAX {
          run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, fieldStep(index))
        }
        return ()
      }
      Expression.Index {value, index, element} => {
        run extendPath(nodes, value, temporary, &mut path.*)
        if path.root != usize.MAX {
          // A slice's elements live in its referent: indexing one reads through the slice as `.*`
          // does, so it reads the holder and keeps the loans it holds live.
          if sliceValue(nodes, value) {
            run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, referent())
            path.through = true
          }
          // A literal in-bounds index of a fixed array names its static element, the component a
          // move of it leaves; any other index may name every element.
          let mut step = anyElement()
          if element != usize.MAX { step = elementStep(element) }
          run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, step)
          run List<NodeId>.append(&mut path.indexes, index)
        }
        return ()
      }
      Expression.Dereference {value} => {
        run extendPath(nodes, value, temporary, &mut path.*)
        if path.root != usize.MAX {
          run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, referent())
          path.through = true
        }
        return ()
      }
      Expression.PatternBinding {subject, path: steps, access, ..} => {
        run bindingPath(nodes, subject, List<PlaceStep>.asSlice(&steps), access, &mut path.*)
        return ()
      }
      _ => {}
    }
  }
  return ()
}

fn guardedRoot(guarded: &[usize], root: usize) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < guarded.length {
    if guarded[at] == root { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// The root of the parts a match subject holds when it is not a place of this body: the subject was
// copied, consumed or evaluated into storage of its own, so it overlaps no local.
fn subjectRoot(subject: NodeId) -> usize {
  return usize.MAX / 4 + subject.index
}

// The place a pattern binding names. A place-addressing binding (`match place`, `&`, `&mut`) is a
// projection of the subject's own place; a copied or moved binding, or a binding of a subject with no
// place, is a projection of the subject's own storage. The subject's index operands were evaluated
// with the match, so the binding re-evaluates none.
effect fn bindingPath(nodes: &[Node], subject: NodeId, steps: &[PlaceStep], access: BindingAccess, path: &mut Path) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if access == BindingAccess.Place || access == BindingAccess.Shared || access == BindingAccess.Exclusive {
    let base = run pathOf(nodes, subject)
    if base.root != usize.MAX {
      path.root = base.root
      path.through = base.through
      path.refiner = base.refiner
      path.refinedDepth = base.refinedDepth
      if access == BindingAccess.Place {
        path.refiner = subject.index
        path.refinedDepth = List<Step>.length(&base.steps)
      }
      path.steps = move base.steps
      path.binders = move base.binders
    }
    // A borrowed binding reaches what its match lends to the arm: the subject place, or the
    // storage a subject with no place borrows.
    if access != BindingAccess.Place { run List<usize>.append(&mut path.binders, subject.index) }
  }
  if path.root == usize.MAX {
    path.root = subjectRoot(subject)
  }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < steps.length {
    match &steps[at] {
      PlaceStep.Member {tag, ..} => { run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, memberStep(tag)) }
      PlaceStep.VariantField {tag, field} => {
        run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, memberStep(tag))
        run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, fieldStep(field))
      }
      PlaceStep.Field {index} => { run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, fieldStep(index)) }
      PlaceStep.Element {index} => { run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, elementStep(index)) }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// The overlap of two places: 0 disjoint, 1 overlapping, 2 decided only by an unknown index.
fn overlap(left: &Place, right: &Place) -> usize {
  if left.root != right.root {
    return usize.ZERO
  }
  let first = List<Step>.asSlice(&left.steps)
  let second = List<Step>.asSlice(&right.steps)
  let mut unknown = false
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < first.length && at < second.length {
    if first[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || second[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement {
      unknown = true
    } else if !sameStep(first[at], second[at]) {
      return usize.ZERO
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if unknown {
    return 2
  }
  return usize.ONE
}

// Whether an access through the bindings of `binders` reaches `loan`'s place by the loan itself.
fn lentTo(loan: &Loan, binders: &List<usize>) -> bool {
  if loan.binder == usize.MAX { return false }
  let through = List<usize>.asSlice(binders)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < through.length {
    if through[at] == loan.binder { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a place names no element by an unknown index.
fn determined(place: &Place) -> bool {
  let steps = List<Step>.asSlice(&place.steps)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < steps.length {
    if steps[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Whether an access may replace the value of its place: a write, a move or drop, or an exclusive
// borrow or update, through which a callee or a later store can replace it.
fn replaces(kind: Kind) -> bool {
  return kind == Kind.Write || kind == Kind.Move || kind == Kind.Drop || kind == Kind.ExclusiveBorrow || kind == Kind.Update
}

// Whether `written` may name the first `depth` steps of `used`, or a prefix of them: replacing it
// replaces the subject a refined binding of `used` was selected from. An unknown index may name
// the refined element.
fn coversRefined(written: &Place, used: &Place, depth: usize) -> bool {
  if written.root != used.root { return false }
  let first = List<Step>.asSlice(&written.steps)
  let second = List<Step>.asSlice(&used.steps)
  if first.length > depth || depth > second.length { return false }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < first.length {
    let indexed = first[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement
      && (second[at].kind == StepKind.Element || second[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement)
    if !indexed && !sameStep(first[at], second[at]) { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// The points control can reach from point `from` without passing `test`, where the match selects
// its variant again. Back edges count: a later iteration of a loop in the arm reaches it.
effect fn reachableAvoiding(walker: &Walker, from: usize, test: usize) -> List<bool> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut seen = List<bool>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length {
    run List<bool>.append(&mut seen, false)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut pending = List<usize>.make()
  run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, from)
  while List<usize>.length(&pending) > usize.ZERO {
    let last = List<usize>.length(&pending) - usize.ONE
    let point = List<usize>.remove(&mut pending, last)
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
    let mut successor = usize.ZERO
    while successor < next.length {
      let target = next[successor]
      if !List<bool>.asSlice(&seen)[target] {
        let mut marked = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut seen)
        marked[target] = true
        if target != test { run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, target) }
      }
      successor = successor + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return move seen
}

// The points one replacement reaches before its match selects again, computed once per pair.
struct ReplacementReach {
  source: usize
  test: usize
  seen: List<bool>
}

// Whether `loan` is live at `point` by its `until`: the point lies on a path from where the loan is
// taken to that end.
effect fn liveUntil(walker: &Walker, reaches: &mut List<ReplacementReach>, loan: &Loan, point: usize) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let taken = run reachesAvoiding(walker, &mut reaches.*, loan.created, point, usize.MAX)
  if !taken { return false }
  return run reachesAvoiding(walker, &mut reaches.*, point, loan.until, usize.MAX)
}

// Whether control can pass from replacement point `from` to point `to` without passing `test`.
effect fn reachesAvoiding(walker: &Walker, reaches: &mut List<ReplacementReach>, from: usize, to: usize, test: usize) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let known = List<ReplacementReach>.asSlice(&reaches.*)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < known.length {
    if known[at].source == from && known[at].test == test { return List<bool>.asSlice(&known[at].seen)[to] }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let seen = run reachableAvoiding(walker, from, test)
  let reached = List<bool>.asSlice(&seen)[to]
  run List<ReplacementReach>.append(&mut reaches.*, ReplacementReach {source: from, test: test, seen: move seen})
  return reached
}

// The point where the `match place` at `subject` selects its variant, or `usize.MAX`.
fn refinementTest(walker: &Walker, subject: usize) -> usize {
  let refinements = List<Refinement>.asSlice(&walker.refinements)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < refinements.length {
    if refinements[at].subject == subject { return refinements[at].test }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return usize.MAX
}

// Every access kind, for the codes an access can report.
effect fn everyKind() -> List<Kind> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut kinds = List<Kind>.make()
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.Read)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.Write)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.Move)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.Drop)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.SharedBorrow)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.ExclusiveBorrow)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.Update)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.Inspect)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.End)
  run List<Kind>.append(&mut kinds, Kind.Expire)
  return move kinds
}

// The code for a use of a loan's view after the loan expired.
fn expiredCode() -> RejectionCode {
  return RejectionCode.ExpiredLifetime
}

/// The codes loan liveness reports: every code an access conflicting with a live loan reports, and
/// the code of a use after a loan expired. A body that is not borrow-checked has not had its loan
/// lifetimes proved, so these are the codes it may be missing; its moves are checked regardless.
pub effect fn livenessCodes() -> List<RejectionCode> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut codes = List<RejectionCode>.make()
  run List<RejectionCode>.append(&mut codes, expiredCode())
  let every = run everyKind()
  let kinds = List<Kind>.asSlice(&every)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < kinds.length {
    let mut exclusive = 0
    while exclusive < 2 {
      if let Option<RejectionCode>.Some {value} = move conflictCode(kinds[at], exclusive == 1) {
        let listed = List<RejectionCode>.asSlice(&codes)
        let mut seen = false
        let mut look = usize.ZERO
        while look < listed.length {
          if listed[look] == value { seen = true }
          look = look + usize.ONE
        }
        if !seen { run List<RejectionCode>.append(&mut codes, value) }
      }
      exclusive = exclusive + 1
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move codes
}

fn conflictCode(kind: Kind, exclusive: bool) -> Option<RejectionCode> {
  if kind == Kind.ExclusiveBorrow || (kind == Kind.SharedBorrow && exclusive) {
    return Option<RejectionCode>.some(RejectionCode.LoanConflict)
  }
  if kind == Kind.Write || kind == Kind.Move || kind == Kind.Drop || kind == Kind.Update || kind == Kind.Inspect
    || (kind == Kind.Read && exclusive) {
    return Option<RejectionCode>.some(RejectionCode.AccessDuringLoan)
  }
  return Option<RejectionCode>.none()
}

// Records an access to a written place at a fresh point after `at`.
effect fn access(walker: &mut Walker, path: &Path, kind: Kind, span: Location, at: usize, loan: usize) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if (kind == Kind.Move || kind == Kind.Drop) && guardedRoot(List<usize>.asSlice(&walker.guarded), path.root) {
    if let Option<Location>.None = &walker.guardConsumed { walker.guardConsumed = Option<Location>.some(span) }
  }
  let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, at)
  let holder = holderOf(&walker.*, path.root)
  let read = run readPath(&mut walker.*, path)
  if kind != Kind.Write && kind != Kind.End && kind != Kind.Expire { usedEffect(&mut walker.*, holder) }
  let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  points[point].event = List<Event>.length(&walker.events)
  points[point].span = span
  // Record reads independently of the definitions seen so far: a later loop assignment can
  // reach this access through the back edge. Slots with no eventual loans have no liveness bit.
  if kind != Kind.Write && kind != Kind.End && kind != Kind.Expire {
    points[point].uses = holder
    points[point].read = read
  }
  if (kind == Kind.Move || kind == Kind.Drop || kind == Kind.End) && List<Step>.length(&path.steps) == usize.ZERO {
    points[point].defines = holder
  }
  run List<Event>.append(
    &mut walker.events,
    Event {
      point: point,
      place: Place {root: path.root, steps: run copySteps(List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps))},
      kind: kind,
      span: span,
      target: span,
      loan: loan,
      consumesTarget: usize.ZERO,
      refiner: path.refiner,
      refinedDepth: path.refinedDepth,
      binders: run copyBinders(List<usize>.asSlice(&path.binders)),
    },
  )
  return point
}

// A read of a holder local at a fresh point, reaching the path `read` within it: the value carries
// the loans it holds.
effect fn useHolder(walker: &mut Walker, root: usize, read: usize, span: Location, at: usize) -> Flow ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, at)
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  let local = holderOf(&walker.*, root)
  usedEffect(&mut walker.*, local)
  let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  points[point].uses = local
  points[point].read = read
  points[point].span = span
  if !holds(&walker.*, root) { return Flow {at: point, carried: move carried} }
  let held = List<List<usize>>.asSlice(&walker.held)
  let definitions = List<usize>.asSlice(&held[local])
  let all = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < definitions.length {
    let definition = definitions[at]
    run List<Carry>.append(&mut carried, Carry {loan: all[definition].loan, since: point, operand: usize.MAX, definition: definition, read: point, field: all[definition].field, direct: all[definition].direct})
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return Flow {at: point, carried: move carried}
}

// The loans a read of `path` carries, each with where the value read holds it: a loan's field is
// kept only when the read contains where the loan is held, which a read through a reference reaches
// past its `Referent` step. The reference's own loan is held by the whole reference, which no such
// read contains. Anything else keeps an unknown field, which nothing forwards, except a read strictly
// within a call result's whole-value hold whose `declared` field type the loan provably cannot reach
// (`unreachableField`): that part of the result holds none of it.
effect fn attributeRead(nodes: &[Node], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, path: &Path, carried: &[Carry],
  declared: &DeclaredRead) -> List<Carry>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let steps = List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps)
  let mut read = List<Carry>.make()
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < carried.length {
    let mut carry = carried[index]
    let mut held = true
    if carry.field != usize.MAX {
      let heldPath = run copyPath(&walker.*, carry.field)
      let heldSteps = List<Step>.asSlice(&heldPath)
      if readContains(steps, heldSteps) {
        carry.field = run strippedPath(&mut walker.*, carry.field, steps.length)
      } else {
        carry.field = usize.MAX
        carry.direct = false
        if !path.through && disjointFields(steps, heldSteps) { held = false }
        if held && !path.through && declared.known && pathContains(heldSteps, steps)
          && !reborrowedByCarried(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), carried, index) {
          held = !run unreachableField(nodes, owner, &walker.*, carry, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&declared.regions))
        }
      }
    }
    if held { run List<Carry>.append(&mut read, carry) }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return move read
}

// Different declared record fields store disjoint values, even when their lifetime arguments
// happen to be equal. Unknown elements and reference boundaries provide no such separation.
fn disjointFields(read: &[Step], held: &[Step]) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < read.length && at < held.length {
    if read[at].kind == StepKind.Field && held[at].kind == StepKind.Field
      && read[at].ordinal != held[at].ordinal { return true }
    if !sameStep(read[at], held[at]) || read[at].kind == StepKind.Referent { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether another carried loan reborrows the loan `carried[index]` carries, so it stays live with it.
fn reborrowedByCarried(loans: &[Loan], carried: &[Carry], index: usize) -> bool {
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loans[carried[index].loan].borrowed {
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < carried.length {
      if at != index {
        if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: parent} = &loans[carried[at].loan].parent {
          if meetMember(&parent, &borrowed) { return true }
        }
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return false
}

// Whether the loan `carry` carries provably lies in no part of a call result typed by `named`: the
// same test `finish` applies to a whole result, with the field's declared regions in place of the
// result's. The loan is exact, all its regions are body regions that no named region shares, it is
// no retained source outlives requirements need, and the facts every call that holds it implies
// (the body's open relations and the well-formedness of the call's argument and result types) lead
// none of its regions to a named region or outside the body. A hold no signature describes, such
// as a callable invocation's or a built value's, decides nothing.
effect fn unreachableField(nodes: &[Node], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &Walker, carry: Carry, named: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let loan = &loans[carry.loan]
  let regionsOf = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
  if loan.precision != LoanPrecision.Exact || regionsOf.length == usize.ZERO || !bodyRegions(regionsOf, owner) || sharesAtom(regionsOf, named) {
    return false
  }
  let mut single = List<Carry>.make()
  run List<Carry>.append(&mut single, carry)
  let required = run requiredRetainedRegions(loans, List<Carry>.asSlice(&single), named, owner,
    List<RetentionEdge>.asSlice(&walker.requirements))
  if requiredLoan(loan, owner, List<usize>.asSlice(&required)) { return false }
  let mut implied = Implied {groups: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), known: walker.settled}
  let holds = List<WholeHold>.asSlice(&walker.wholeHolds)
  let mut found = false
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < holds.length {
    if holds[at].loan == carry.loan {
      if !holds[at].described { return false }
      found = true
      let facts = run signatureImplied(nodes, walker, holds[at].result)
      if !facts.known { implied.known = false }
      let groups = List<ImpliedGroup>.asSlice(&facts.groups)
      let mut group = usize.ZERO
      while group < groups.length {
        let mut members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
        run appendAllAtoms(&mut members, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&groups[group].members))
        let mut container = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
        run appendAllAtoms(&mut container, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&groups[group].container))
        run List<ImpliedGroup>.append(&mut implied.groups, ImpliedGroup {container: move container, members: move members})
        group = group + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if !found || !implied.known { return false }
  return !run mayOutlive(&implied, regionsOf, named, owner)
}

// Where a reference to the sub-place `borrowed` of a holder holds a loan the holder holds at
// `field`: behind its `Referent` step, at the rest of the loan's path, when the borrowed place
// contains it. A loan the borrowed place does not contain travels with the reference unreachable.
effect fn referencedPath(walker: &mut Walker, borrowed: &[Step], field: usize) -> usize ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if field == usize.MAX { return usize.MAX }
  let held = run copyPath(&walker.*, field)
  let listed = List<Step>.asSlice(&held)
  if !readContains(borrowed, listed) { return usize.MAX }
  let mut steps = List<Step>.make()
  run List<Step>.append(&mut steps, referent())
  let mut at = borrowed.length
  while at < listed.length {
    run List<Step>.append(&mut steps, listed[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return run internPath(&mut walker.*, move steps)
}

// Marks the replacement recorded at `point` when a move recorded since event `since` overlaps its
// target; the bootstrap then reports the whole `statement`.
fn markConsumedTarget(walker: &mut Walker, since: usize, point: usize, statement: Location) -> () {
  let recorded = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)[point].event
  let mut events = List<Event>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.events)
  let mut at = since
  while at < recorded {
    if events[at].kind == Kind.Move || events[at].kind == Kind.Drop {
      let shared = overlap(&events[at].place, &events[recorded].place)
      if shared == usize.ONE || (shared != usize.ZERO && events[recorded].consumesTarget == usize.ZERO) {
        events[recorded].consumesTarget = shared
        events[recorded].span = statement
        events[recorded].target = statement
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// An access to a place behind a reference. Reaching it reads the root holder, whose loans the
// result carries, and the access is recorded at the referent place.
effect fn throughReference(walker: &mut Walker, path: &Path, kind: Kind, span: Location, at: usize) -> Flow ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let read = run readPath(&mut walker.*, path)
  let used = run useHolder(&mut walker.*, path.root, read, span, at)
  let point = run access(&mut walker.*, path, kind, span, used.at, usize.MAX)
  return Flow {at: point, carried: move used.carried}
}

// A use of a borrowed match binding: each match whose binding names `path` holds its loan through
// the use, so the loan lives exactly as long as its bindings do. The value read carries no such
// loan: a borrow of the binding lends the subject place itself.
effect fn useBinders(nodes: &[Node], walker: &mut Walker, path: &Path, span: Location, at: usize) -> usize ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let binders = List<usize>.asSlice(&path.binders)
  let mut current = at
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < binders.length {
    let root = bindingsRoot(nodes, binders[index])
    if holds(&walker.*, root) {
      let holder = holderOf(&walker.*, root)
      current = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, current)
      let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
      points[current].uses = holder
      points[current].span = span
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return current
}

fn lexicalHolder(walker: &Walker, root: usize) -> bool {
  let holders = List<usize>.asSlice(&walker.lexicalHolders)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < holders.length {
    if holders[at] == root { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// The reference a subject with no place dereferences or indexes as a slice beneath its field and
// index steps, or the subject itself when it does neither. Evaluating that reference and then `indexes`, the index
// operands of the steps above it, innermost first, evaluates the whole subject.
effect fn viewedReference(nodes: &[Node], subject: NodeId, indexes: &mut List<NodeId>) -> NodeId ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut current = subject
  let mut reference = subject
  let mut steps = List<NodeId>.make()
  let mut walking = true
  while walking {
    walking = false
    if let NodeKind.Expression {form, ..} = &nodes[current.index].kind {
      match &form {
        Expression.Field {value, ..} => {
          current = value
          walking = true
        }
        Expression.Index {value, index, ..} => {
          run List<NodeId>.append(&mut steps, index)
          // A slice's elements live in its referent, so indexing it reads through it as `.*` does.
          if sliceValue(nodes, value) {
            reference = value
          } else {
            current = value
            walking = true
          }
        }
        Expression.Dereference {value} => { reference = value }
        _ => {}
      }
    }
  }
  if reference.index != subject.index {
    let walked = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&steps)
    let mut at = walked.length
    while at > usize.ZERO {
      at = at - usize.ONE
      run List<NodeId>.append(&mut indexes.*, walked[at])
    }
  }
  return reference
}

// Where a write to `target` is reported: the target place, or the reference a dereferenced target
// writes through, as the bootstrap reports them.
fn writtenSpan(nodes: &[Node], target: NodeId) -> Location {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Dereference {value}, ..} = &nodes[target.index].kind {
    return nodes[value.index].origin.location
  }
  return nodes[target.index].origin.location
}

// Leaves the checked slice; the first reason is the one reported.
fn leave(walker: &mut Walker, reason: BorrowStatus) -> () {
  if !walker.outside {
    walker.outside = true
    walker.reason = reason
  }
  return ()
}

fn holderOf(walker: &Walker, root: usize) -> usize {
  if root >= usize.MAX / 4 {
    return walker.localCount + root - usize.MAX / 4
  }
  return root
}

// An `effect` block's value that is used is no longer held to the end of its scope.
fn usedEffect(walker: &mut Walker, local: usize) -> () {
  if local < List<bool>.length(&walker.unrun) {
    let mut unrun = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.unrun)
    unrun[local] = false
  }
  return ()
}

fn holds(walker: &Walker, root: usize) -> bool {
  let local = holderOf(walker, root)
  let held = List<List<usize>>.asSlice(&walker.held)
  return local < held.length && List<usize>.length(&held[local]) > usize.ZERO
}

// Evaluates a place's index operands in order; each index value is consumed when it is read.
effect fn indexes(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, path: &Path, at: usize) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let operands = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&path.indexes)
  let mut current = at
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < operands.length {
    let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, operands[index], current)
    let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
    run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
    current = point
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return current
}

// Creates a loan of a written place at a fresh point, carried by the borrowing value. A reborrow
// through a reference is a loan of the referent place (BORROW-005): while it lives, an access
// through the parent reference conflicts with it as with any loan of that place.
effect fn borrow(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, place: NodeId, exclusive: bool, span: Location,
  node: usize, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut path = run pathOf(nodes, place)
  let mut source = run borrowedPlaceLifetime(nodes, place)
  let mut current = at
  if path.root == usize.MAX {
    // A borrow of a value with no place lends its hidden owner (BORROW-006).
    let base = projectedBase(nodes, place)
    current = run holdTemporary(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, base, at)
    path = run temporaryPath(nodes, place, base)
  }
  // A slice borrow reborrows its backing storage; it never lends the local descriptor slot.
  // Reference reborrows already have an explicit typed Dereference from checkBorrowOperand.
  if node != usize.MAX && sliceValue(nodes, place) && sliceValue(nodes, NodeId {index: node}) {
    run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, referent())
    path.through = true
    source = run descriptorLifetime(nodes, place)
  }
  let mut evaluated = run indexes(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, current)
  // A reference to a whole holder, or a reborrow through one, reaches what its loans borrow, so
  // the holder's loans travel with the reference: the parent loan outlives every reborrow of it,
  // and borrowing a callable to invoke it keeps its capture loans live.
  evaluated = run useBinders(nodes, &mut walker.*, &path, span, evaluated)
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  if holds(&walker.*, path.root) {
    let read = run readPath(&mut walker.*, &path)
    let used = run useHolder(&mut walker.*, path.root, read, span, evaluated)
    let travelling = List<Carry>.asSlice(&used.carried)
    let mut index = usize.ZERO
    while index < travelling.length {
      let mut carry = travelling[index]
      carry.field = run referencedPath(&mut walker.*, List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps), carry.field)
      carry.direct = carry.direct && carry.field != usize.MAX
      run List<Carry>.append(&mut carried, carry)
      index = index + usize.ONE
    }
    evaluated = used.at
  }
  return run takeLoan(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, exclusive, span, node, move source, evaluated, move carried)
}

fn loanLifetime(ty: &Type) -> Option<Shared<Lifetime>> {
  return match &ty.* {
    Type.Reference {lifetime, ..} => Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&lifetime))
    Type.Slice {lifetime, ..} => Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&lifetime))
    _ => Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  }
}

fn nodeLoanLifetime(nodes: &[Node], node: NodeId) -> Option<Shared<Lifetime>> {
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, node) {
    return Shared<Type>.with<Option<Shared<Lifetime>>>(&value, loanLifetime)
  }
  return Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
}

// The meet of the descriptors that reach the borrowed storage, not a lifetime mentioned by a
// nested field's type. A reborrow through several references is valid only while each of them
// is. A shared descriptor is Copy, so its referent stays valid for its own lifetime whatever
// path reached it: the chain ends at the first shared one, and a shared reborrow through shared
// references keeps the innermost lifetime. A reference to a descriptor slot is bounded by the
// slot's place instead.
effect fn borrowedPlaceLifetime(nodes: &[Node], node: NodeId) -> Option<Shared<Lifetime>> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut chain = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run placeDescriptors(nodes, node, &mut chain)
  return run descriptorMeet(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&chain))
}

// The bound of a reborrow of the storage `descriptor` itself views, such as a slice reborrow.
effect fn descriptorLifetime(nodes: &[Node], descriptor: NodeId) -> Option<Shared<Lifetime>> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut chain = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run descriptorChain(nodes, descriptor, &mut chain)
  return run descriptorMeet(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&chain))
}

effect fn descriptorMeet(chain: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> Option<Shared<Lifetime>> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if chain.length == usize.ZERO { return Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none() }
  return Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(run Lifetime.meet(chain))
}

effect fn placeDescriptors(nodes: &[Node], node: NodeId, chain: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  return match &nodes[node.index].kind {
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Dereference {value}, ..} => run descriptorChain(nodes, value, &mut chain.*)
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Field {value, ..}, ..} => run placeDescriptors(nodes, value, &mut chain.*)
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Index {value, ..}, ..} => {
      if sliceValue(nodes, value) { return run descriptorChain(nodes, value, &mut chain.*) }
      return run placeDescriptors(nodes, value, &mut chain.*)
    }
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.PatternBinding {subject, access, ..}, ..} => {
      if access == BindingAccess.Shared || access == BindingAccess.Exclusive { return run placeDescriptors(nodes, subject, &mut chain.*) }
      return ()
    }
    _ => ()
  }
}

// Appends one descriptor's lifetime and, unless it is shared, the descriptors its own place is
// reached through.
effect fn descriptorChain(nodes: &[Node], descriptor: NodeId, chain: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value} = move nodeLoanLifetime(nodes, descriptor) {
    run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut chain.*, move value)
    if !sharedDescriptor(nodes, descriptor) { run placeDescriptors(nodes, descriptor, &mut chain.*) }
  }
  return ()
}

fn sharedDescriptor(nodes: &[Node], node: NodeId) -> bool {
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, node) {
    return Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&value, fn(ty: &Type) -> bool {
      return match &ty.* {
        Type.Reference {access, ..} => access == Access.Shared
        Type.Slice {access, ..} => access == Access.Shared
        _ => false
      }
    })
  }
  return false
}

// Evaluates `base`, a value with no place, into its hidden owner and returns the point after it.
// The owner holds the loans that value carries and ends with the innermost statement, arm,
// condition, guard or short-circuit operand that evaluates it. In the initializer of a binding that
// can hold a view, lowering keeps every temporary for the binding's scope, so the owner's storage
// and cleanup end there; only a borrowed array stays valid that long, and any other temporary's
// loans expire with its statement (BORROW-006).
effect fn holdTemporary(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, base: NodeId, at: usize) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, base, at)
  let root = temporaryRoot(nodes, base.index)
  let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
  let holder = holderOf(&walker.*, root)
  let mut initialized = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  initialized[point].initializes = root
  initialized[point].defines = holder
  let retention = walker.retention
  run registerTemporary(&mut walker.*, root, retention != Retention.None)
  if retention == Retention.Storage || (retention == Retention.Arrays && !arrayValue(nodes, base)) {
    let at = List<Scope>.length(&walker.scopes) - usize.ONE
    let mut scopes = List<Scope>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.scopes)
    run List<usize>.append(&mut scopes[at].expiring, root)
  }
  if List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO {
    run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
    let retained = run nodeRetains(nodes, base, owner)
    if retained {
      run hold(&mut walker.*, root, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point, true)
    }
  }
  return point
}

// Whether `id` is a fixed array value.
fn arrayValue(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> bool {
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, id) {
    return Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&value, fn(node: &Type) -> bool {
      return match &node.* {
        Type.Array {..} => true
        _ => false
      }
    })
  }
  return false
}

// A captured exclusive descriptor's referent, reborrowed by the environment it was read into
// (CAPTURE-002). The loan's regions are the descriptor's, which the field keeps.
effect fn reborrowReferent(nodes: &[Node], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, operand: NodeId, exclusive: bool, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut path = run pathOf(nodes, operand)
  if path.root == usize.MAX || path.through || List<Step>.length(&path.steps) > usize.ZERO {
    leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
    return flowAt(at)
  }
  run List<Step>.append(&mut path.steps, referent())
  path.through = true
  let span = nodes[operand.index].origin.location
  let source = nodeLoanLifetime(nodes, operand)
  return run takeLoan(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, exclusive, span, operand.index, move source, at, List<Carry>.make())
}

// The referent of a borrow typed as a reference.
fn loanReferent(value: &Type) -> Option<Shared<Type>> {
  return match &value.* {
    Type.Reference {referent, ..} => Option<Shared<Type>>.some(Shared<Type>.clone(&referent))
    _ => Option<Shared<Type>>.none()
  }
}

// Records a new loan of `path` at a fresh point after `at`; the borrowing value carries it after
// `carried`. `node` is the expression whose type names the loan's regions, or `usize.MAX`.
effect fn takeLoan(nodes: &[Node], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, path: &Path, exclusive: bool, span: Location, node: usize,
  parent: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>, at: usize, carried: List<Carry>) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut onward = move carried
  let mut regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut borrowed = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  let mut viewed = Option<Shared<Type>>.none()
  if node != usize.MAX {
    borrowed = nodeLoanLifetime(nodes, NodeId {index: node})
    let typed = expressionType(nodes, NodeId {index: node})
    if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move typed {
      let known = run retainedBy(&value, owner, &mut regions)
      if !known {
        regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
      }
      viewed = Shared<Type>.with<Option<Shared<Type>>>(&value, loanReferent)
    }
  }
  let created = List<Loan>.length(&walker.loans)
  run List<Loan>.append(
    &mut walker.loans,
    Loan {
      place: Place {root: path.root, steps: run copySteps(List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps))},
      exclusive: exclusive,
      origin: span,
      intervals: List<Interval>.make(),
      precision: LoanPrecision.Exact,
      regions: move regions,
      local: !path.through,
      borrowed: move borrowed,
      parent: move parent,
      crossed: false,
      created: usize.MAX,
      escapes: false,
      binder: usize.MAX,
      block: usize.MAX,
      until: usize.MAX,
      referent: move viewed,
      bound: false,
    },
  )
  let mut kind = Kind.SharedBorrow
  if exclusive {
    kind = Kind.ExclusiveBorrow
  }
  let point = run access(&mut walker.*, path, kind, span, at, created)
  let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  loans[created].created = point
  run List<Carry>.append(&mut onward, Carry {loan: created, since: point, operand: usize.MAX, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, field: usize.ZERO, direct: true})
  return Flow {at: point, carried: move onward}
}

// Reads or moves a written place. An access rooted at a holder uses the holder, so its loans stay
// live through the access, and the accessed value carries them: a whole holder's move takes them to
// the new owner, and a part read out of it may hold them too (a reference field, for instance).
effect fn place(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, path: &Path, kind: Kind, span: Location, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let evaluated = run indexes(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, path, at)
  let lent = run useBinders(nodes, &mut walker.*, path, span, evaluated)
  if path.through {
    let reached = run throughReference(&mut walker.*, path, kind, span, lent)
    return move reached
  }
  if holds(&walker.*, path.root) {
    let read = run readPath(&mut walker.*, path)
    let used = run useHolder(&mut walker.*, path.root, read, span, lent)
    let accessed = run access(&mut walker.*, path, kind, span, used.at, usize.MAX)
    return Flow {at: accessed, carried: move used.carried}
  }
  let point = run access(&mut walker.*, path, kind, span, lent, usize.MAX)
  return flowAt(point)
}

// Evaluates operands in order and consumes everything they carry at one fresh point. A variant's
// operands lie within its `member` payload; any other aggregate's `member` is `usize.MAX`.
effect fn operands(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, values: &[NodeId], places: &[usize], member: usize,
  result: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  let mut current = at
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < values.length {
    let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, values[index], current)
    run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), index)
    current = flow.at
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  // An aggregate places each operand at its field, at its element of an array, or at its field of the
  // constructed variant's payload.
  let mut placed = List<List<Step>>.make()
  let elements = match move expressionType(nodes, result) {
    Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} => Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&value, arrayType)
    Option<Shared<Type>>.None => false
  }
  index = usize.ZERO
  while index < places.length {
    let mut steps = List<Step>.make()
    if member != usize.MAX { run List<Step>.append(&mut steps, memberStep(member)) }
    if elements {
      let mut step = Step {kind: StepKind.RepeatedElement, ordinal: usize.ZERO}
      if places[index] != usize.MAX { step = elementStep(places[index]) }
      run List<Step>.append(&mut steps, step)
    } else {
      run List<Step>.append(&mut steps, fieldStep(places[index]))
    }
    run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut placed, move steps)
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  run keepWrittenOperands(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, result, values, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried))
  let untyped = List<NodeId>.make()
  let noSinks = List<OperandSink>.make()
  return run finish(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, result, current, &carried, false, Forwarding.Operands, List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&placed), List<NodeId>.asSlice(&untyped), List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&noSinks))
}

// The type operand `operand` of call or record literal `result` has under the generic arguments the
// source wrote for it: the call's parameter type, or the literal's field type.
effect fn writtenOperandType(nodes: &[Node], result: NodeId, operand: usize) -> Option<Shared<Type>>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  // An immediate run's operands are those of the call it executes.
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Run {value, access}, ..} = &nodes[result.index].kind {
    if access == RunAccess.Immediate { return run writtenOperandType(nodes, value, operand) }
  }
  return match &nodes[result.index].kind {
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.DirectCall {written, ..}, ..} => {
      let chosen = List<Shared<Type>>.asSlice(&written)
      if operand < chosen.length { return Option<Shared<Type>>.some(Shared<Type>.clone(&chosen[operand])) }
      return Option<Shared<Type>>.none()
    }
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Aggregate {written, ..}, ..} => {
      let chosen = List<Shared<Type>>.asSlice(&written)
      if operand < chosen.length { return Option<Shared<Type>>.some(Shared<Type>.clone(&chosen[operand])) }
      return Option<Shared<Type>>.none()
    }
    _ => Option<Shared<Type>>.none()
  }
}

// A call or literal types each operand with the regions its written generic arguments chose: an
// operand typed there only at universal lifetime parameters must stay valid for them, so every
// loan it carries outlives the body wherever its creation reaches, its own borrow and those of a
// local reference it reborrows through alike. A loan of a body local is the region proof's to
// refute, since no universal region can outlive it.
effect fn keepWrittenOperands(nodes: &[Node], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, result: NodeId, operands: &[NodeId],
  carried: &[Carry]) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carried.length {
    if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value: typed} = move run writtenOperandType(nodes, result, carried[at].operand) {
      if run universallyTyped(&typed, owner) {
        let mut all = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
        if !all[carried[at].loan].local { all[carried[at].loan].escapes = true }
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// Which local loans a result that names only caller regions keeps exactly (see `finish`).
enum Forwarding {
  // None: the result's type decides what it holds, as for a call.
  None,
  // Every operand loan: the result is built from its operands.
  Operands,
  // The loans a place read found held where it reads (`Carry.field` known).
  Matched,
}

// Known result borrows also retain their actual reborrow ancestors. Follow only the borrowed
// atom and parent recorded when each loan was taken, never an inner retained atom or a typing
// obligation. Shared inference atoms describe possible sources, so the closure is a union;
// it does not establish exact retention. Existing Unknown precision remains Unknown.
effect fn retainedParents(loans: &[Loan], carried: &[Carry], named: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> List<bool>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut supported = List<bool>.make()
  let mut pending = List<usize>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carried.length {
    let mut seed = false
    if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value} = &loans[carried[at].loan].borrowed {
      seed = proofContains(named, &value)
    }
    run List<bool>.append(&mut supported, seed)
    if seed { run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, at) }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut next = usize.ZERO
  while next < List<usize>.length(&pending) {
    let queue = List<usize>.asSlice(&pending)
    let child = &loans[carried[queue[next]].loan]
    if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: parent} = &child.parent {
      at = usize.ZERO
      while at < carried.length {
        let seen = List<bool>.asSlice(&supported)
        if !seen[at] {
          if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loans[carried[at].loan].borrowed {
            if meetMember(&parent, &borrowed) {
              let mut marked = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut supported)
              marked[at] = true
              run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, at)
            }
          }
        }
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    next = next + usize.ONE
  }
  return move supported
}

// Whether `region` is a meet of this body's regions with universal ones. Such a meet is valid only
// while each of its local constituents is, and the universal ones outlive the body, so its local
// constituents carry every finite requirement it has: a binding that held a parameter's reference
// and is then assigned a borrow types the borrow under that meet.
fn localMeet(region: &Shared<Lifetime>, owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool {
  let count = Lifetime.atomCount(region)
  if count <= usize.ONE { return false }
  let mut local = false
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < count {
    let domain = regionDomain(&Lifetime.atomAt(region, at), owner, supplied)
    if domain == RegionDomain.Unknown { return false }
    if domain == RegionDomain.Local { local = true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return local
}

// Whether `region` is `named` itself or a local constituent of `named`, a `localMeet`.
fn carriesRegion(named: &Shared<Lifetime>, region: &Shared<Lifetime>, owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool {
  if Lifetime.equalsShared(named, region) { return true }
  return localMeet(named, owner, supplied) && meetMember(named, region)
}

// Whether one of `regions` carries `region` (`carriesRegion`).
fn regionsCarry(regions: &[Shared<Lifetime>], region: &Shared<Lifetime>, owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < regions.length {
    if carriesRegion(&regions[at], region, owner, supplied) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether some constituent of the meet `bound` is a region local to `owner`'s body.
fn meetHoldsLocal(bound: &Shared<Lifetime>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  let count = Lifetime.atomCount(bound)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < count {
    if regionLocal(&Lifetime.atomAt(bound, at), owner) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether `atom` is one of the descriptor lifetimes a reborrow's parent meet is made of.
fn meetMember(bound: &Shared<Lifetime>, atom: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> bool {
  let count = Lifetime.atomCount(bound)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < count {
    let member = Lifetime.atomAt(bound, at)
    if Lifetime.equalsShared(&member, atom) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// A complete known result must account for each local atom with an already-carried exact
// actual source. An inner atom in some unrelated loan's type is not that source's identity.
fn completeLocalResultSources(loans: &[Loan], carried: &[Carry], named: &[Shared<Lifetime>], owner: &DeclarationId,
  supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool {
  let mut source = usize.ZERO
  while source < carried.length {
    if loans[carried[source].loan].precision != LoanPrecision.Exact { return false }
    source = source + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut local = false
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < named.length {
    let domain = regionDomain(&named[at], owner, supplied)
    if domain == RegionDomain.Unknown { return false }
    if domain == RegionDomain.Local {
      local = true
      let mut found = false
      source = usize.ZERO
      while source < carried.length {
        let loan = &loans[carried[source].loan]
        if loan.precision == LoanPrecision.Exact {
          if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
            if Lifetime.equalsShared(&borrowed, &named[at])
              && proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions), &borrowed) { found = true }
          }
        }
        source = source + usize.ONE
      }
      if !found { return false }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return local
}

// Only a fresh exact borrow of owned storage can be released by the complete-source
// proof. Reborrow ancestry, required sources, and any previous uncertainty remain authoritative.
fn unneededOwnedLoan(loan: &Loan, owner: &DeclarationId, named: &[Shared<Lifetime>], required: &[usize], ancestor: bool) -> bool {
  if !loan.local || loan.precision != LoanPrecision.Exact || ancestor || requiredLoan(loan, owner, required) { return false }
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {..} = &loan.parent { return false }
  let regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
  if regions.length != usize.ONE { return false }
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
    return retentionOrdinal(&borrowed, owner) != usize.MAX && Lifetime.equalsShared(&regions[0], &borrowed)
      && !proofContains(named, &borrowed)
  }
  return false
}

// Read the same source component as Semantic.resultSourceAtoms: a shared reference supplies
// its outer access region, while other shapes require complete stored-region evidence. Knowing
// an outer reference never authenticates an unknown referent or any loan within that referent.
effect fn declaredSourceRegions(nodes: &[Node], source: NodeId, owner: &DeclarationId, regions: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, source) {
    if let Type.Reference {access, lifetime, ..} = move run Type.copy(&value) {
      if access == Access.Shared {
        run appendAtoms(&mut regions.*, &lifetime)
        return true
      }
    }
  }
  return run resultRegions(nodes, source, owner, &mut regions.*)
}

// Preserve an exact finite source only when the declared signature permits this operand
// to supply the result and its authenticated region is the loan's actual borrowed region.
// Reborrow ancestors follow their authenticated parent edges within that same operand.
// Neither an unrelated inner atom nor prior Alternatives/Unknown can acquire this evidence.
effect fn declaredResultLoans(nodes: &[Node], result: NodeId, carried: &[Carry], loans: &[Loan], owner: &DeclarationId)
-> List<bool> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut call = result
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Run {value, access}, ..} = &nodes[result.index].kind {
    if access == RunAccess.Immediate { call = value }
  }
  let mut proven = List<bool>.make()
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < carried.length {
    let carry = &carried[index]
    let loan = &loans[carry.loan]
    let mut exact = false
    if loan.precision == LoanPrecision.Exact && carry.field != usize.MAX {
      if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.DirectCall {arguments, resultBorrows, ..}, ..} = &nodes[call.index].kind {
        let operands = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)
        let selected = List<ResultBorrow>.asSlice(&resultBorrows)
        let mut at = usize.ZERO
        while carry.operand < operands.length && at < selected.length {
          if selected[at].argument.index == operands[carry.operand].index {
            let mut named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
            if run declaredSourceRegions(nodes, selected[at].argument, owner, &mut named) {
              let regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named)
              let actual = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
              if regions.length == usize.ONE && actual.length == usize.ONE {
                if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
                  exact = Lifetime.equalsShared(&regions[0], &borrowed) && Lifetime.equalsShared(&actual[0], &borrowed)
                }
              }
            }
          }
          at = at + usize.ONE
        }
      }
    }
    run List<bool>.append(&mut proven, exact)
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut changed = true
  while changed {
    changed = false
    index = usize.ZERO
    while index < carried.length {
      if List<bool>.asSlice(&proven)[index] {
        if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: parent} = &loans[carried[index].loan].parent {
          let mut ancestor = usize.ZERO
          while ancestor < carried.length {
            let loan = &loans[carried[ancestor].loan]
            if !List<bool>.asSlice(&proven)[ancestor] && carried[ancestor].operand == carried[index].operand
              && loan.precision == LoanPrecision.Exact {
              if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
                if meetMember(&parent, &borrowed) {
                  let mut marked = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut proven)
                  marked[ancestor] = true
                  changed = true
                }
              }
            }
            ancestor = ancestor + usize.ONE
          }
        }
      }
      index = index + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return move proven
}

// Place an authenticated source at each complete result field path the signature can return it in.
// This mapping must not be reconstructed from inferred output atoms: sibling binders may coincide.
effect fn declaredResultCarries(nodes: &[Node], result: NodeId, walker: &mut Walker, carry: Carry, point: usize,
  onward: &mut List<Carry>) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut call = result
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Run {value, access}, ..} = &nodes[result.index].kind {
    if access == RunAccess.Immediate { call = value }
  }
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.DirectCall {arguments, resultBorrows, ..}, ..} = &nodes[call.index].kind {
    let operands = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)
    let sources = List<ResultBorrow>.asSlice(&resultBorrows)
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while carry.operand < operands.length && at < sources.length {
      if sources[at].argument.index == operands[carry.operand].index {
        let mut path = List<Step>.make()
        let fields = List<usize>.asSlice(&sources[at].fields)
        let mut step = usize.ZERO
        while step < fields.length {
          run List<Step>.append(&mut path, fieldStep(fields[step]))
          step = step + usize.ONE
        }
        let field = run internPath(&mut walker.*, move path)
        run List<Carry>.append(&mut onward.*, Carry {loan: carry.loan, since: point, operand: usize.MAX,
          definition: carry.definition, read: carry.read, field: field, direct: false})
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return ()
}

// Records the operands of the direct call `result` whose loans its result cannot hold.
effect fn recordUnheld(nodes: &[Node], walker: &mut Walker, result: NodeId) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.DirectCall {arguments, ..}, ..} = &nodes[result.index].kind {
    let operands = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < operands.length {
      if !retainedOperand(nodes, result, at) {
        run List<Location>.append(&mut walker.unheld, nodes[operands[at].index].origin.location)
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return ()
}

// Whether `site` lies in an operand whose loans its call's result cannot hold (`Walker.unheld`). A
// `return` or a store nested in that operand sends its own value elsewhere, so a site inside one is
// decided there, not by the call.
fn unheldSite(walker: &Walker, site: Location) -> bool {
  let unheld = List<Location>.asSlice(&walker.unheld)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < unheld.length {
    if within(site, unheld[at]) && !nestedWindow(List<StoreWindow>.asSlice(&walker.returns), site, unheld[at])
      && !nestedWindow(List<StoreWindow>.asSlice(&walker.stores), site, unheld[at]) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

fn within(inner: Location, outer: Location) -> bool {
  return inner.start >= outer.start && inner.end <= outer.end
}

// Whether one of `windows` lies within `operand` and holds `site`.
fn nestedWindow(windows: &[StoreWindow], site: Location, operand: Location) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < windows.length {
    if within(windows[at].span, operand) && within(site, windows[at].span) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a direct call's result can hold what its operand `operand` carries: typing lists the
// arguments the callee's signature lets its result retain. Any other result, and a loan carried by
// no single operand, may hold it.
fn retainedOperand(nodes: &[Node], result: NodeId, operand: usize) -> bool {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.DirectCall {arguments, retained, ..}, ..} = &nodes[result.index].kind {
    let operands = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)
    if operand >= operands.length { return true }
    let listed = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&retained)
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < listed.length {
      if listed[at].index == operands[operand].index { return true }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    return false
  }
  return true
}

// Whether typing requires one of `regions` to outlive one of `named`: a relation offers a region of
// the loan and wants a region of the result.
fn outlivesResult(relations: &[ImpliedGroup], regions: &[Shared<Lifetime>], named: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < relations.length {
    if sharesAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&relations[at].members), regions)
      && sharesAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&relations[at].container), named) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}


// Operation-wide facts are sampled before the per-carry loop. The loan supplied to
// resultDecision is sampled at that carry, after all preceding carries' effects.
struct ResultFacts {
  stores: bool
  known: bool
  outside: bool
  forwarding: Forwarding
  placedCount: usize
  naming: usize
  several: bool
  complete: bool
  retained: bool
  declared: bool
  ancestor: bool
}

// Explicit effects of the result policy. Keeping a source never repairs prior precision.
struct ResultDecision {
  kept: bool
  precision: LoanPrecision
  bound: bool
  unretained: bool
  declared: bool
  whole: bool
  described: bool
}

effect fn resultDecision(loan: &Loan, carry: Carry, facts: &ResultFacts, owner: &DeclarationId,
  named: &[Shared<Lifetime>], requiredSources: &[usize], relations: &[ImpliedGroup], implied: &Implied, field: usize, hasTyped: bool) -> ResultDecision
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut precision = loan.precision
  let mut bound = false
  let mut kept = true
  let mut exact = false
  let mut dropped = false
  if facts.stores {
    exact = true
  } else if !facts.retained && !requiredLoan(loan, owner, requiredSources) {
    kept = false
  } else if facts.known {
    let regionsOf = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
    let forwarded = facts.forwarding == Forwarding.Operands
      || (facts.forwarding == Forwarding.Matched && carry.field != usize.MAX)
    if facts.outside && forwarded && loan.local {
      // A value built from its operands holds their loans, as does a value read from where a
      // loan is held, and a loan of storage this body owns cannot outlive a caller region
      // whatever typing related: the result keeps it exactly so the walk reports where it
      // escapes (OWN0019).
      exact = true
    } else if facts.outside && loan.local && facts.forwarding != Forwarding.Matched
      && outlivesResult(relations, regionsOf, named) {
      // A call or `run` result that can retain the loan holds a loan of storage this body owns
      // when typing requires the loan's own region to outlive a region the result names:
      // typing bound the result to caller regions only, which no solution lets the loan
      // outlive. The result keeps it exactly, as when the binding names the loan's own
      // region, so the walk reports where it escapes (OWN0019) rather than leaving the
      // relation unproved, unless the return-slot refutation decides it (`Loan.bound`). A
      // value read from where the loan lies somewhere within is not that result: it may be a
      // part the loan does not reach.
      exact = true
      bound = true
    } else if facts.declared {
      // An authenticated declared source survives filtering by instantiated result atoms.
      // Owned-storage escape and bound diagnostics above retain their original precedence.
      exact = true
    } else if facts.outside && (loan.local || bodyRegions(regionsOf, owner)) {
      kept = false
      dropped = true
    } else if facts.complete && unneededOwnedLoan(loan, owner, named, requiredSources, facts.ancestor) {
      kept = false
    } else if facts.several && facts.forwarding == Forwarding.Operands && carry.operand < facts.placedCount
      && regionsOf.length > usize.ZERO && (sharesAtom(regionsOf, named) || requiredLoan(loan, owner, requiredSources)) {
      // A value built from its operands holds each operand's loans exactly where it places
      // them, however many of them name a result region; only a call's result leaves open
      // which of them it retains.
      exact = true
    } else if !facts.several && facts.naming == carry.operand && regionsOf.length > usize.ZERO
      && (sharesAtom(regionsOf, named) || requiredLoan(loan, owner, requiredSources)) {
      exact = true
    } else if implied.known && loan.precision == LoanPrecision.Exact
      && !facts.ancestor && !requiredLoan(loan, owner, requiredSources)
      && bodyRegions(regionsOf, owner) && !run mayOutlive(implied, regionsOf, named, owner) {
      kept = false
    }
  }
  if kept {
    if !exact {
      let regionsOf = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
      let ancestor = facts.ancestor
      let alternatives = facts.known && ((facts.several && regionsOf.length > usize.ZERO
        && (sharesAtom(regionsOf, named) || requiredLoan(loan, owner, requiredSources))) || ancestor)
      if alternatives {
        // All possible operands are retained. Preserve prior uncertainty: a later call
        // cannot repair a mapping already lost at another operation.
        if loan.precision == LoanPrecision.Exact { precision = LoanPrecision.Alternatives }
        else if loan.precision == LoanPrecision.Stored { precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown }
      } else {
        precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown
      }
    }
  }
  let declared = !facts.stores && facts.declared
  return ResultDecision {kept: kept, precision: precision, bound: bound, unretained: dropped,
    declared: declared, whole: kept && !declared && field == usize.ZERO && facts.forwarding != Forwarding.Matched,
    described: !facts.stores && facts.forwarding == Forwarding.None && hasTyped}
}

// Consumes carried loans at a fresh point for `result`, which keeps carrying the loans it can
// retain (VIEW-002), so a returned view holds its source loan through its last use. Typing gives the
// result its instantiated regions, with the callee's bounds, type arguments and elisions applied:
// - A result whose regions are all static or enclosing/own lifetime parameters, or that is one
//   of its type parameters, holds no loan of a body local or with a body region, which cannot
//   outlive them; the region slice proves that relation. A result that `forwards` its operands'
//   values (an aggregate or an operator) is the exception for a loan of storage the body owns:
//   the value still holds it, so it keeps flowing exactly and its storage end reports the escape.
//   So is a call or `run` result that can retain such a loan when typing requires the loan's
//   region to outlive a result region: typing's binding to caller regions then demands what no
//   solution gives.
//   A read place does not forward: reading through a borrow of a local carries that borrow's
//   loan, which a value copied out of it does not hold.
// - When exactly one operand's loans name a result region, the result may hold them: a conflict
//   rejects.
// - A declared result preserves authenticated finite sources, including reborrow ancestors,
//   through shared views and stored inputs. This proof precedes inference of call atoms.
// - Other operands naming a known result form a complete union of possible source loans.
//   The region proof must check all of them, while a conflict with one remains imprecise:
//   sharing a fresh call atom does not prove which operand the result actually retains.
// - Other undecided retention stays unknown, including callable capture loans whose regions
//   the result type does not name. Unknown retention cannot participate in a region proof.
// - A loan whose regions are all body regions, of a call whose signature types it, is not held when
//   none of them can outlive a result region. Typing relates two body regions only by equality or
//   a meet, which shares an atom, or by a region relation it leaves open, so a callee can reach a
//   result region only through those relations and the outlives facts its parameter and result
//   types imply: a reference's or slice's referent outlives its region, and a nominal's arguments
//   may outlive one another. If they lead the loan's regions to a result region, or to a region
//   from outside the body, whose premises the walk does not read, the loan stays carried,
//   approximately. Retained capture contents relate regions in ways the walk does not describe, so
//   a body with them keeps every such loan.
// - A direct call's result holds no loan an operand carries when the callee's declared signature,
//   with its lifetime binders distinct, relates none of that argument's regions to a region its
//   result names, through its bounds and the bounds its types imply (typing's `retained`). The
//   callee's body is proved against that signature, so typing's region relations cannot route the
//   loan into the result, whatever atoms they share; a loan the region requirements need stays.
// A `stores` result keeps every operand, as the Effect an `effect fn` call constructs does, so it
// keeps all their loans exactly whatever regions its type names.
effect fn finish(nodes: &[Node], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, result: NodeId, at: usize, carried: &List<Carry>,
  stores: bool, forwarding: Forwarding, placed: &[List<Step>], typed: &[NodeId], sinks: &[OperandSink]) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, at)
  let mut onward = List<Carry>.make()
  if !run nodeRetains(nodes, result, owner) {
    run List<Location>.append(&mut walker.sealed, nodes[result.index].origin.location)
  }
  run recordUnheld(nodes, &mut walker.*, result)
  // A loan a call can keep in a universal region must outlive the body; one that reaches a call this
  // walk cannot describe leaves the body unchecked.
  run keepCarried(&mut walker.*, owner, List<Carry>.asSlice(carried), sinks, usize.MAX, point)
  if List<Carry>.length(carried) > usize.ZERO {
    run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(carried), point)
    let retained = run nodeRetains(nodes, result, owner)
    if retained {
      let mut regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
      let known = run resultRegions(nodes, result, owner, &mut regions)
      let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&regions)
      let outside = known && externalRegions(named, owner)
      let loans = List<Carry>.asSlice(carried)
      let mut parents = List<bool>.make()
      if known && !stores && loans.length > usize.ONE {
        parents = run retainedParents(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), loans, named)
      }
      let supported = List<bool>.asSlice(&parents)
      let declared = run declaredResultLoans(nodes, result, loans, List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), owner)
      let declaredSources = List<bool>.asSlice(&declared)
      let mut required = List<usize>.make()
      if known && !stores {
        required = run requiredRetainedRegions(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), loans, named, owner,
          List<RetentionEdge>.asSlice(&walker.requirements))
      }
      let requiredSources = List<usize>.asSlice(&required)
      // The one operand whose loans may name a result region, or `usize.MAX`.
      let mut naming = usize.MAX
      let mut several = false
      // Whether a loan has body regions that no result region shares.
      let mut unnamed = false
      let mut index = usize.ZERO
      while index < loans.length {
        let all = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
        let regionsOf = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&all[loans[index].loan].regions)
        // A loan the result cannot hold names none of its regions.
        let held = retainedOperand(nodes, result, loans[index].operand) || requiredLoan(&all[loans[index].loan], owner, requiredSources)
        if held && (regionsOf.length == usize.ZERO || sharesAtom(regionsOf, named)
          || requiredLoan(&all[loans[index].loan], owner, requiredSources)) {
          if naming == usize.MAX {
            naming = loans[index].operand
          } else if naming != loans[index].operand {
            several = true
          }
        } else if held && bodyRegions(regionsOf, owner) {
          unnamed = true
        }
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
      let complete = known && !stores && !outside && !several && naming != usize.MAX && loans.length > usize.ONE
        && completeLocalResultSources(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), loans, named, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied))
      let mut implied = noImplied()
      if unnamed && known && !stores && typed.length > usize.ZERO {
        implied = run callImplied(nodes, &walker.*, typed, result)
      }
      index = usize.ZERO
      while index < loans.length {
        let loan = loans[index].loan
        // Where the result holds the loan: where a read found it, under its operand's place in a
        // built aggregate, or somewhere within the whole result.
        let mut field = usize.ZERO
        let mut direct = false
        if forwarding == Forwarding.Matched {
          field = loans[index].field
          direct = loans[index].direct
        } else if loans[index].operand < placed.length {
          field = run prefixedPath(&mut walker.*, List<Step>.asSlice(&placed[loans[index].operand]), loans[index].field)
          direct = loans[index].direct
        }
        direct = direct && field != usize.MAX
        let facts = ResultFacts {stores: stores, known: known, outside: outside, forwarding: forwarding,
          placedCount: placed.length, naming: naming, several: several, complete: complete,
          retained: retainedOperand(nodes, result, loans[index].operand),
          declared: index < declaredSources.length && declaredSources[index],
          ancestor: index < supported.length && supported[index]}
        let decision = run resultDecision(&List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)[loan], loans[index], &facts,
          owner, named, requiredSources, List<ImpliedGroup>.asSlice(&walker.retentionRelations), &implied, field, typed.length > usize.ZERO)
        let mut all = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
        if decision.bound { all[loan].bound = true }
        all[loan].precision = decision.precision
        if decision.kept {
          if decision.declared {
            run declaredResultCarries(nodes, result, &mut walker.*, loans[index], point, &mut onward)
          } else {
            run List<Carry>.append(&mut onward, Carry {loan: loan, since: point, operand: usize.MAX, definition: loans[index].definition, read: loans[index].read, field: field, direct: direct})
          }
          if decision.whole {
            run List<WholeHold>.append(&mut walker.wholeHolds, WholeHold {loan: loan, result: result,
              described: decision.described})
          }
        }
        if decision.unretained { run List<usize>.append(&mut walker.unretained, loan) }
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
    }
  }
  return Flow {at: point, carried: move onward}
}

// The regions a field or pattern binding read holds as its place is declared, the subject's type
// instantiated into the field's declared type before typing fits the read's own type to its use;
// unknown for any other read, or when the declared type's regions are unknown.
struct DeclaredRead {
  known: bool
  regions: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
}

effect fn declaredRead(nodes: &[Node], read: NodeId, owner: &DeclarationId) -> DeclaredRead
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut known = false
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form, ..} = &nodes[read.index].kind {
    if let Expression.Field {declared, ..} = &form {
      known = run bodyRetainedRegions(&declared, owner, &mut regions)
    } else if let Expression.PatternBinding {declared, ..} = &form {
      known = run bodyRetainedRegions(&declared, owner, &mut regions)
    }
  }
  return DeclaredRead {known: known, regions: move regions}
}

// The regions `result`'s value can retain; `false` when they are unknown, as for a callable, whose
// capture loans its type does not name. A type parameter bound outside the body, by the checked
// declaration or by one enclosing it (a method's impl, an anonymous body's enclosing function),
// retains no region of the body, alone or inside the result: it is instantiated before the body runs
// with a type that cannot name a region the body creates, and safe code obtains a value of it only as
// such a value. A region the body itself binds, a loan region or an invocation binder, is not erased.
effect fn resultRegions(nodes: &[Node], result: NodeId, owner: &DeclarationId, regions: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let found = expressionType(nodes, result)
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move found {
    if Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&value, callableValue) {
      return false
    }
    return run bodyRetainedRegions(&value, owner, &mut regions.*)
  }
  return false
}

// Types chosen outside this body cannot name one of its fresh loan regions. Apply the same
// parametricity proof to holders and projections as to call results.
effect fn bodyRetainedRegions(
  value: &Shared<Type>,
  owner: &DeclarationId,
  regions: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>
) -> bool
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  // Type parameters bound outside the body stand for types chosen before it runs, so they are
  // read as retaining nothing; what remains is the regions the result can hold of this body.
  let mut bindings = List<Binding>.make()
  let mut depth = DeclarationId.ownerCount(owner)
  while depth > usize.ZERO {
    let binder = run Shared<DeclarationId>.make(run DeclarationId.enclosing(owner, depth))
    let mut types = List<usize>.make()
    let mut lifetimes = List<usize>.make()
    let mut rows = List<usize>.make()
    let declaration = DeclarationId.copyShared(&binder)
    run Type.collectOwned(value, &declaration, &mut types, &mut lifetimes, &mut rows)
    let ordinals = List<usize>.asSlice(&types)
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < ordinals.length {
      run List<
        Binding
      >.append(
        &mut bindings,
        Binding {
          declaration: Shared<DeclarationId>.clone(&binder),
          ordinal: ordinals[at],
          value: Argument.Type { value: run Types.intern(Type.Unit) },
        }
      )
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    depth = depth - usize.ONE
  }
  if List<Binding>.length(&bindings) == usize.ZERO {
    return run retainedBy(value, owner, &mut regions.*)
  }
  let erased = run Type.applyBindings(value, List<Binding>.asSlice(&bindings), true)
  return run retainedBy(&erased, owner, &mut regions.*)
}

// Whether every atom is static or a parameter chosen outside this body. A result promising
// only these regions cannot retain owned body storage. Static source loans still remain live:
// their region is external too, so the filter does not erase them as fresh body loans.
fn externalRegions(regions: &[Shared<Lifetime>], owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < regions.length {
    let parameter = Lifetime.allAtoms(&regions[at], fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> bool {
      return match &atom.* {
        Lifetime.Static => true
        Lifetime.Parameter {declaration, ..} => DeclarationId.isPrefixOf(&declaration, owner)
        _ => false
      }
    })
    if !parameter {
      return false
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Whether `regions` is known and every atom of it is a body region of the checked declaration, as
// typing gives a fresh borrow, even a reborrow through a reference parameter.
fn bodyRegions(regions: &[Shared<Lifetime>], owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  if regions.length == usize.ZERO {
    return false
  }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < regions.length {
    let local = Lifetime.allAtoms(&regions[at], fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> bool {
      return match &atom.* {
        Lifetime.Local {declaration, ..} => DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner)
        _ => false
      }
    })
    if !local {
      return false
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// The outlives facts a call's argument and result types imply by being well formed, which its
// callee may assume: a reference's or slice's referent outlives its region, and the arguments of
// a nominal may outlive one another by its declared bounds, so they are taken as one class. `known`
// is false when a type has a form this summary does not describe.
struct Implied {
  groups: List<ImpliedGroup>
  known: bool
}

// The atoms of one well-formedness fact: every member outlives every container atom, or, with no
// container, the members of one nominal may outlive one another.
struct ImpliedGroup {
  container: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
  members: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
}

// What a dropped loan's region proof can ground on: the loans naming a region the proof walks,
// and those regions. The walk past the drop cannot see where the dropped loan goes, so an access
// that conflicts with any of these loans after the drop contests every one of these regions.
struct UnretainedChain {
  dropped: usize
  loans: List<usize>
  regions: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
}

fn noImplied() -> Implied {
  return Implied {groups: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), known: false}
}

// The facts a direct call `result` implies, exactly: the body's open region relations and the
// outlives bounds its callee's signature implies (`impliedSignatureBounds`), which typing proved of
// the call. An immediate run implies those of the call it executes; any other node, nothing known.
effect fn signatureImplied(nodes: &[Node], walker: &Walker, result: NodeId) -> Implied
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut call = result
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Run {value, access}, ..} = &nodes[result.index].kind {
    if access == RunAccess.Immediate { call = value }
  }
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.DirectCall {implied: stated, ..}, ..} = &nodes[call.index].kind {
    let mut implied = Implied {groups: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), known: walker.settled}
    let premises = List<ImpliedGroup>.asSlice(&walker.retentionRelations)
    let mut premise = usize.ZERO
    while premise < premises.length {
      let mut members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
      run appendAllAtoms(&mut members, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&premises[premise].members))
      let mut container = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
      run appendAllAtoms(&mut container, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&premises[premise].container))
      run List<ImpliedGroup>.append(&mut implied.groups, ImpliedGroup {container: move container, members: move members})
      premise = premise + usize.ONE
    }
    let facts = List<ImpliedOutlives>.asSlice(&stated)
    let mut fact = usize.ZERO
    while fact < facts.length {
      let mut members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
      run appendAllAtoms(&mut members, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&facts[fact].longer))
      let mut container = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
      run appendAllAtoms(&mut container, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&facts[fact].shorter))
      run List<ImpliedGroup>.append(&mut implied.groups, ImpliedGroup {container: move container, members: move members})
      fact = fact + usize.ONE
    }
    return move implied
  }
  return noImplied()
}

// The facts a call implies: the body's open region relations and the well-formedness of the
// types of `arguments` and `result`.
effect fn callImplied(nodes: &[Node], walker: &Walker, arguments: &[NodeId], result: NodeId) -> Implied
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut implied = Implied {groups: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), known: walker.settled}
  let premises = List<ImpliedGroup>.asSlice(&walker.retentionRelations)
  let mut premise = usize.ZERO
  while premise < premises.length {
    let mut members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
    run appendAllAtoms(&mut members, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&premises[premise].members))
    let mut container = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
    run appendAllAtoms(&mut container, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&premises[premise].container))
    run List<ImpliedGroup>.append(&mut implied.groups, ImpliedGroup {container: move container, members: move members})
    premise = premise + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut atoms = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index <= arguments.length {
    let mut typed = Option<Shared<Type>>.none()
    if index < arguments.length { typed = expressionType(nodes, arguments[index]) } else { typed = expressionType(nodes, result) }
    if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move typed {
      run implies(&value, &mut implied, &mut atoms)
    } else {
      implied.known = false
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return move implied
}

effect fn appendAtoms(target: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>, region: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let count = Lifetime.atomCount(region)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < count {
    run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut target.*, Lifetime.atomAt(region, at))
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

effect fn appendAllAtoms(target: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>, atoms: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < atoms.length {
    run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut target.*, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&atoms[at]))
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// Records the facts `ty` implies and appends every atom it names to `atoms`.
effect fn implies(ty: &Shared<Type>, implied: &mut Implied, atoms: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  match move run Type.copy(ty) {
    Type.Primitive {..} => {}
    Type.Unit => {}
    // A type parameter bound outside the body names no body region (see `bodyRetainedRegions`).
    Type.Parameter {..} => {}
    Type.String {lifetime} => {
      run appendAtoms(&mut atoms.*, &lifetime)
    }
    Type.Reference {referent, lifetime, ..} => {
      run contained(&referent, &lifetime, &mut implied.*, &mut atoms.*)
    }
    Type.Slice {element, lifetime, ..} => {
      run contained(&element, &lifetime, &mut implied.*, &mut atoms.*)
    }
    Type.Array {element, ..} => {
      run implies(&element, &mut implied.*, &mut atoms.*)
    }
    Type.Nominal {arguments, ..} => {
      let mut inner = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
      let listed = List<Argument>.asSlice(&arguments)
      let mut at = usize.ZERO
      while at < listed.length {
        match &listed[at] {
          Argument.Type {value} => {
            run implies(&value, &mut implied.*, &mut inner)
          }
          Argument.Lifetime {value} => {
            run appendAtoms(&mut inner, &value)
          }
          Argument.Row {..} => {
            implied.known = false
          }
        }
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
      run appendAllAtoms(&mut atoms.*, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&inner))
      run List<ImpliedGroup>.append(&mut implied.groups, ImpliedGroup {container: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), members: move inner})
    }
    _ => {
      implied.known = false
    }
  }
  return ()
}

// Records that every atom `inside` names outlives `region`.
effect fn contained(inside: &Shared<Type>, region: &Shared<Lifetime>, implied: &mut Implied, atoms: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut inner = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run implies(inside, &mut implied.*, &mut inner)
  let mut container = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run appendAtoms(&mut container, region)
  run appendAllAtoms(&mut atoms.*, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&inner))
  run appendAllAtoms(&mut atoms.*, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&container))
  run List<ImpliedGroup>.append(&mut implied.groups, ImpliedGroup {container: move container, members: move inner})
  return ()
}

fn containsAtom(atoms: &[Shared<Lifetime>], atom: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < atoms.length {
    if Lifetime.equalsShared(&atoms[at], atom) {
      return true
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a loan with body regions `from` may outlive a region of `named` through the facts
// `implied` records: the atoms the facts reach from `from` include one of `named`, or one from
// outside the body, whose premises are not read here.
effect fn mayOutlive(implied: &Implied, from: &[Shared<Lifetime>], named: &[Shared<Lifetime>], owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut reached = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < from.length {
    run appendAtoms(&mut reached, &from[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let groups = List<ImpliedGroup>.asSlice(&implied.groups)
  let mut changed = true
  while changed {
    changed = false
    let mut group = usize.ZERO
    while group < groups.length {
      let members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&groups[group].members)
      let mut entered = false
      let mut member = usize.ZERO
      while !entered && member < members.length {
        entered = containsAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&reached), &members[member])
        member = member + usize.ONE
      }
      if entered {
        let mut targets = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&groups[group].container)
        if targets.length == usize.ZERO {
          targets = members
        }
        let mut target = usize.ZERO
        while target < targets.length {
          if !containsAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&reached), &targets[target]) {
            run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut reached, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&targets[target]))
            changed = true
          }
          target = target + usize.ONE
        }
      }
      group = group + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  let atoms = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&reached)
  return !bodyRegions(atoms, owner) || sharesAtom(atoms, named)
}

// Whether any atom of `left` is an atom of `right`.
fn sharesAtom(left: &[Shared<Lifetime>], right: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool {
  let mut first = usize.ZERO
  while first < left.length {
    let leftCount = Lifetime.atomCount(&left[first])
    let mut leftAt = usize.ZERO
    while leftAt < leftCount {
      let atom = Lifetime.atomAt(&left[first], leftAt)
      let mut second = usize.ZERO
      while second < right.length {
        let rightCount = Lifetime.atomCount(&right[second])
        let mut rightAt = usize.ZERO
        while rightAt < rightCount {
          let other = Lifetime.atomAt(&right[second], rightAt)
          if Lifetime.equalsShared(&atom, &other) {
            return true
          }
          rightAt = rightAt + usize.ONE
        }
        second = second + usize.ONE
      }
      leftAt = leftAt + usize.ONE
    }
    first = first + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

effect fn fieldIndexes(fields: &[AggregateField]) -> List<usize> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut indexes = List<usize>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < fields.length {
    run List<usize>.append(&mut indexes, fields[at].index)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move indexes
}

// Where each field, in evaluation order, can have what it carries stored, from per-ordinal answers.
// A field typing recorded no answer for can hold anywhere.
effect fn fieldHoldable(fields: &[AggregateField], holdable: &[CaptureHold]) -> List<CaptureHold> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut ordered = List<CaptureHold>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < fields.length {
    let mut hold = CaptureHold.Any
    if fields[at].index < holdable.length { hold = holdable[fields[at].index] }
    run List<CaptureHold>.append(&mut ordered, hold)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move ordered
}

effect fn fieldValues(fields: &[AggregateField]) -> List<NodeId> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut values = List<NodeId>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < fields.length {
    run List<NodeId>.append(&mut values, fields[at].value)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move values
}

// The referent captures of an environment, each naming the position of its field's operand.
effect fn referentOperands(fields: &[AggregateField], referents: &[ReferentCapture]) -> List<ReferentCapture>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut operands = List<ReferentCapture>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < referents.length {
    let mut position = usize.ZERO
    while position < fields.length && fields[position].index != referents[at].field {
      position = position + usize.ONE
    }
    run List<ReferentCapture>.append(&mut operands, ReferentCapture {field: position, access: referents[at].access})
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move operands
}

effect fn single(value: NodeId) -> List<NodeId> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut values = List<NodeId>.make()
  run List<NodeId>.append(&mut values, value)
  return move values
}

effect fn copyIds(values: &[NodeId]) -> List<NodeId> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut copied = List<NodeId>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < values.length {
    run List<NodeId>.append(&mut copied, values[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move copied
}

// A call's arguments in order. A shared or mutable receiver pass borrows the receiver place for the
// whole call; a taking receiver pass moves it.
effect fn call(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, arguments: &[NodeId], receiver: usize, exact: bool,
  signature: bool, result: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  let mut current = at
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < arguments.length {
    let argument = arguments[index]
    let mut handled = false
    if index == usize.ZERO && receiver != usize.ZERO {
      let path = run pathOf(nodes, argument)
      if path.root != usize.MAX && !isBorrow(nodes, argument) {
        let span = nodes[argument.index].origin.location
        let mut flow = flowAt(current)
        if receiver == 3 {
          flow = run place(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Read, span, current)
        } else {
          flow = run borrow(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, argument, receiver == 2, span, usize.MAX, current)
        }
        run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), index)
        current = flow.at
        handled = true
      }
    }
    if !handled {
      let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, argument, current)
      run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), index)
      current = flow.at
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut typed = List<NodeId>.make()
  if signature {
    typed = run copyIds(arguments)
  }
  run keepWrittenOperands(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, result, arguments, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried))
  let sinks = run operandSinks(nodes, result, arguments, owner)
  let unplaced = List<List<Step>>.make()
  let called = run finish(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, result, current, &carried, exact, Forwarding.None, List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&unplaced), List<NodeId>.asSlice(&typed), List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&sinks))
  let lent = run storeIntoLent(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, result, arguments, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried),
    nodes[result.index].origin.location, called.at)
  // The callee may invoke a closure an argument carries, whether passed by value, by reference, or
  // within a holder, so its storable loans reach the call as that closure's do.
  let stored = run storeThroughExclusive(locals, owner, &mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried), List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried),
    nodes[result.index].origin.location, lent)
  return Flow {at: stored, carried: move called.carried}
}

// A call can keep an operand's loans in the caller regions its signature lets it write (`KeptRegions`,
// R3 amendment 4). A body holder the call lends exclusively, whose type names such a region, may
// receive through that `&mut` each loan lying in an operand slot whose contract can store there,
// including a view shortened under an outlives bound or copied from another holder. It holds
// those from the call on, as a field store into it would: an access to their referents conflicts
// with them while the holder lives, and a value read from the holder carries them. A holder that is
// a reference holding body loans may reach body storage the walk cannot place, so such a store
// leaves the body unchecked; a reference this body was passed reaches caller storage, which the
// region proof answers for.
effect fn storeIntoLent(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, result: NodeId, arguments: &[NodeId],
  carried: &[Carry], span: Location, at: usize) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  if carried.length == usize.ZERO || walker.outside || at == usize.MAX { return at }
  let recorded = match move callKept(nodes, result) {
    Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.Some {value} => move value
    _ => { return at }
  }
  let mut holders = List<usize>.make()
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  while index < carried.length {
    let lent = loans[carried[index].loan].place.root
    if loans[carried[index].loan].exclusive && lent < walker.localCount && !listsIndex(List<usize>.asSlice(&holders), lent) {
      run List<usize>.append(&mut holders, lent)
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut point = at
  let roots = List<usize>.asSlice(&holders)
  let mut holder = usize.ZERO
  while holder < roots.length {
    let root = roots[holder]
    let ty = localType(locals, root)
    let mut named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
    run Type.regionAtoms(&ty, &mut named)
    let mut received = List<Carry>.make()
    if run retains(&ty, owner) {
      index = usize.ZERO
      while index < carried.length {
        let operand = carried[index].operand
        let loan = carried[index].loan
        if List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)[loan].place.root != root && operand < arguments.length {
          let mut target = usize.ZERO
          while target < carried.length {
            let destination = carried[target]
            let targetLoan = &List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)[destination.loan]
            if targetLoan.exclusive && targetLoan.place.root == root {
              let count = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<usize>(&recorded, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> usize {
                let entries = List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)
                if destination.operand >= entries.length { return usize.ZERO }
                return List<KeptSlot>.length(&entries[destination.operand].slots)
              })
              let mut slot = usize.ZERO
              while slot < count {
                if run keptIn(&recorded, operand, &List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)[loan], carried[index], &walker.*, owner,
                  List<RetentionEdge>.asSlice(&walker.requirements), List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), destination, slot) {
                  let mut carry = carried[index]
                  carry.field = run destinationField(&recorded, &mut walker.*, destination, slot)
                  carry.direct = false
                  run List<Carry>.append(&mut received, carry)
                }
                slot = slot + usize.ONE
              }
            }
            target = target + usize.ONE
          }
        }
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    if List<Carry>.length(&received) > usize.ZERO {
      if Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&ty, referenceType) {
        if holds(&walker.*, root) {
          leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
          return point
        }
      } else {
        // The new definition replaces the holder's earlier ones, so it holds what they did, once
        // per retained position: re-holding earlier holdings would double them at each call.
        let used = run useHolder(&mut walker.*, root, usize.MAX, span, point)
        let mut carrying = List<Carry>.make()
        run appendCarried(&mut carrying, List<Carry>.asSlice(&used.carried))
        run appendCarried(&mut carrying, List<Carry>.asSlice(&received))
        run hold(&mut walker.*, root, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carrying), used.at, true)
        point = used.at
      }
    }
    holder = holder + usize.ONE
  }
  return point
}

// Whether this particular loan can occupy a parameter slot that can store into the destination's
// regions. KeptSlot.kept records the destination regions reached under the declared bounds, not
// just the source's region. A projected value may carry a loan typed at an earlier region: compare
// the slot's referent and access, not that original region's spelling. Loans of a receiver's storage
// cannot occupy its stored reference slots merely because both travel through the same operand.
effect fn keptIn(recorded: &Shared<List<KeptRegions>>, operand: usize, loan: &Loan, carry: Carry, walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId,
  edges: &[RetentionEdge], named: &[Shared<Lifetime>], destination: Carry, target: usize) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if excludedTransferRead(walker, carry) { return false }
  let mut source = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value} = &loan.borrowed {
    run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut source, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&value))
  } else {
    run appendAllAtoms(&mut source, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions))
  }
  // A prior store or coercion can shorten the loan into this source position. Follow only the
  // finite requirements in their source-to-extent direction; they retain a loan, never prove it.
  let mut reached = List<usize>.make()
  let origins = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&source)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < origins.length {
    let ordinal = retentionOrdinal(&origins[at], owner)
    if ordinal != usize.MAX && !retentionListed(List<usize>.asSlice(&reached), ordinal) {
      run List<usize>.append(&mut reached, ordinal)
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&reached) {
    let origin = List<usize>.asSlice(&reached)[at]
    let mut edge = usize.ZERO
    while edge < edges.length {
      if edges[edge].source == origin && !retentionListed(List<usize>.asSlice(&reached), edges[edge].extent) {
        run List<usize>.append(&mut reached, edges[edge].extent)
      }
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<bool>(recorded, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> bool {
    let entries = List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)
    if operand >= entries.length { return false }
    let slots = List<KeptSlot>.asSlice(&entries[operand].slots)
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < slots.length {
      let mut fits = true
      if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value: referent} = &loan.referent {
        fits = Type.mayHoldLoan(slots[at].view, &slots[at].referent, slots[at].exclusive, &referent, loan.exclusive)
      }
      let sources = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&slots[at].source)
      let mut enters = sharesAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&source), sources)
      let mut each = usize.ZERO
      while !enters && each < sources.length {
        let ordinal = retentionOrdinal(&sources[each], owner)
        enters = ordinal != usize.MAX && retentionListed(List<usize>.asSlice(&reached), ordinal)
        each = each + usize.ONE
      }
      if carry.direct && carry.field != usize.MAX {
        let paths = List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths)
        let matched = transferSlotPath(List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[carry.field]), List<KeptStep>.asSlice(&slots[at].path), slots[at].view)
        if matched != SlotPath.Unknown { enters = matched == SlotPath.Same }
      }
      if fits && enters && sharesAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&slots[at].kept), named)
        && destinationKeeps(entries, &slots[at], walker, destination, target, named) { return true }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    return false
  })
}

// Inferred regions can coincide even when the holder cannot contain this source value. Match
// the eligible source to a slot reached through a loan of this particular destination, retaining
// both its directed region eligibility and its referent/access contract. Opaque source storage
// can contain loans its outer type does not describe, so only known views constrain the contents.
fn destinationKeeps(entries: &[KeptRegions], source: &KeptSlot, walker: &Walker, destination: Carry, targetIndex: usize,
  named: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool {
  let slots = List<KeptSlot>.asSlice(&entries[destination.operand].slots)
  let target = &slots[targetIndex]
  return destinationSlot(walker, destination, target)
    && sharesAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&target.source), named)
    && sharesAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&source.kept), List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&target.source))
    && (!source.view || Type.mayHoldLoan(target.view, &target.referent, target.exclusive, &source.referent, source.exclusive))
}

// Translate the contract slot through the actual exclusive loan. Keep the known storage prefix
// before opaque or indirect contents: replacing that prefix drops all of those contents, while a
// narrower write cannot claim to reset them. Never infer which eligible slot the callee writes.
effect fn destinationField(recorded: &Shared<List<KeptRegions>>, walker: &mut Walker, destination: Carry, slot: usize) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if !destination.direct || destination.field == usize.MAX { return usize.MAX }
  let lent = run copyPath(&walker.*, destination.field)
  let prefix = List<Step>.asSlice(&lent)
  if !exactPath(prefix) { return usize.MAX }
  let loan = &List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)[destination.loan]
  if !exactPath(List<Step>.asSlice(&loan.place.steps)) { return usize.MAX }
  let mut path = run copySteps(List<Step>.asSlice(&loan.place.steps))
  let count = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<usize>(recorded, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> usize {
    return List<KeptStep>.length(&List<KeptSlot>.asSlice(&List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)[destination.operand].slots)[slot].path)
  })
  let mut at = prefix.length
  if at >= count { return usize.MAX }
  let boundary = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<KeptStep>(recorded, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> KeptStep {
    return List<KeptStep>.asSlice(&List<KeptSlot>.asSlice(&List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)[destination.operand].slots)[slot].path)[at]
  })
  if boundary.kind != KeptStepKind.Referent { return usize.MAX }
  at = at + usize.ONE
  while at < count {
    let step = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<KeptStep>(recorded, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> KeptStep {
      return List<KeptStep>.asSlice(&List<KeptSlot>.asSlice(&List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)[destination.operand].slots)[slot].path)[at]
    })
    if step.kind != KeptStepKind.Field { break }
    run List<Step>.append(&mut path, fieldStep(step.index))
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return run internPath(&mut walker.*, move path)
}

// A lent reference is not itself writable holder contents. Known aggregate paths locate that
// reference within the operand; contents begin at its Referent step. Opaque ancestors and unknown
// paths can reach storage we cannot place, so they remain possible destinations.
fn destinationSlot(walker: &Walker, carry: Carry, slot: &KeptSlot) -> bool {
  let target = List<KeptStep>.asSlice(&slot.path)
  if !carry.direct || carry.field == usize.MAX { return !slot.view || target.length != usize.ZERO }
  let paths = List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths)
  let lent = List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[carry.field])
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < lent.length {
    if at >= target.length { return !slot.view }
    if target[at].kind != KeptStepKind.Field || lent[at].kind == StepKind.Referent
      || lent[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || lent[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement { return true }
    if lent[at].kind != StepKind.Field || target[at].index != lent[at].ordinal { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if at == target.length { return !slot.view }
  return target[at].kind == KeptStepKind.Referent || target[at].kind == KeptStepKind.Unknown
}

// A holder read can keep sibling loans live without passing their references as the value read.
// Restrict only the transfer: the ordinary holder liveness and field-release policy are unchanged.
fn excludedTransferRead(walker: &Walker, carry: Carry) -> bool {
  if carry.definition == usize.MAX || carry.read == usize.MAX { return false }
  let definitions = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let field = definitions[carry.definition].field
  let read = points[carry.read].read
  if field == usize.MAX || read == usize.MAX { return false }
  let paths = List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths)
  let held = List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[field])
  let used = List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[read])
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < held.length && at < used.length {
    if held[at].kind == StepKind.Referent || used[at].kind == StepKind.Referent
      || held[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || used[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement
      || held[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement || used[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement { return false }
    if held[at].kind == used[at].kind && held[at].ordinal != used[at].ordinal { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

enum SlotPath { Unknown, Same, Different }

// A direct carried reference occupies exactly this source sub-place, even if parameter coercion
// shortened its region. Opaque slots may contain it below their prefix. Reference and unknown
// element/union boundaries leave region correspondence to decide: they cannot prove field identity.
fn transferSlotPath(loan: &[Step], slot: &[KeptStep], view: bool) -> SlotPath {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < slot.length {
    if slot[at].kind == KeptStepKind.Unknown || slot[at].kind == KeptStepKind.Referent
      || slot[at].kind == KeptStepKind.Element { return SlotPath.Unknown }
    if at >= loan.length { return SlotPath.Different }
    if loan[at].kind == StepKind.Referent || loan[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement
      || loan[at].kind == StepKind.RepeatedElement { return SlotPath.Unknown }
    if loan[at].kind != StepKind.Field || loan[at].ordinal != slot[at].index { return SlotPath.Different }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if view && loan.length != slot.length { return SlotPath.Different }
  return SlotPath.Same
}

// An invoked callable whose body may store a loan it carries stores it wherever it can write
// (CAPTURE-002, ANON-OWN-001): into a holder it reaches through an exclusive capture or a `&mut`
// argument. Neither its signature nor typing records which, so each body-local holder the
// invocation lends exclusively, whose type can retain a region, retains every such loan from the
// invocation on, as a field store into it would. A holder that is a reference holding body loans may
// reach body storage the walk cannot place, so such a store leaves the body unchecked; a reference
// this body was passed reaches caller storage, which the region proof answers for only where it sees
// the store, so a loan of body storage that may go there keeps the body from being Checked.
effect fn storeThroughExclusive(locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, carried: &[Carry], stored: &[Carry],
  span: Location, at: usize) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  if stored.length == usize.ZERO || walker.outside || at == usize.MAX { return at }
  let mut holders = List<usize>.make()
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  while index < carried.length {
    let lent = loans[carried[index].loan].place.root
    if loans[carried[index].loan].exclusive && lent < walker.localCount && !listsIndex(List<usize>.asSlice(&holders), lent) {
      run List<usize>.append(&mut holders, lent)
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut point = at
  let roots = List<usize>.asSlice(&holders)
  let mut holder = usize.ZERO
  while holder < roots.length {
    let root = roots[holder]
    let ty = localType(locals, root)
    let mut kept = List<Carry>.make()
    if run retains(&ty, owner) {
      index = usize.ZERO
      while index < stored.length {
        let loan = stored[index].loan
        if listsIndex(List<usize>.asSlice(&walker.storable), loan) && List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)[loan].place.root != root {
          let mut carry = stored[index]
          carry.field = usize.MAX
          carry.direct = false
          run List<Carry>.append(&mut kept, carry)
        }
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    if List<Carry>.length(&kept) > usize.ZERO {
      if Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&ty, referenceType) {
        if holds(&walker.*, root) {
          leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
          return point
        }
      } else {
        let used = run useHolder(&mut walker.*, root, usize.MAX, span, point)
        let mut carrying = move used.carried
        run appendCarried(&mut carrying, List<Carry>.asSlice(&kept))
        run hold(&mut walker.*, root, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carrying), used.at, false)
        point = used.at
      }
    }
    holder = holder + usize.ONE
  }
  return point
}

// Constructs a callable or section from its captured operands, in order (CAPTURE-001). A borrowed capture's
// loan begins here and travels with the callable value, so it stays live while the callable can
// still be invoked (CALLABLE-003); a moved capture leaves its place here (CAPTURE-002). A captured
// exclusive descriptor is read into its field and its referent reborrowed with the access the body
// needs through it. A section copies or takes its base callable's environment, so it carries the
// loans that callee holds.
effect fn construct(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, values: &[NodeId],
  referents: &[ReferentCapture], staged: bool, holdable: &[CaptureHold], body: BorrowStatus, result: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  // A body the borrow check did not close may store a loan it carries anywhere it can write.
  let stores = body != BorrowStatus.Checked
  let hasBase = match &nodes[result.index].kind {
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.StagedCallable {..}, ..} => true
    _ => false
  }
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  // The value each carried loan entered through, in step with `carried`.
  let mut sources = List<usize>.make()
  let mut current = at
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < values.length {
    let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, values[index], current)
    run appendCarried(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried))
    current = flow.at
    let mut captured = usize.ZERO
    while captured < referents.length {
      if referents[captured].field == index {
        let reborrow = run reborrowReferent(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, values[index], referents[captured].access == Access.Mutable, current)
        run appendCarried(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&reborrow.carried))
        current = reborrow.at
      }
      captured = captured + usize.ONE
    }
    while List<usize>.length(&sources) < List<Carry>.length(&carried) { run List<usize>.append(&mut sources, index) }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  // The loans travel with the callable whatever regions its type names: holding them longer is
  // conservative, and the region slice proves the environment's own regions. A loan the callable can
  // store, through a capture or an argument that names a universal region where it can store, must
  // outlive the body (R3 amendment 4).
  // A capture or contract parameter naming a type parameter can store through an instantiation or
  // conformance this walk cannot see. The body's callers choose that type, so it names no body
  // region: a loan typed only at body regions can be stored through it only where the callable's
  // own body admits a relation from a body region to one the type names, which a body the borrow
  // check closed never does. Such a loan of a closed body stays with the callable as any other
  // capture's loan does, held by what an invocation lends exclusively (see `storeThroughExclusive`);
  // one a body that is not Checked carries (`stores`), or one with no typed region, leaves the
  // body unchecked. A loan typed at a universal region may reach caller storage through it, so it
  // escapes. The walk still
  // continues: a definite conflict among exact loans rejects whatever the callable stores. A staged
  // callable's callee stores only through the contract its stage exposes.
  // Construction really holds each capture, but has not executed a destination write.
  // A closed selected contract can prove a capture non-storing; every other capture keeps
  // the existing conservative policy. The classification never creates caller retention.
  let closed = match &nodes[result.index].kind {
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.StagedCallable {retention, ..}, ..} => retention.closed
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Aggregate {section: Option<SectionRetention>.Some {value}, ..}, ..} => value.closed
    _ => false
  }
  let mut sinks = List<OperandSink>.make()
  if staged && closed { sinks = run operandSinks(nodes, result, values, owner) }
  let entries = List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&sinks)
  let captured = List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried)
  let entered = List<usize>.asSlice(&sources)
  let mut supplied = List<Carry>.make()
  index = usize.ZERO
  while index < captured.length {
    let mut carry = captured[index]
    carry.operand = entered[index]
    run List<Carry>.append(&mut supplied, carry)
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let classification = run retainedSinks(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths),
    owner, List<Carry>.asSlice(&supplied), entries, usize.MAX)
  let decisions = List<CallSink>.asSlice(&classification.sinks)
  let mut nonstoring = List<bool>.make()
  index = usize.ZERO
  while index < captured.length {
    let operand = entered[index]
    run List<bool>.append(&mut nonstoring, closed && !(hasBase && operand == usize.ZERO)
      && operand < entries.length && !entries[operand].undescribed
      && List<SlotSink>.length(&entries[operand].slots) != usize.ZERO && decisions[index] == CallSink.Local)
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut stored = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut opaque = false
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, result) {
    run Type.callableStoredRegions(&value, &mut stored)
    opaque = run Type.contractNamesTypeParameter(&value)
  }
  index = usize.ZERO
  while index < values.length {
    run storedRegionsOf(nodes, values[index], &mut stored)
    if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, values[index]) {
      if !(hasBase && index == usize.ZERO) && run Type.namesTypeParameter(&value) { opaque = true }
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  if opaque {
    let captured = List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried)
    let mut held = usize.ZERO
    while held < captured.length {
      let mut all = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
      if universalRegions(&all[captured[held].loan].regions, owner) {
        all[captured[held].loan].escapes = true
      } else if List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(&all[captured[held].loan].regions) == usize.ZERO && !all[captured[held].loan].local {
        walker.storing = true
      }
      held = held + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  if universalRegions(&stored, owner) {
    // Whether the callable's body stores a capture is not visible here: a loan typed at a universal
    // region escapes. A capture whose type no position the callable can write admits is never
    // stored, so the loans it carries stay in the environment. A loan of storage the body owns
    // (`ownedStorageLoan`), typed only at body regions (`typedLocally`), stays with a callable whose
    // body the borrow check closed and whose types name no type parameter: that storage ends within
    // the body, so no region proof shows its region outlives a universal one, and a slot whose region
    // names only universal regions never admits it. A reborrow through a reference is not such a
    // loan: its region may be proved to outlive the reference's. Any other loan leaves the body
    // unchecked: an unclosed body (`stores`) may store it anywhere it can write, and an
    // instantiation (`opaque`) may hold it where no region shows.
    let captured = List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried)
    let entered = List<usize>.asSlice(&sources)
    let mut unchecked = false
    let mut held = usize.ZERO
    while held < captured.length {
      // Closing the selected inference can still leave a caller type parameter opaque.
      // Its possible instantiations retain the conservative capture policy below.
      if !opaque && List<bool>.asSlice(&nonstoring)[held] { held = held + usize.ONE  continue }
      let mut all = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
      let mut hold = CaptureHold.Any
      if held < entered.length && entered[held] < holdable.length { hold = holdable[entered[held]] }
      if universalRegions(&all[captured[held].loan].regions, owner) {
        if hold != CaptureHold.Never { all[captured[held].loan].escapes = true }
      } else if hold == CaptureHold.Any && (stores || opaque || !typedLocally(&all[captured[held].loan].regions, owner)
        || !ownedStorageLoan(&all[captured[held].loan])) {
        unchecked = true
      }
      held = held + usize.ONE
    }
    // The walk keeps going: a definite conflict among exact loans, including one a closure it carries
    // stores where an exclusive capture reaches, still rejects, and the body is never Checked.
    if unchecked { walker.storing = true }
  }
  // A loan that entered through a capture no position the callable can write admits is never
  // stored by its body either.
  if stores {
    let captured = List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried)
    let entered = List<usize>.asSlice(&sources)
    index = usize.ZERO
    while index < captured.length {
      let stays = index < entered.length && entered[index] < holdable.length && holdable[entered[index]] == CaptureHold.Never
      if !stays && !listsIndex(List<usize>.asSlice(&walker.storable), captured[index].loan) {
        run List<usize>.append(&mut walker.storable, captured[index].loan)
      }
      index = index + usize.ONE
    }
    // Nothing reports an anonymous body on its own: what it does with its captures, its own locals
    // or any service its requirement row names is proved only by its own check. This body therefore
    // claims no more than the bodies it constructs, for the same reason, and the walk goes on.
    if walker.inherited == BorrowStatus.Checked { walker.inherited = body }
  }
  let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, current)
  return Flow {at: point, carried: move carried}
}

// Appends the regions a captured value can store into, when typing recorded its type. A captured
// callable stores only through what its contract's parameters reach.
effect fn storedRegionsOf(nodes: &[Node], node: NodeId, stored: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, node) { run Type.callableStoredRegions(&value, &mut stored.*) }
  return ()
}

// An invocation of a callable value (CALLABLE-002). A pipeline's input is evaluated before the
// callee. Reading the callee keeps the loans its environment holds live for the whole call
// (CALLABLE-003). A `mut fn` callee is accessed exclusively for the call; a `once fn` callee is
// already a typed move of its place, so a second invocation uses a moved place.
effect fn invoke(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, callee: NodeId, arguments: &[NodeId],
  pipeline: bool, exclusive: bool, result: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  let mut current = at
  let mut first = usize.ZERO
  if pipeline && arguments.length > usize.ZERO {
    let input = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, arguments[0], current)
    run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&input.carried), usize.ZERO)
    current = input.at
    first = usize.ONE
  }
  let target = run calleeAccess(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, exclusive, current)
  run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&target.carried), arguments.length)
  current = target.at
  let mut index = first
  while index < arguments.length {
    let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, arguments[index], current)
    run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), index)
    current = flow.at
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let untyped = List<NodeId>.make()
  let sinks = run operandSinks(nodes, result, arguments, owner)
  let unplaced = List<List<Step>>.make()
  let invoked = run finish(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, result, current, &carried, false, Forwarding.None, List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&unplaced), List<NodeId>.asSlice(&untyped), List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&sinks))
  let transferred = run storeIntoLent(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, result, arguments, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried),
    nodes[result.index].origin.location, invoked.at)
  // The callable stores what its environment holds, not the loan this invocation takes of it.
  let callee = run pathOf(nodes, callee)
  let mut environment = List<Carry>.make()
  let lent = List<Carry>.asSlice(&target.carried)
  index = usize.ZERO
  while index < lent.length {
    if List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)[lent[index].loan].place.root != callee.root || callee.root == usize.MAX {
      run List<Carry>.append(&mut environment, lent[index])
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let stored = run storeThroughExclusive(locals, owner, &mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried), List<Carry>.asSlice(&environment),
    nodes[result.index].origin.location, transferred)
  return Flow {at: stored, carried: move invoked.carried}
}

// Constructs the Effect an `effect fn` value's invocation promises without calling it (EFF-001). The
// Effect takes its callee as the callee's mode grants: it owns a `once fn` callee, already a typed
// move, and holds a shared or exclusive loan of any other callee place, which carries the callee's
// own loans. Its operands enter the environment by CAPTURE-002. Every loan travels with the Effect
// value, so it stays live until the Effect's last run or drop (EFFECT-OWN-001, EFFECT-OWN-002).
effect fn defer(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, callee: NodeId, arguments: &[NodeId],
  pipeline: bool, mode: CallableMode, result: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  let mut current = at
  let mut first = usize.ZERO
  let sinks = run operandSinks(nodes, result, arguments, owner)
  let kept = List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&sinks)
  if pipeline && arguments.length > usize.ZERO {
    let input = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, arguments[0], current)
    run keepCarried(&mut walker.*, owner, List<Carry>.asSlice(&input.carried), kept, usize.ZERO, input.at)
    run appendCarried(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&input.carried))
    current = input.at
    first = usize.ONE
  }
  let target = run capturedCallee(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, mode, current)
  run appendCarried(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&target.carried))
  current = target.at
  let mut index = first
  while index < arguments.length {
    let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, arguments[index], current)
    run keepCarried(&mut walker.*, owner, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), kept, index, flow.at)
    run appendCarried(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried))
    current = flow.at
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, current)
  return Flow {at: point, carried: move carried}
}

// The callee a constructed Effect retains: a borrow of a shared or `mut fn` callee place, otherwise
// the callee's value.
effect fn capturedCallee(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, callee: NodeId, mode: CallableMode, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  if mode == CallableMode.Once {
    return run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, at)
  }
  let path = run pathOf(nodes, callee)
  if path.root == usize.MAX {
    return run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, at)
  }
  let span = nodes[callee.index].origin.location
  return run borrow(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, mode == CallableMode.Mutable, span, usize.MAX, at)
}

// The callee of an invocation. A shared or consuming callee is an ordinary read or move of its
// value. A `mut fn` callee written as a place is borrowed exclusively for the call, which reads its
// held loans, so another live loan of that place conflicts with the invocation.
effect fn calleeAccess(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, callee: NodeId, exclusive: bool, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  if !exclusive {
    return run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, at)
  }
  let path = run pathOf(nodes, callee)
  if path.root == usize.MAX {
    return run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, at)
  }
  let span = nodes[callee.index].origin.location
  return run borrow(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, true, span, usize.MAX, at)
}

fn isBorrow(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> bool {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form, ..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
    if let Expression.Borrow {..} = &form {
      return true
    }
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a node constructs a callable value from its captures: a closure or an `effect` block.
fn isCallable(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> bool {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form, ..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
    if let Expression.Callable {..} = &form {
      return true
    }
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a type is an Effect type.
fn effectType(ty: &Type) -> bool {
  return match &ty.* {
    Type.Effect {..} => true
    Type.EffectComposite {..} => true
    Type.EffectJoin {..} => true
    _ => false
  }
}

// Whether a callable value of this type is an Effect: an `effect` block's value, or an Effect an
// `effect fn` call constructs.
fn effectBlock(ty: &Type) -> bool {
  return match &ty.* {
    Type.CallableValue {contract, ..} => Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&contract, effectType)
    _ => false
  }
}

// Whether a type is a reference, whose referent's storage another place owns.
fn referenceType(ty: &Type) -> bool {
  return match &ty.* {
    Type.Reference {..} => true
    _ => false
  }
}

// Whether a local of this type is a callable value in any of its typed forms.
fn callableValue(ty: &Type) -> bool {
  return match &ty.* {
    Type.Callable {..} => true
    Type.CallableValue {..} => true
    Type.CallableSchema {..} => true
    Type.CallableStage {..} => true
    Type.CallableResult {..} => true
    Type.CallableOrigin {..} => true
    Type.CallableWitnessResult {..} => true
    Type.CallableView {..} => true
    _ => false
  }
}

fn localType(locals: &[Local], local: usize) -> Shared<Type> {
  return Shared<Type>.clone(&locals[local].ty)
}

// The node shape `visit` dispatches on, read without holding a borrow of the node across calls.
union Shape {
  Leaf,
  Outside {reason: BorrowStatus},
  ReadPlace,
  Borrow {access: Access, value: NodeId},
  Move {value: NodeId, consumed: bool},
  // `places` are the field or element indexes of an aggregate's operands, in order; usize.MAX
  // denotes all repeated elements. Empty for any other value built from operands.
  Operands {values: List<NodeId>, places: List<usize>, member: usize},
  // `&&` or `||`: the right operand runs on one path, and its temporaries end with it.
  ShortCircuit {left: NodeId, right: NodeId},
  PassThrough {value: NodeId},
  // `signature` marks a call to a declaration or interface operation, whose written signature
  // types its arguments and result.
  Call {arguments: List<NodeId>, receiver: usize, exact: bool, signature: bool},
  Invoke {callee: NodeId, arguments: List<NodeId>, pipeline: bool, exclusive: bool},
  // `referents` name their operands by position.
  // `holdable` says, per value, where the callable could store a loan it carries; empty when typing
  // recorded nothing, which lets every value be stored anywhere. `body` is the status of the callable's
  // own anonymous body, `Checked` for one with none.
  Construct {values: List<NodeId>, referents: List<ReferentCapture>, staged: bool, holdable: List<CaptureHold>, body: BorrowStatus},
  Defer {callee: NodeId, arguments: List<NodeId>, pipeline: bool, mode: CallableMode},
  Binding {local: usize, initializer: NodeId, mutable: bool},
  Assignment {local: usize, value: NodeId},
  PlaceAssignment {target: NodeId, value: NodeId},
  Displace {target: NodeId, value: NodeId},
  Exit {value: Option<NodeId>},
  Drop {value: NodeId, consumed: bool},
  Branch {condition: NodeId, thenBranch: NodeId, elseBranch: Option<NodeId>},
  While {condition: NodeId, body: NodeId},
  Break,
  Continue,
  // A statement that failed to check in a rejected body. No edge leaves it, so no move or loan
  // crosses a statement whose effects are unknown. When it surely let a path continue, the
  // statement after it resumes from the body's entry and the statements after it are still
  // checked among themselves; otherwise they stay unreached, as after a `return`.
  Recovered {resumes: bool},
  Block {statements: List<NodeId>},
  Match {subject: NodeId, access: Scrutinee, arms: List<ArmShape>, syntax: MatchSyntax},
}

// How a match reaches its subject, read from `SubjectAccess` without holding the node.
enum Scrutinee {
  // A bare match copies the subject; `match move` of a value with no place consumes it.
  Value,
  // `match move` of a place moves it.
  Moved,
  // `match &` reads the subject place.
  Shared,
  // `match &mut` updates it.
  Exclusive,
  // `match place` inspects its tag.
  Place,
}

struct ArmShape {
  guard: Option<NodeId>
  result: NodeId
  // Whether the arm's pattern declares a binding.
  binds: bool
}

fn scrutineeOf(access: &SubjectAccess) -> Scrutinee {
  return match &access.* {
    SubjectAccess.Copy => Scrutinee.Value
    SubjectAccess.Consume {consumed} => {
      if hasPlace(&consumed) {
        return Scrutinee.Moved
      }
      return Scrutinee.Value
    }
    SubjectAccess.Place {access: binding} => {
      if binding == BindingAccess.Shared {
        return Scrutinee.Shared
      }
      if binding == BindingAccess.Exclusive {
        return Scrutinee.Exclusive
      }
      return Scrutinee.Place
    }
  }
}

effect fn armShapes(arms: &[MatchArm]) -> List<ArmShape> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut shapes = List<ArmShape>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < arms.length {
    run List<ArmShape>.append(&mut shapes, ArmShape {guard: copyNode(&arms[at].guard), result: arms[at].result,
      binds: List<NodeId>.length(&arms[at].bindings) > usize.ZERO})
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move shapes
}

effect fn shapeOf(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> Shape ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  return match &nodes[id.index].kind {
    NodeKind.Expression {form, ty} => {
      // A named function's section is an aggregate of its captured operands (CALLABLE-001).
      if let Expression.Aggregate {fields, section, ..} = &form {
        if Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&ty, callableValue) {
          return Shape.Construct {values: run fieldValues(List<AggregateField>.asSlice(&fields)), referents: List<ReferentCapture>.make(), holdable: List<CaptureHold>.make(),
            staged: match &section { Option<SectionRetention>.Some {..} => true _ => false }, body: BorrowStatus.Checked}
        }
      }
      // An immediate run is exactly the one call it executes (EFF-003): the Effect that call
      // constructs is a temporary only this run consumes, so its operands are the call's arguments
      // and the run node is the call's result (EFFECT-OWN-001, BORROW-004).
      if let Expression.Run {value, access} = &form {
        if access == RunAccess.Immediate {
          if let NodeKind.Expression {form: operand, ..} = &nodes[value.index].kind {
            // Running an `effect fn` value's invocation in place invokes that value (CALLABLE-002).
            if let Expression.CallableCall {callee, mode, arguments, pipeline, ..} = &operand {
              return Shape.Invoke {callee: callee, arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), pipeline: pipeline,
                exclusive: mode == CallableMode.Mutable}
            }
            // The run's result is the call's success value, which stores none of its operands
            // beyond what its own type retains.
            if let Expression.DirectCall {arguments, receiverPass, ..} = &operand {
              return Shape.Call {arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), receiver: receiverOf(&receiverPass), exact: false,
                signature: true}
            }
            if let Expression.InterfaceCall {arguments, receiverPass, ..} = &operand {
              return Shape.Call {arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), receiver: receiverOf(&receiverPass), exact: false,
                signature: true}
            }
            // A drive retains its operands in an opaque Effect until activation. Only this
            // immediate run can consume all operand/capture loans at the S2 call point.
            if let Expression.StorageCall {operation, arguments, ..} = &operand {
              if operation == StorageOperation.ExecutionDrive {
                return Shape.Call {arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), receiver: usize.ZERO, exact: false,
                  signature: false}
              }
            }
            return run expressionShape(&operand)
          }
        }
      }
      return run expressionShape(&form)
    }
    NodeKind.LocalBinding {local, initializer} => Shape.Binding {local: local.index, initializer: initializer, mutable: false}
    NodeKind.MutableBinding {local, initializer} => Shape.Binding {local: local.index, initializer: initializer, mutable: true}
    NodeKind.Assignment {local, value} => Shape.Assignment {local: local.index, value: value}
    NodeKind.PlaceAssignment {target, value} => Shape.PlaceAssignment {target: target, value: value}
    NodeKind.Return {value} => Shape.Exit {value: copyNode(&value)}
    NodeKind.Fail {value} => Shape.Exit {value: Option<NodeId>.some(value)}
    NodeKind.Drop {value, consumed} => Shape.Drop {value: value, consumed: hasPlace(&consumed)}
    NodeKind.Branch {condition, thenBranch, elseBranch, ..} => Shape.Branch {condition: condition, thenBranch: thenBranch, elseBranch: copyNode(&elseBranch)}
    NodeKind.While {condition, body} => Shape.While {condition: condition, body: body}
    NodeKind.Break => Shape.Break
    NodeKind.Continue => Shape.Continue
    NodeKind.Recovered {resumes} => Shape.Recovered {resumes: resumes}
    NodeKind.Block {statements, ..} => Shape.Block {statements: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&statements))}
  }
}

fn copyNode(value: &Option<NodeId>) -> Option<NodeId> {
  if let Option<NodeId>.Some {value: node} = &value.* {
    return Option<NodeId>.some(node)
  }
  return Option<NodeId>.none()
}

// The receiver pass of a call: 0 none, 1 shared, 2 mutable, 3 taking.
fn receiverOf(value: &Option<ReceiverPass>) -> usize {
  if let Option<ReceiverPass>.Some {value: pass} = &value.* {
    if pass == ReceiverPass.Shared {
      return usize.ONE
    }
    if pass == ReceiverPass.Mutable {
      return 2
    }
    return 3
  }
  return usize.ZERO
}

fn hasPlace(consumed: &Option<ConsumedPlace>) -> bool {
  return match &consumed.* {
    Option<ConsumedPlace>.Some {..} => true
    Option<ConsumedPlace>.None => false
  }
}

effect fn expressionShape(form: &Expression) -> Shape ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  return match &form.* {
    Expression.Local {..} => Shape.ReadPlace
    Expression.Field {..} => Shape.ReadPlace
    Expression.Index {..} => Shape.ReadPlace
    Expression.Dereference {..} => Shape.ReadPlace
    Expression.Borrow {access, value} => Shape.Borrow {access: access, value: value}
    Expression.Move {value, consumed} => Shape.Move {value: value, consumed: hasPlace(&consumed)}
    Expression.PointerWeaken {value} => Shape.PassThrough {value: value}
    Expression.ArraySlice {value, ..} => Shape.PassThrough {value: value}
    Expression.SliceLength {value} => Shape.Operands {values: run single(value), places: List<usize>.make(), member: usize.MAX}
    Expression.ArrayLength {value, ..} => Shape.Operands {values: run single(value), places: List<usize>.make(), member: usize.MAX}
    Expression.ArrayRepeat {value, count} => {
      if count == usize.ZERO { return Shape.Drop {value: value, consumed: false} }
      let mut places = List<usize>.make()
      let mut element = usize.MAX
      if count == usize.ONE { element = usize.ZERO }
      run List<usize>.append(&mut places, element)
      return Shape.Operands {values: run single(value), places: move places, member: usize.MAX}
    }
    Expression.EnumValue {value} => Shape.Operands {values: run single(value), places: List<usize>.make(), member: usize.MAX}
    Expression.UnionInject {value, ..} => Shape.Operands {values: run single(value), places: List<usize>.make(), member: usize.MAX}
    Expression.UnionWiden {value} => Shape.Operands {values: run single(value), places: List<usize>.make(), member: usize.MAX}
    Expression.ConcretePrefix {operand, ..} => Shape.Operands {values: run single(operand), places: List<usize>.make(), member: usize.MAX}
    Expression.CompileError {message} => Shape.Operands {values: run single(message), places: List<usize>.make(), member: usize.MAX}
    Expression.ConcreteInfix {operator, left, right} => {
      if operator == InfixOperator.And || operator == InfixOperator.Or {
        return Shape.ShortCircuit {left: left, right: right}
      }
      let mut values = run single(left)
      run List<NodeId>.append(&mut values, right)
      return Shape.Operands {values: move values, places: List<usize>.make(), member: usize.MAX}
    }
    Expression.Aggregate {fields, ..} => Shape.Operands {
      values: run fieldValues(List<AggregateField>.asSlice(&fields)), places: run fieldIndexes(List<AggregateField>.asSlice(&fields)), member: usize.MAX,
    }
    Expression.VariantConstruct {tag, fields} => Shape.Operands {
      values: run fieldValues(List<AggregateField>.asSlice(&fields)), places: run fieldIndexes(List<AggregateField>.asSlice(&fields)), member: tag,
    }
    // An `effect fn` call's Effect stores exactly its written arguments (EFFECT-OWN-001).
    Expression.DirectCall {arguments, receiverPass, constructs, ..} => Shape.Call {
      arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), receiver: receiverOf(&receiverPass), exact: constructs, signature: true,
    }
    Expression.InterfaceCall {arguments, receiverPass, isEffect, ..} => Shape.Call {
      arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), receiver: receiverOf(&receiverPass), exact: isEffect, signature: true,
    }
    Expression.ForeignCall {arguments, ..} => Shape.Call {
      arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), receiver: usize.ZERO, exact: false, signature: false,
    }
    Expression.IntrinsicCall {arguments, ..} => Shape.Call {
      arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), receiver: usize.ZERO, exact: false, signature: false,
    }
    Expression.Integer {..} => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.Float {..} => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.Text {..} => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.Boolean {..} => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.Unit => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.Embedded {..} => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.EnumMember {..} => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.Constant {..} => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.ForeignStatic {..} => Shape.Leaf
    Expression.ForeignAddress {..} => Shape.Leaf
    // An anonymous body that stores one captured loan where another capture reaches needs a
    // relation between two body regions, which no premise of its own proves, so a body the borrow
    // check closed stores none (ANON-OWN-001).
    Expression.Callable {fields, referents, holdable, body} => Shape.Construct {
      values: run fieldValues(List<AggregateField>.asSlice(&fields)),
      referents: run referentOperands(List<AggregateField>.asSlice(&fields), List<ReferentCapture>.asSlice(&referents)), staged: false,
      holdable: run fieldHoldable(List<AggregateField>.asSlice(&fields), List<CaptureHold>.asSlice(&holdable)),
      body: Shared<TypedBody>.with<BorrowStatus>(&body, TypedBody.borrowStatus),
    }
    Expression.StagedCallable {callee, arguments, ..} => {
      let mut values = run single(callee)
      let supplied = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)
      let mut at = usize.ZERO
      while at < supplied.length {
        run List<NodeId>.append(&mut values, supplied[at])
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
      return Shape.Construct {values: move values, referents: List<ReferentCapture>.make(), staged: true, holdable: List<CaptureHold>.make(), body: BorrowStatus.Checked}
    }
    Expression.CallableCall {callee, mode, arguments, pipeline, constructs, ..} => {
      // Invoking an `effect fn` value without running it constructs an Effect that stores its
      // operands (EFF-001).
      if constructs {
        return Shape.Defer {callee: callee, arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), pipeline: pipeline, mode: mode}
      }
      return Shape.Invoke {callee: callee, arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), pipeline: pipeline,
        exclusive: mode == CallableMode.Mutable}
    }
    // A stored Effect's run invokes the Effect value with the access its contract grants
    // (EFFECT-OWN-002): a shared Effect is read, a `mut Effect` place is borrowed exclusively, and a
    // `once Effect` operand is already a typed move. The loans its environment holds stay live
    // through the run (EFFECT-OWN-001, CALLABLE-003).
    Expression.Run {value, access} => Shape.Invoke {callee: value, arguments: List<NodeId>.make(), pipeline: false,
      exclusive: access == RunAccess.Exclusive}
    Expression.Match {subject, access, arms, syntax, ..} => Shape.Match {
      subject: subject, access: scrutineeOf(&access), arms: run armShapes(List<MatchArm>.asSlice(&arms)), syntax: syntax,
    }
    Expression.PatternBinding {..} => Shape.ReadPlace
    // A storage primitive whose contract names every region its result reaches is a call to that
    // contract; `unsafe` discharges only its memory obligations, never an aliasing one. Each result
    // that views or reaches an operand names that operand's region, so the call's retention rules
    // hold its loans.
    // `sharedWithMut` is such a call: it consumes its two callbacks, whose capture loans are live
    // through it, and the `&mut T` it lends comes from the runtime conflict check (SHARED-004), not
    // from a place this body holds. Callback result retention is checked against that invocation's
    // contract; Semantic.buildFrom judges every reached callback's suspension and notification
    // escapes with localSharedEscapes before emission (OWN0016, SHARED-003), even if this body is
    // region-closed and Checked. Notifications have the same independent gate; see
    // SemanticLoweringCases.localSharedAccessRejectsEveryReachedEscape's exact OWN0016 spans.
    // Current and relinquish have no operands or capture loans. `executionFromAllocation` consumes its
    // allocation, body, readiness state and endpoint; typing proves the last three
    // `Intrinsic.Detached` (EXEC-004), so the package retains no loan of the caller beyond what its
    // `Intrinsic.Execution<A>` result names. `slotAddress` consumes its slot, and its `*mut T` result
    // names no region, so it holds no loan: the address keeps no storage alive, and every access
    // through it is `unsafe` and proves its own validity.
    Expression.StorageCall {operation, arguments, ..} => {
      // `replace` writes its place operand and yields the value it displaces.
      if operation == StorageOperation.Replace {
        let operands = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)
        return Shape.Displace {target: operands[usize.ZERO], value: operands[usize.ONE]}
      }
      // A delayed drive's empty native environment does not prove the loans it stores; lowering
      // runs only an immediate drive, so such a body is never emitted (EXEC-002).
      if operation == StorageOperation.ExecutionDrive {
        return Shape.Outside {reason: BorrowStatus.StoredLoans}
      }
      if contractCall(operation) {
        return Shape.Call {arguments: run copyIds(List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments)), receiver: usize.ZERO, exact: false, signature: false}
      }
      // Only `replace` and a stored drive have no contract call, and both are handled above.
      return Shape.Outside {reason: BorrowStatus.StoredLoans}
    }
  }
}

// Whether a storage primitive is checked as a call to its catalog contract. The match is
// exhaustive, so a new primitive is classified before the walk accepts it.
fn contractCall(operation: StorageOperation) -> bool {
  return match operation {
    StorageOperation.RawBufferFrom => true
    StorageOperation.RawBufferSlot => true
    StorageOperation.RawBufferCount => true
    StorageOperation.RawBufferRead => true
    StorageOperation.RawBufferCopy => true
    StorageOperation.RawBufferFill => true
    StorageOperation.RawBufferView => true
    StorageOperation.RawBufferViewMut => true
    StorageOperation.SlotWrite => true
    StorageOperation.SlotTake => true
    StorageOperation.SlotDrop => true
    StorageOperation.SlotCopy => true
    StorageOperation.SlotAddress => true
    StorageOperation.SharedLayout => true
    StorageOperation.SharedFromAllocation => true
    StorageOperation.SharedClone => true
    StorageOperation.SharedWithMut => true
    StorageOperation.LayoutOf => true
    StorageOperation.SystemAllocationAcquire => true
    StorageOperation.StringUtf8Bytes => true
    StorageOperation.StringFromUtf8Unchecked => true
    StorageOperation.StringByteLength => true
    StorageOperation.Replace => false
    StorageOperation.ExecutionLayout => true
    StorageOperation.ExecutionFromAllocation => true
    StorageOperation.ExecutionDrive => false
    StorageOperation.Relinquish => true
    StorageOperation.ExecutionCurrent => true
    StorageOperation.ExecutionRefOf => true
    StorageOperation.ExecutionLoad => true
    StorageOperation.ExecutionStore => true
    StorageOperation.ExecutionNotify => true
    StorageOperation.ExecutionLive => true
  }
}


// The walk keeps lexical roots in acquisition order. Every outgoing edge replays the same
// reverse order; only the normal walk changes the stack used while constructing sibling paths.
effect fn registerRoot(walker: &mut Walker, root: usize) -> ()
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator {
  run registerTemporary(&mut walker.*, root, true)
  return ()
}

// Registers a root in the innermost scope, or in the innermost scope that is not a statement's
// when `lexical`.
effect fn registerTemporary(walker: &mut Walker, root: usize, lexical: bool) -> ()
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut at = List<Scope>.length(&walker.scopes) - usize.ONE
  while lexical && at > usize.ZERO && List<Scope>.asSlice(&walker.scopes)[at].statement {
    at = at - usize.ONE
  }
  let mut scopes = List<Scope>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.scopes)
  run List<usize>.append(&mut scopes[at].roots, root)
  return ()
}

effect fn releaseScopes(walker: &mut Walker, keep: usize, span: Location, at: usize) -> usize
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator {
  if at == usize.MAX {
    return at
  }

  // Copy identities before mutating the graph: no view into Walker stays borrowed across a
  // mutable borrow of the complete walk.
  let mut releasing = List<usize>.make()
  let mut expiring = List<bool>.make()
  let scopes = List<Scope>.asSlice(&walker.scopes)
  let mut scope = scopes.length
  while scope > keep {
    scope = scope - usize.ONE
    let ended = List<usize>.asSlice(&scopes[scope].expiring)
    let mut index = ended.length
    while index > usize.ZERO {
      index = index - usize.ONE
      run List<usize>.append(&mut releasing, ended[index])
      run List<bool>.append(&mut expiring, true)
    }
    let roots = List<usize>.asSlice(&scopes[scope].roots)
    index = roots.length
    while index > usize.ZERO {
      index = index - usize.ONE
      run List<usize>.append(&mut releasing, roots[index])
      run List<bool>.append(&mut expiring, false)
    }
  }
  let roots = List<usize>.asSlice(&releasing)
  let expires = List<bool>.asSlice(&expiring)
  let mut current = at
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < roots.length {
    let root = roots[index]
    let path = Path {
      root: root,
      through: false,
      steps: List<Step>.make(),
      indexes: List<NodeId>.make(),
      refiner: usize.MAX,
      refinedDepth: usize.ZERO,
      binders: List<usize>.make(),
    }
    if expires[index] {
      current = run access(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Expire, span, current, usize.MAX)
    } else {
      let holder = holderOf(&walker.*, root)
      if lexicalHolder(&walker.*, root) {
        // A borrowed destructuring `let` lends its subject until its bindings' scope ends.
        current = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, current)
        let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
        points[current].uses = holder
        points[current].span = span
      } else if holder < List<bool>.length(&walker.unrun) && List<bool>.asSlice(&walker.unrun)[holder] {
        // An `effect` block's value that is never run or used keeps the loans of its own captures
        // to its scope end (EFFECT-OWN-001); what it holds through a captured value follows that
        // value's own uses, and one that is used holds its captures through its last use.
        current = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, current)
        let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
        let mut loan = usize.ZERO
        while loan < loans.length {
          if loans[loan].block == holder { loans[loan].until = current }
          loan = loan + usize.ONE
        }
      }
      current = run observeCleanup(&mut walker.*, holder, root >= usize.MAX / 4, span, current)
      current = run access(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.End, span, current, usize.MAX)
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return current
}

// Whether the cleanup of `holder`'s value can observe a loan: its type runs a hook that names a
// borrowed region, or one whose regions are unknown.
fn observingCleanup(walker: &Walker, holder: usize) -> bool {
  let available = List<LoanCleanup>.asSlice(&walker.cleanup)
  if holder >= available.length { return false }
  return available[holder].unknown || List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(&available[holder].regions) > usize.ZERO
}

// Cleanup uses just the initialized definitions whose named regions the hook can observe.
// It is not a whole-holder read: a Drop in an unrelated field cannot extend every other loan. A
// hidden owner's cleanup that observes unknown regions (`hidden`) uses every loan the owner holds:
// it ends within the body, where the hook may observe any of them.
effect fn observeCleanup(walker: &mut Walker, holder: usize, hidden: bool, span: Location, at: usize) -> usize
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator {
  let available = List<LoanCleanup>.asSlice(&walker.cleanup)
  if holder >= available.length {
    return at
  }
  let repeat = outermostOpenLoop(&walker.*)
  if (available[holder].unknown || List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(&available[holder].regions) > usize.ZERO)
    && repeat != usize.MAX {
    let recorded = List<LoopCleanup>.asSlice(&walker.loopCleanup)
    let mut index = usize.ZERO
    while index < recorded.length && (recorded[index].holder != holder || recorded[index].repeat != repeat) {
      index = index + usize.ONE
    }
    if index == recorded.length {
      run List<LoopCleanup>.append(&mut walker.loopCleanup, LoopCleanup {holder: holder, repeat: repeat})
    }
  }
  let mut unknownHeld = false
  if available[holder].unknown && holder < List<List<usize>>.length(&walker.held) {
    let held = List<List<usize>>.asSlice(&walker.held)
    unknownHeld = List<usize>.length(&held[holder]) > usize.ZERO
  }
  if unknownHeld && !hidden {
    leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
    return at
  }
  let everything = unknownHeld && hidden
  if !everything && List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(&available[holder].regions) == usize.ZERO {
    return at
  }
  let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, at)
  let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  points[point].span = span
  let cleanup = List<LoanCleanup>.asSlice(&walker.cleanup)
  let observed = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&cleanup[holder].regions)
  let definitions = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < definitions.length {
    let definition = definitions[index]
    if definition.holder == holder {
      let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
      let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loans[definition.loan].regions)
      if everything || named.length == usize.ZERO || sharesAtom(named, observed) {
        if named.length == usize.ZERO {
          loans[definition.loan].precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown
        }
        run List<
          Interval
        >.append(
          &mut loans[definition.loan].intervals,
          Interval {
            from: definition.point,
            to: point,
            definition: index,
            read: point,
            cleanup: true
          }
        )
      }
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return point
}

// Visits one node from point `at` and returns the point after it, or `usize.MAX` when no path
// continues, with the loans its value carries.
effect fn visit(
  nodes: &[Node],
  locals: &[Local],
  owner: &DeclarationId,
  walker: &mut Walker,
  id: NodeId,
  at: usize
) -> Flow
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let flow = run visitNode(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, id, at)
  if
    !walker.outside && flow.at != usize.MAX {
    let mut runs = false
    if let NodeKind.Expression { form: Expression.Run { .. }, .. } = &nodes[id.index].kind {
      runs = true
    }
    if runs {
      let failed = run releaseScopes(
        &mut walker.*,
        usize.ZERO,
        nodes[id.index].origin.location,
        flow.at
      )
      let exit = walker.exit
      run edge(&mut walker.*, failed, exit)
    }
  }
  // An expression of type `never` does not complete: no path continues past it, so the code after
  // it is unreachable and never borrow-checked, as after a `return`.
  if !walker.outside && flow.at != usize.MAX && neverValue(nodes, id) {
    run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), flow.at)
    return flowAt(usize.MAX)
  }
  return move flow
}

fn neverValue(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> bool {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {ty, ..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
    return Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&ty, uninhabited)
  }
  return false
}

fn uninhabited(ty: &Type) -> bool {
  return match &ty.* {
    Type.Union {members} => List<Shared<Type>>.length(&members) == usize.ZERO
    _ => false
  }
}

effect fn visitNode(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, id: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  if walker.outside || at == usize.MAX {
    return flowAt(at)
  }
  let span = nodes[id.index].origin.location
  let shape = run shapeOf(nodes, id)
  match move shape {
    Shape.Leaf => {
      return flowAt(at)
    }
    Shape.Outside {reason} => {
      leave(&mut walker.*, reason)
      return flowAt(at)
    }
    Shape.ReadPlace => {
      let mut path = run pathOf(nodes, id)
      let mut current = at
      if path.root == usize.MAX {
        // Lowering drops a temporary that needs cleanup at the end of its statement, or of a
        // viewing binding's scope when that binding's initializer retains it. A projection out of
        // one whose cleanup can observe a loan is read through its hidden owner, which
        // `holdTemporary` registers in that same scope, so the owner holds the loan until the
        // cleanup (BORROW-006).
        let base = projectedBase(nodes, id)
        if !observingCleanup(&walker.*, holderOf(&walker.*, temporaryRoot(nodes, base.index))) {
          return run readValue(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, id, at)
        }
        current = run holdTemporary(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, base, at)
        path = run temporaryPath(nodes, id, base)
      }
      let flow = run place(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Read, span, current)
      if path.through || List<Step>.length(&path.steps) > usize.ZERO {
        // A read through or out of a holder copies a value; one that retains a region would carry
        // the holder's loan onward.
        if List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO || (path.through && holds(&walker.*, path.root)) {
          let retained = run nodeRetains(nodes, id, owner)
          if retained {
            let declared = run declaredRead(nodes, id, owner)
            let read = run attributeRead(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), &declared)
            let unplaced = List<List<Step>>.make()
            let untyped = List<NodeId>.make()
            let noSinks = List<OperandSink>.make()
            return run finish(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, id, flow.at, &read, false, Forwarding.Matched, List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&unplaced), List<NodeId>.asSlice(&untyped), List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&noSinks))
          }
        }
        let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
        // Overwritten holdings describe the holder's historical type, not the source of this
        // scalar read. Retained-value reads above still carry that history. An inherited holding
        // is a distinct value and remains a possible source until its own place is overwritten.
        let mut selected = List<Carry>.make()
        let carried = List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried)
        let definitions = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
        let mut index = usize.ZERO
        while index < carried.length {
          let carry = carried[index]
          if carry.definition == usize.MAX || !definitions[carry.definition].shadowed {
            run List<Carry>.append(&mut selected, carry)
          }
          index = index + usize.ONE
        }
        run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&selected), point)
        return flowAt(point)
      }
      return move flow
    }
    Shape.Borrow {access, value} => {
      return run borrow(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, value, access == Access.Mutable, span, id.index, at)
    }
    Shape.Move {value, consumed} => {
      if consumed {
        let path = run pathOf(nodes, value)
        if path.root == usize.MAX || path.through {
          leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
          return flowAt(at)
        }
        let moved = run place(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Move, span, at)
        let event = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)[moved.at].event
        let mut events = List<Event>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.events)
        events[event].target = nodes[value.index].origin.location
        return move moved
      }
      return run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, value, at)
    }
    Shape.Operands {values, places, member} => {
      return run operands(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, List<NodeId>.asSlice(&values), List<usize>.asSlice(&places), member, id, at)
    }
    Shape.ShortCircuit {left, right} => {
      let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
      let first = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, left, at)
      run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&first.carried), usize.ZERO)
      let second = run settled(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, right, first.at)
      run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&second.carried), usize.ONE)
      // The left operand alone can decide the result, so the path that skips the right operand
      // joins it: a right operand that never completes does not end the expression.
      let mut reached = second.at
      if first.at != usize.MAX {
        reached = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, second.at)
        run edge(&mut walker.*, first.at, reached)
      }
      let untyped = List<NodeId>.make()
      let noSinks = List<OperandSink>.make()
      let unplaced = List<List<Step>>.make()
      return run finish(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, id, reached, &carried, false, Forwarding.None, List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&unplaced), List<NodeId>.asSlice(&untyped), List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&noSinks))
    }
    Shape.PassThrough {value} => {
      return run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, value, at)
    }
    Shape.Call {arguments, receiver, exact, signature} => {
      return run call(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments), receiver, exact, signature, id, at)
    }
    Shape.Construct {values, referents, staged, holdable, body} => {
      return run construct(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, List<NodeId>.asSlice(&values), List<ReferentCapture>.asSlice(&referents), staged,
        List<CaptureHold>.asSlice(&holdable), body, id, at)
    }
    Shape.Invoke {callee, arguments, pipeline, exclusive} => {
      return run invoke(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments), pipeline, exclusive, id, at)
    }
    Shape.Defer {callee, arguments, pipeline, mode} => {
      return run defer(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, callee, List<NodeId>.asSlice(&arguments), pipeline, mode, id, at)
    }
    Shape.Binding {local, initializer, mutable} => {
      let declared = localType(locals, local)
      run recordStore(&mut walker.*, owner, &declared, span, local)
      walker.retention = Retention.None
      if Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&declared, Type.holdsView) {
        walker.retention = Retention.Arrays
      } else if Type.hasOpenRuntimeParameters(&declared) {
        walker.retention = Retention.Storage
      }
      let firstLoan = List<Loan>.length(&walker.loans)
      let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, initializer, at)
      walker.retention = Retention.None
      let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
      let mut initialized = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
      initialized[point].initializes = local
      initialized[point].defines = local
      // A binding retains its initializer's value here, which is where a loan it carries is retained.
      initialized[point].span = nodes[initializer.index].origin.location
      run registerRoot(&mut walker.*, local)
      if isCallable(nodes, initializer) && Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&declared, effectBlock) && local < List<bool>.length(&walker.unrun) {
        let mut unrun = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.unrun)
        unrun[local] = true
        // The loans this initializer took are the block's own captures.
        let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
        let mut loan = firstLoan
        while loan < loans.length {
          loans[loan].block = local
          loan = loan + usize.ONE
        }
      }
      if List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO {
        // A binding whose written type names only universal regions, chosen before the body runs,
        // keeps what it is given valid for them: its loans outlive the body wherever their creation
        // reaches. An inferred type may name a parameter's region without requiring it.
        if locals[local].written && run universallyTyped(&declared, owner) {
          let given = List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried)
          let mut all = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
          let mut each = usize.ZERO
          while each < given.length {
            all[given[each].loan].escapes = true
            each = each + usize.ONE
          }
        }
        run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
        let ty = localType(locals, local)
        let callable = Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&ty, callableValue)
        let retained = callable || run retains(&ty, owner)
        if retained {
          // A `mut fn` is invoked through a mutable binding. Its capture loans stay held until the
          // local's last use even if it is replaced, and a replacement that carries loans leaves.
          if mutable && !callable {
            cross(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried))
          }
          run hold(&mut walker.*, local, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point, true)
        }
      }
      return flowAt(point)
    }
    Shape.Assignment {local, value} => {
      run recordStore(&mut walker.*, owner, &localType(locals, local), span, local)
      // The written binding is the statement's first token.
      let target = Location {start: span.start, end: span.start + usize.ONE}
      return run replace(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, local, value, span, target, at)
    }
    Shape.PlaceAssignment {target, value} => {
      let path = run pathOf(nodes, target)
      if path.through {
        if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value: written} = move expressionType(nodes, target) {
          run recordStore(&mut walker.*, owner, &written, span, usize.MAX)
        }
        let source = run pathOf(nodes, movedOperand(nodes, value))
        if source.root < walker.localCount && !source.through { run List<usize>.append(&mut walker.escaping, source.root) }
      } else if path.root < walker.localCount {
        run recordStore(&mut walker.*, owner, &localType(locals, path.root), span, path.root)
      }
      if path.root != usize.MAX && !path.through && List<Step>.length(&path.steps) == usize.ZERO {
        return run replace(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, path.root, value, span, nodes[target.index].origin.location, at)
      }
      if path.root == usize.MAX {
        leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
        return flowAt(at)
      }
      let evaluated = run indexes(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, at)
      let since = List<Event>.length(&walker.events)
      let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, value, evaluated)
      // Storage behind a reference may outlive this body whatever regions its type names, so a
      // loan of storage this body owns stored there is left unchecked rather than consumed.
      if path.through && carriesLocal(&walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried)) {
        leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
        return flowAt(flow.at)
      }
      if List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO {
        let retained = run nodeRetains(nodes, target, owner)
        if retained {
          if path.through {
            leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
            return flowAt(flow.at)
          }
          let carried = List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried)
          let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
          let mut index = usize.ZERO
          while index < carried.length {
            // A field store keeps an exact loan's flow but not its region relation.
            let stored = loans[carried[index].loan].precision
            if stored == LoanPrecision.Exact { loans[carried[index].loan].precision = LoanPrecision.Stored }
            else if stored == LoanPrecision.Alternatives { loans[carried[index].loan].precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown }
            index = index + usize.ONE
          }
        }
      }
      let targetSpan = writtenSpan(nodes, target)
      let mut point = usize.MAX
      if path.through {
        let reached = run throughReference(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Write, targetSpan, flow.at)
        run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&reached.carried), reached.at)
        point = reached.at
      } else {
        point = run access(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Write, targetSpan, flow.at, usize.MAX)
        markConsumedTarget(&mut walker.*, since, point, span)
      }
      run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
      if !path.through && run nodeRetains(nodes, target, owner) {
        // The written place's old value leaves, and with it every loan held within that place.
        let used = run useHolder(&mut walker.*, path.root, usize.MAX, targetSpan, point)
        if exactPath(List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps)) {
          let written = run internPath(&mut walker.*, run copySteps(List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps)))
          let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
          points[used.at].written = written
        }
        let mut carrying = List<Carry>.make()
        let mut discarded = List<Carry>.make()
        let previous = List<Carry>.asSlice(&used.carried)
        let mut index = usize.ZERO
        while index < previous.length {
          let shadowed = previous[index].definition != usize.MAX
            && List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)[previous[index].definition].shadowed
          if shadowed || run discards(&walker.*, List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps), previous[index].field) {
            run List<Carry>.append(&mut discarded, previous[index])
          } else {
            run List<Carry>.append(&mut carrying, previous[index])
          }
          index = index + usize.ONE
        }
        let stored = List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried)
        index = usize.ZERO
        while index < stored.length {
          let mut moved = stored[index]
          moved.field = run prefixedPath(&mut walker.*, List<Step>.asSlice(&path.steps), stored[index].field)
          moved.direct = moved.direct && moved.field != usize.MAX
          run List<Carry>.append(&mut carrying, moved)
          index = index + usize.ONE
        }
        run hold(&mut walker.*, path.root, List<Carry>.asSlice(&carrying), used.at, true)
        run shadow(&mut walker.*, path.root, List<Carry>.asSlice(&discarded), used.at)
        return flowAt(used.at)
      }
      return flowAt(point)
    }
    // `replace` is `let old = place; place = value` with nothing in between: the value is evaluated,
    // then the place is read and written at the call.
    Shape.Displace {target, value} => {
      let path = run pathOf(nodes, target)
      if path.root == usize.MAX {
        leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
        return flowAt(at)
      }
      // A displaced value that retains a region carries what its place held: through a reference,
      // what that reference reaches, as a read through it does. A local holder's definitions would
      // have to move to the displaced value, which this walk does not model.
      let retained = run nodeRetains(nodes, target, owner)
      if retained && !path.through {
        leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
        return flowAt(at)
      }
      let evaluated = run indexes(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, at)
      let since = List<Event>.length(&walker.events)
      let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, value, evaluated)
      let targetSpan = writtenSpan(nodes, target)
      let mut point = usize.MAX
      if path.through {
        // Storing a loan behind a reference is a retaining write through a referent.
        if retained && List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO {
          leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
          return flowAt(flow.at)
        }
        let read = run throughReference(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Read, targetSpan, flow.at)
        let written = run throughReference(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Write, targetSpan, read.at)
        run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&written.carried), written.at)
        point = written.at
        run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
        if retained {
          let untyped = List<NodeId>.make()
          let noSinks = List<OperandSink>.make()
          let unplaced = List<List<Step>>.make()
          return run finish(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, id, point, &read.carried, false, Forwarding.None, List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&unplaced), List<NodeId>.asSlice(&untyped), List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&noSinks))
        }
        run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&read.carried), point)
        return flowAt(point)
      }
      // Reading a part of a holder uses the holder, as every read rooted at one does.
      let mut reading = flow.at
      if holds(&walker.*, path.root) {
        let read = run readPath(&mut walker.*, &path)
        let used = run useHolder(&mut walker.*, path.root, read, targetSpan, reading)
        run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&used.carried), used.at)
        reading = used.at
      }
      let read = run access(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Read, targetSpan, reading, usize.MAX)
      point = run access(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Write, targetSpan, read, usize.MAX)
      markConsumedTarget(&mut walker.*, since, point, span)
      run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
      return flowAt(point)
    }
    Shape.Exit {value} => {
      let mut flow = flowAt(at)
      let mut required = span
      if let Option<NodeId>.Some {value: operand} = &value {
        // A returned value is stored in the caller's result slot, typed at the body's lifetime
        // parameters its result names, as a write through a reference is (`storedGoal`).
        if let NodeKind.Return {..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
          if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value: returned} = move expressionType(nodes, operand) {
            if let Option<StoreWindow>.Some {value: window} = move run storeWindow(owner, &returned, span, usize.MAX) {
              run List<StoreWindow>.append(&mut walker.returns, move window)
            }
          }
        }
        flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, operand, at)
        if let NodeKind.Return {..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
          required = nodes[operand.index].origin.location
        }
      }
      let current = run releaseScopes(&mut walker.*, usize.ZERO, required, flow.at)
      let exit = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, current)
      let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
      points[exit].span = required
      run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), exit)
      cross(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried))
      let target = walker.exit
      run edge(&mut walker.*, exit, target)
      return flowAt(usize.MAX)
    }
    Shape.Drop {value, consumed} => {
      if consumed {
        let path = run pathOf(nodes, value)
        if path.root == usize.MAX || path.through {
          leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
          return flowAt(at)
        }
        let flow = run place(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Drop, span, at)
        let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
        run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
        return flowAt(point)
      }
      let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, value, at)
      let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
      run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
      return flowAt(point)
    }
    Shape.Branch {condition, thenBranch, elseBranch} => {
      let tested = run settled(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, condition, at)
      let split = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, tested.at)
      run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&tested.carried), split)
      let taken = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, thenBranch, split)
      let mut other = flowAt(split)
      if let Option<NodeId>.Some {value: alternative} = &elseBranch {
        other = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, alternative, split)
      }
      // When neither arm completes, nothing follows the branch.
      if taken.at == usize.MAX && other.at == usize.MAX {
        return flowAt(usize.MAX)
      }
      let joined = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, taken.at)
      run edge(&mut walker.*, other.at, joined)
      let mut onward = List<Carry>.make()
      // `if` is a statement: its branches cannot yield a loan-carrying result. These consumes
      // may coincide with the last End; value-producing match arms instead consume after End.
      run rejoin(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&taken.carried), taken.at, joined, &mut onward)
      run rejoin(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&other.carried), other.at, joined, &mut onward)
      return Flow {at: joined, carried: move onward}
    }
    Shape.While {condition, body} => {
      let header = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, at)
      let exit = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, usize.MAX)
      let repeat = List<Loop>.length(&walker.loops)
      run List<Loop>.append(&mut walker.loops, Loop {before: at, header: header, sources: List<usize>.make(), end: usize.ZERO, span: span})
      // A `break` or `continue` in the condition belongs to the enclosing loop (TRANSFER-001), as
      // lowering evaluates the condition before it enters this loop's targets, so the condition is
      // walked before this loop's frame is pushed.
      let tested = run settled(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, condition, header)
      if tested.at == usize.MAX {
        let mut loops = List<Loop>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loops)
        loops[repeat].end = List<Point>.length(&walker.points)
        return flowAt(usize.MAX)
      }
      // Only the checked literal supplies a feasible-edge fact. Evaluate the condition normally;
      // calls, local reads and other runtime expressions retain both alternatives.
      let mut enters = true
      let mut skips = true
      if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Boolean {value}, ..} = &nodes[condition.index].kind {
        enters = value
        skips = !value
      }
      run List<Frame>.append(&mut walker.frames, Frame {exit: exit, repeat: repeat, scopes: List<Scope>.length(&walker.scopes)})
      let split = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, tested.at)
      run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&tested.carried), split)
      if skips { run edge(&mut walker.*, split, exit) }
      let mut repeated = flowAt(usize.MAX)
      if enters { repeated = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, body, split) }
      run backEdge(&mut walker.*, repeat, repeated.at)
      let mut loops = List<Loop>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loops)
      loops[repeat].end = List<Point>.length(&walker.points)
      let enclosing = List<Frame>.length(&walker.frames) - usize.ONE
      List<Frame>.truncate(&mut walker.frames, enclosing)
      if List<Carry>.length(&repeated.carried) > usize.ZERO {
        leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
      }
      if !skips {
        // A literal-true loop completes only through an actual break path. Do not revive code
        // after a returning or endlessly repeating body through its unattached exit point.
        let mut paths = List<ReplacementReach>.make()
        if !run reachesAvoiding(&walker.*, &mut paths, split, exit, usize.MAX) { return flowAt(usize.MAX) }
      }
      return flowAt(exit)
    }
    Shape.Break => {
      let frames = List<Frame>.asSlice(&walker.frames)
      if frames.length == usize.ZERO {
        leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.Awaiting)
        return flowAt(usize.MAX)
      }
      let frame = frames[frames.length - usize.ONE]
      let released = run releaseScopes(&mut walker.*, frame.scopes, span, at)
      run edge(&mut walker.*, released, frame.exit)
      return flowAt(usize.MAX)
    }
    Shape.Recovered {resumes} => {
      if !resumes { return flowAt(usize.MAX) }
      let entry = walker.entry
      return flowAt(run newPoint(&mut walker.*, entry))
    }
    Shape.Continue => {
      let frames = List<Frame>.asSlice(&walker.frames)
      if frames.length == usize.ZERO {
        leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.Awaiting)
        return flowAt(usize.MAX)
      }
      let frame = frames[frames.length - usize.ONE]
      let released = run releaseScopes(&mut walker.*, frame.scopes, span, at)
      run backEdge(&mut walker.*, frame.repeat, released)
      return flowAt(usize.MAX)
    }
    Shape.Match {subject, access, arms, syntax} => {
      return run matchArms(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, subject, access, List<ArmShape>.asSlice(&arms), syntax, id, at)
    }
    Shape.Block {statements} => {
      let enclosing = List<Scope>.length(&walker.scopes)
      run List<Scope>.append(&mut walker.scopes, Scope {roots: List<usize>.make(), expiring: List<usize>.make(), statement: false})
      let list = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&statements)
      let mut flow = flowAt(at)
      let retention = walker.retention
      let mut index = usize.ZERO
      while index < list.length {
        // A statement's temporaries end with it (BORROW-006); a statement of a nested block is
        // never a binding initializer of an enclosing one.
        let statement = List<Scope>.length(&walker.scopes)
        run List<Scope>.append(&mut walker.scopes, Scope {roots: List<usize>.make(), expiring: List<usize>.make(), statement: true})
        walker.retention = Retention.None
        flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, list[index], flow.at)
        let ended = run releaseScopes(&mut walker.*, statement, nodes[list[index].index].origin.location, flow.at)
        List<Scope>.truncate(&mut walker.scopes, statement)
        flow.at = ended
        if index + usize.ONE < list.length && flow.at != usize.MAX {
          let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
          run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
          flow = flowAt(point)
        }
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
      walker.retention = retention
      let released = run releaseScopes(&mut walker.*, enclosing, span, flow.at)
      List<Scope>.truncate(&mut walker.scopes, enclosing)
      return Flow {at: released, carried: move flow.carried}
    }
  }
}

// A whole replacement observes displaced cleanup, then kills the earlier holder definitions
// and installs the new carried loans (ASSIGN-002). An access conflict is reported at the written
// `target`; a target the value moves out of is reported over the whole statement `span`.
effect fn replace(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, local: usize, value: NodeId, span: Location, target: Location,
  at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let since = List<Event>.length(&walker.events)
  let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, value, at)
  let ty = localType(locals, local)
  let callable = Shared<Type>.with<bool>(&ty, callableValue)
  if callable && List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO {
    // Replacing an exact callable environment needs its representation transfer proof. Do not
    // silently discard the new capture loans while retaining the old environment's bound.
    leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
    return flowAt(flow.at)
  }
  let mut retained = false
  if List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO {
    retained = run retains(&ty, owner)
  }
  let path = Path {root: local, through: false, steps: List<Step>.make(), indexes: List<NodeId>.make(), refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: usize.ZERO, binders: List<usize>.make()}
  let cleaned = run observeCleanup(&mut walker.*, local, false, span, flow.at)
  let point = run access(&mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Write, target, cleaned, usize.MAX)
  markConsumedTarget(&mut walker.*, since, point, span)
  run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point)
  // A replaced `mut fn` keeps its capture loans until the local's last use, as bound.
  if !callable {
    let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
    points[point].defines = local
    if retained {
      cross(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried))
      run hold(&mut walker.*, local, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), point, true)
    }
  }
  return flowAt(point)
}

// The extent and kind of a borrowing match's loan of its subject place (MATCH-001), pending the
// language decision. Spanning the arm holds the loan through every point of the selected arm, guard
// included, whether or not the arm binds; otherwise it ends at the arm's last binding use. Matching
// the access lends `&mut` exclusively; otherwise the owner may still be read beside an idle
// exclusive binding. These agree with the bootstrap's `armLoan`, which governs `match` alone. An
// `if let` lends through its whole taken body when it binds, and a destructuring `let` until its
// bindings' scope ends, each exclusively for `&mut` (PATT-009).
fn armLoanSpansArm() -> bool { return false }

fn armLoanMatchesAccess() -> bool { return false }

// A match (MATCH-001): the subject is accessed once as its form declares, then the arms are tried
// in written order. A pattern that does not select the value, or a guard that answers false, goes on
// to the next arm; every selected arm joins after the match. A borrowing match's bindings are
// projections of the subject place (MATCH-002): a slot of the match holds a loan of that place, which
// every use of a binding uses, so writing, moving or exclusively borrowing the place other than
// through a binding conflicts while a binding is still used. What the bindings retain is the region
// slice's to prove.
effect fn matchArms(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, subject: NodeId, access: Scrutinee,
  arms: &[ArmShape], syntax: MatchSyntax, result: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let span = nodes[subject.index].origin.location
  let mut flow = flowAt(at)
  // Whether the subject's carried loans are placed within its own value.
  let mut attributed = false
  let path = run pathOf(nodes, subject)
  // A borrowing destructuring `let` keeps its subject's temporaries for its bindings' scope.
  let retention = walker.retention
  if syntax == MatchSyntax.Let && (access == Scrutinee.Shared || access == Scrutinee.Exclusive || access == Scrutinee.Place) {
    walker.retention = Retention.Storage
  }
  if access == Scrutinee.Moved {
    if path.root == usize.MAX || path.through {
      leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans)
      return flowAt(at)
    }
    let moved = run place(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, Kind.Move, span, at)
    // The subject is read whole, so no loan it holds is within a narrower read.
    let whole = DeclaredRead {known: false, regions: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()}
    flow = Flow {at: moved.at, carried: run attributeRead(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, List<Carry>.asSlice(&moved.carried), &whole)}
    attributed = true
  } else if (access == Scrutinee.Exclusive || access == Scrutinee.Place) && path.root != usize.MAX {
    let mut kind = Kind.Inspect
    if access == Scrutinee.Exclusive {
      kind = Kind.Update
    }
    flow = run place(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, kind, span, at)
  } else if (access == Scrutinee.Shared || access == Scrutinee.Exclusive) && path.root == usize.MAX {
    // Projecting a reference value names no place; the reference carries the loans of the storage
    // the subject is, which its bindings view.
    let mut indexes = List<NodeId>.make()
    let reference = run viewedReference(nodes, subject, &mut indexes)
    flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, reference, at)
    let operands = List<NodeId>.asSlice(&indexes)
    let mut operand = usize.ZERO
    while operand < operands.length {
      let indexed = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, operands[operand], flow.at)
      run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&indexed.carried), indexed.at)
      flow.at = indexed.at
      operand = operand + usize.ONE
    }
  } else {
    flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, subject, at)
    attributed = true
  }
  walker.retention = retention
  let mut armLoan = usize.MAX
  // The loans a borrowed subject with no place carries, such as the argument loans a returned
  // reference keeps: its bindings view that storage, so they hold the loans as an arm loan.
  let mut viewed = List<usize>.make()
  if (access == Scrutinee.Shared || access == Scrutinee.Exclusive) && path.root == usize.MAX
    && List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO {
    let lent = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
    run hold(&mut walker.*, bindingsRoot(nodes, subject.index), List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), lent, false)
    let carried = List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried)
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < carried.length {
      run List<usize>.append(&mut viewed, carried[at].loan)
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    flow.at = lent
    if syntax == MatchSyntax.Let && arms.length > usize.ZERO && arms[usize.ZERO].binds {
      run List<usize>.append(&mut walker.lexicalHolders, bindingsRoot(nodes, subject.index))
      run registerRoot(&mut walker.*, bindingsRoot(nodes, subject.index))
    }
  }
  if (access == Scrutinee.Shared || access == Scrutinee.Exclusive) && path.root != usize.MAX {
    // An `if let` or destructuring `let` lends as its subject is borrowed (PATT-009).
    let exclusive = access == Scrutinee.Exclusive && (syntax != MatchSyntax.Match || armLoanMatchesAccess())
    let parent = run borrowedPlaceLifetime(nodes, subject)
    let loaned = run takeLoan(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, exclusive, span, usize.MAX, move parent, flow.at, List<Carry>.make())
    let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
    armLoan = loans.length - usize.ONE
    loans[armLoan].binder = subject.index
    let lent = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, loaned.at)
    run hold(&mut walker.*, bindingsRoot(nodes, subject.index), List<Carry>.asSlice(&loaned.carried), lent, false)
    run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&loaned.carried), lent)
    flow.at = lent
    if syntax == MatchSyntax.Let && arms.length > usize.ZERO && arms[usize.ZERO].binds {
      // Its bindings belong to the enclosing block (PATT-008), which keeps the loan to its end.
      run List<usize>.append(&mut walker.lexicalHolders, bindingsRoot(nodes, subject.index))
      run registerRoot(&mut walker.*, bindingsRoot(nodes, subject.index))
    }
  }
  let tested = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, flow.at)
  if access == Scrutinee.Place && path.root != usize.MAX {
    run List<Refinement>.append(&mut walker.refinements, Refinement {subject: subject.index, test: tested})
  }
  if List<Carry>.length(&flow.carried) > usize.ZERO {
    // Bindings of a subject that carries a loan would hold it, where the subject's value holds it
    // when that value was moved or computed; loans an accessed place carries are its holder's.
    let retained = run nodeRetains(nodes, subject, owner)
    if retained {
      run hold(&mut walker.*, subjectRoot(subject), List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), tested, attributed)
    }
    run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), tested)
  }
  let enclosing = List<Scope>.length(&walker.scopes)
  // A destructuring let's bindings belong to its enclosing block (PATT-008), rather than the
  // synthetic arm used by typing. Match and if-let bindings end on their selected arm path.
  if syntax != MatchSyntax.Let {
    run List<Scope>.append(&mut walker.scopes, Scope {roots: List<usize>.make(), expiring: List<usize>.make(), statement: false})
  }
  run registerRoot(&mut walker.*, subjectRoot(subject))
  // The subject's own storage is bound here, so moves of its parts in an earlier iteration of an
  // enclosing loop do not reach this one.
  let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  points[tested].initializes = subjectRoot(subject)
  let mut ends = List<usize>.make()
  // Whether some arm completes; when none does, nothing follows the match.
  let mut completes = false
  // The referent loans the selected arms' results carry to the join.
  let mut joining = List<Carry>.make()
  let mut rejected = List<usize>.make()
  run List<usize>.append(&mut rejected, tested)
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < arms.length {
    let entry = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, usize.MAX)
    let earlier = List<usize>.asSlice(&rejected)
    let mut from = usize.ZERO
    while from < earlier.length {
      run edge(&mut walker.*, earlier[from], entry)
      from = from + usize.ONE
    }
    List<usize>.truncate(&mut rejected, usize.ZERO)
    run List<usize>.append(&mut rejected, entry)
    let mut selected = entry
    if let Option<NodeId>.Some {value: guard} = &arms[index].guard {
      // A consuming match's bindings are parts of the subject's own storage until the guard holds.
      let consuming = access == Scrutinee.Moved || access == Scrutinee.Value
      if consuming { run List<usize>.append(&mut walker.guarded, subjectRoot(subject)) }
      let checked = run settled(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, guard, entry)
      if consuming { drop List<usize>.pop(&mut walker.guarded) }
      selected = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, checked.at)
      run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&checked.carried), selected)
      run List<usize>.append(&mut rejected, selected)
    }
    let taken = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, arms[index].result, selected)
    let released = run releaseScopes(&mut walker.*, enclosing, nodes[result.index].origin.location, taken.at)
    if released != usize.MAX { completes = true }
    let point = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, released)
    // An `if let` body that binds holds the loan throughout (PATT-009).
    let spans = (syntax == MatchSyntax.Match && armLoanSpansArm()) || (syntax == MatchSyntax.IfLet && arms[index].binds)
    if spans {
      // Every point of the arm, guard included, lies between its entry and its end.
      let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
      if armLoan != usize.MAX {
        run List<Interval>.append(&mut loans[armLoan].intervals,
          Interval {from: entry, to: point, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, cleanup: false})
      }
      let lent = List<usize>.asSlice(&viewed)
      let mut at = usize.ZERO
      while at < lent.length {
        run List<Interval>.append(&mut loans[lent[at]].intervals,
          Interval {from: entry, to: point, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, cleanup: false})
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    if List<Carry>.length(&taken.carried) > usize.ZERO {
      // A loan carried out of an arm is joined across the arms.
      let retained = run nodeRetains(nodes, result, owner)
      if retained {
        if taken.at != usize.MAX {
          cross(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&taken.carried))
          run appendCarried(&mut joining, List<Carry>.asSlice(&taken.carried))
        }
      }
    }
    run consume(&mut walker.*, List<Carry>.asSlice(&taken.carried), point)
    run List<usize>.append(&mut ends, point)
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let joined = run newPoint(&mut walker.*, usize.MAX)
  let selected = List<usize>.asSlice(&ends)
  index = usize.ZERO
  while index < selected.length {
    run edge(&mut walker.*, selected[index], joined)
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let carried = List<Carry>.asSlice(&joining)
  let mut onward = List<Carry>.make()
  index = usize.ZERO
  while index < carried.length {
    run List<Carry>.append(&mut onward, Carry {loan: carried[index].loan, since: joined, operand: usize.MAX, definition: carried[index].definition, read: carried[index].read, field: carried[index].field, direct: carried[index].direct})
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  List<Scope>.truncate(&mut walker.scopes, enclosing)
  if !completes { return flowAt(usize.MAX) }
  return Flow {at: joined, carried: move onward}
}

// Visits an operand whose temporaries end with it, before control flow depends on its value: a
// condition, a guard or a short-circuit right operand (BORROW-006). Lowering never keeps them for a
// binding, so they never extend to an enclosing scope.
effect fn settled(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, id: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let scope = List<Scope>.length(&walker.scopes)
  run List<Scope>.append(&mut walker.scopes, Scope {roots: List<usize>.make(), expiring: List<usize>.make(), statement: true})
  let retention = walker.retention
  walker.retention = Retention.None
  let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, id, at)
  walker.retention = retention
  let ended = run releaseScopes(&mut walker.*, scope, nodes[id.index].origin.location, flow.at)
  List<Scope>.truncate(&mut walker.scopes, scope)
  return Flow {at: ended, carried: move flow.carried}
}

// A field, index or dereference of a value that is not a written place: its operand is evaluated
// and consumed by the projection. A field selects the same carried source paths as a named holder
// read, including disjoint sibling fields. Whole-value or unknown paths remain conservative unless
// the field's declared type proves that the loan cannot reach it (`unreachableField`).
effect fn readValue(nodes: &[Node], locals: &[Local], owner: &DeclarationId, walker: &mut Walker, id: NodeId, at: usize) -> Flow
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut values = List<NodeId>.make()
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form, ..} = &nodes[id.index].kind {
    match &form {
      Expression.Field {value, ..} => {
        let subject = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, value, at)
        let declared = run declaredRead(nodes, id, owner)
        // Reuse the same field mapping as a named holder read. The synthetic temporary path
        // describes only this projection; no storage or lifetime extension is introduced.
        let path = run temporaryPath(nodes, id, value)
        let selected = run attributeRead(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, &path, List<Carry>.asSlice(&subject.carried), &declared)
        let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
        run appendOperand(&mut carried, List<Carry>.asSlice(&selected), usize.ZERO)
        // The extracted value forwards each selected source at its residual field path.
        // An empty prefix preserves that path across successive rvalue projections.
        let mut placed = List<List<Step>>.make()
        run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut placed, List<Step>.make())
        let untyped = List<NodeId>.make()
        let noSinks = List<OperandSink>.make()
        return run finish(nodes, owner, &mut walker.*, id, subject.at, &carried, false, Forwarding.Operands,
          List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&placed), List<NodeId>.asSlice(&untyped), List<OperandSink>.asSlice(&noSinks))
      }
      Expression.Dereference {value} => { run List<NodeId>.append(&mut values, value) }
      Expression.Index {value, index, ..} => {
        run List<NodeId>.append(&mut values, value)
        run List<NodeId>.append(&mut values, index)
      }
      _ => {}
    }
  }
  let unplaced = List<usize>.make()
  return run operands(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker.*, List<NodeId>.asSlice(&values), List<usize>.asSlice(&unplaced), usize.MAX, id, at)
}

// The outermost loop still being walked, its condition included, or `usize.MAX` outside every
// loop. A loop's `end` is set once its body has been walked.
fn outermostOpenLoop(walker: &Walker) -> usize {
  let loops = List<Loop>.asSlice(&walker.loops)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < loops.length {
    if loops[at].end == usize.ZERO { return at }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return usize.MAX
}

// Makes `local` hold the loans its initializer carries from point `at`.
// Records that `root` holds `carried` from `at`. An `attributed` hold keeps each loan's field path,
// relative to the root's value; any other forgets it, so no field read forwards the loan.
effect fn hold(walker: &mut Walker, root: usize, carried: &[Carry], at: usize, attributed: bool) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let local = holderOf(&walker.*, root)
  let mut unseenCleanup = false
  if carried.length > usize.ZERO {
    let observed = List<LoopCleanup>.asSlice(&walker.loopCleanup)
    let loops = List<Loop>.asSlice(&walker.loops)
    let mut index = usize.ZERO
    while index < observed.length {
      if observed[index].holder == local && loops[observed[index].repeat].end == usize.ZERO { unseenCleanup = true }
      index = index + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  if unseenCleanup { leave(&mut walker.*, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans) }
  while List<List<usize>>.length(&walker.held) <= local {
    run List<List<usize>>.append(&mut walker.held, List<usize>.make())
  }
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < carried.length {
    let inherited = shadowedSource(&walker.*, carried[index].definition)
    let mut previous = usize.ZERO
    let mut seen = false
    while previous < index {
      if sameHoldingPosition(&walker.*, carried[previous], carried[index], attributed)
        && shadowedSource(&walker.*, carried[previous].definition) == inherited { seen = true }
      previous = previous + usize.ONE
    }
    if !seen {
      let definition = List<Holding>.length(&walker.definitions)
      let mut field = usize.MAX
      let mut direct = false
      if attributed {
        field = carried[index].field
        direct = carried[index].direct && field != usize.MAX
      }
      let sources = List<HoldingSource>.length(&walker.holdingSources)
      let mut unconditional = false
      let mut each = index
      while each < carried.length {
        if sameHoldingPosition(&walker.*, carried[each], carried[index], attributed)
          && shadowedSource(&walker.*, carried[each].definition) == inherited {
          if carried[each].definition == usize.MAX { unconditional = true }
          else {
            let recorded = List<HoldingSource>.asSlice(&walker.holdingSources)
            let mut source = sources
            let mut duplicate = false
            while source < recorded.length {
              if recorded[source].definition == carried[each].definition && recorded[source].read == carried[each].read { duplicate = true }
              source = source + usize.ONE
            }
            if !duplicate {
              run List<HoldingSource>.append(&mut walker.holdingSources, HoldingSource {definition: carried[each].definition, read: carried[each].read})
            }
          }
        }
        each = each + usize.ONE
      }
      let mut sourceCount = List<HoldingSource>.length(&walker.holdingSources) - sources
      if unconditional {
        List<HoldingSource>.truncate(&mut walker.holdingSources, sources)
        sourceCount = usize.ZERO
      }
      run List<Holding>.append(&mut walker.definitions, Holding {loan: carried[index].loan, holder: local, point: at,
        sources: sources, sourceCount: sourceCount, field: field, direct: direct, shadowed: false, inherited: inherited})
      let mut held = List<List<usize>>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.held)
      run List<usize>.append(&mut held[local], definition)
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  points[at].defines = local
  return ()
}

// One destination position may receive the same loan from several conditional source definitions.
// Compact their predicates, never their truth: neither an obsolete nor an alternative source may
// replace the other. Inherited shadow values remain separate from ordinary value holdings.
fn sameHoldingPosition(walker: &Walker, left: Carry, right: Carry, attributed: bool) -> bool {
  if left.loan != right.loan { return false }
  if !attributed { return true }
  if (left.direct && left.field != usize.MAX) != (right.direct && right.field != usize.MAX) { return false }
  if left.field == right.field { return true }
  if left.field == usize.MAX || right.field == usize.MAX { return false }
  let paths = List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths)
  let a = List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[left.field])
  let b = List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[right.field])
  return pathContains(a, b) && pathContains(b, a)
}

fn holdingSourceReaches(walker: &Walker, holding: Holding, definitions: &[u64], width: usize) -> bool {
  if holding.sourceCount == usize.ZERO { return true }
  let sources = List<HoldingSource>.asSlice(&walker.holdingSources)
  let mut at = holding.sources
  while at < holding.sources + holding.sourceCount {
    if width != usize.ZERO && reaches(definitions, width, sources[at].read, sources[at].definition) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a carried loan was read from a shadowed place, or from a value that was.
fn shadowedSource(walker: &Walker, definition: usize) -> bool {
  if definition == usize.MAX { return false }
  let source = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)[definition]
  return source.shadowed || source.inherited
}

// Records that `root`, bound at `at`, still holds `carried` in a place that was overwritten there.
effect fn shadow(walker: &mut Walker, root: usize, carried: &[Carry], at: usize) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let local = holderOf(&walker.*, root)
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < carried.length {
    let definition = List<Holding>.length(&walker.definitions)
    let sources = List<HoldingSource>.length(&walker.holdingSources)
    let mut sourceCount = usize.ZERO
    if carried[index].definition != usize.MAX {
      run List<HoldingSource>.append(&mut walker.holdingSources, HoldingSource {definition: carried[index].definition, read: carried[index].read})
      sourceCount = usize.ONE
    }
    run List<Holding>.append(&mut walker.definitions, Holding {loan: carried[index].loan, holder: local, point: at,
      sources: sources, sourceCount: sourceCount, field: carried[index].field, direct: false, shadowed: true, inherited: false})
    let mut held = List<List<usize>>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.held)
    run List<usize>.append(&mut held[local], definition)
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

effect fn inFlight(walker: &Walker, loan: &Loan, point: usize, definitions: &[u64], width: usize) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let intervals = List<Interval>.asSlice(&loan.intervals)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < intervals.length {
    let interval = intervals[at]
    if interval.from < point && point < interval.to
      && (interval.definition == usize.MAX || reaches(definitions, width, interval.read, interval.definition)) {
      if !interval.cleanup { return true }
      let before = run pathReaches(walker, interval.from, point)
      if before && run pathReaches(walker, point, interval.to) { return true }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

fn wordOf(bit: usize) -> usize { return bit / 64 }

fn maskOf(bit: usize) -> u64 { return u64.shiftLeft(1, usize.toU64(bit % 64)) }

// Backward liveness of holdings: bit `d` of `out[p]` is set when holding `d`'s holder is read on
// some path after point `p`, before it is bound again. With `fields`, only a read that may reach
// where `d` holds its loan counts, so a read of one field leaves a loan held in another field dead,
// an overwrite of the place that held it does not read it, and a shadowed holding is never read. A
// storage end needs only the loans a
// later read reaches (OWN0019); an access conflicts with every loan its holder's later use keeps,
// as BORROW-008 retains the whole holder (OWN0010, OWN0011).
effect fn liveness(walker: &Walker, width: usize, fields: bool) -> List<u64> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let all = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let held = List<List<usize>>.asSlice(&walker.held)
  let mut used = List<u64>.make()
  let mut bound = List<u64>.make()
  let mut liveIn = List<u64>.make()
  let mut liveOut = List<u64>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length * width {
    run List<u64>.append(&mut used, 0)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut bound, 0)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut liveIn, 0)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut liveOut, 0)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut point = usize.ZERO
  while point < points.length {
    if points[point].defines < held.length {
      let holdings = List<usize>.asSlice(&held[points[point].defines])
      let mut index = usize.ZERO
      while index < holdings.length {
        let mut words = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut bound)
        let slot = point * width + wordOf(holdings[index])
        words[slot] = u64.bitOr(words[slot], maskOf(holdings[index]))
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    if points[point].uses < held.length {
      let holdings = List<usize>.asSlice(&held[points[point].uses])
      let mut index = usize.ZERO
      while index < holdings.length {
        if !fields || (!all[holdings[index]].shadowed && pathsOverlap(walker, points[point].read, all[holdings[index]].field)
          && !overwrites(walker, points[point].written, all[holdings[index]].field)) {
          let mut words = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut used)
          let slot = point * width + wordOf(holdings[index])
          words[slot] = u64.bitOr(words[slot], maskOf(holdings[index]))
        }
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    point = point + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut changed = true
  while changed {
    changed = false
    point = points.length
    while point > usize.ZERO {
      point = point - usize.ONE
      let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
      let mut word = usize.ZERO
      while word < width {
        let mut out = u64.MIN
        let mut successor = usize.ZERO
        while successor < next.length {
          out = u64.bitOr(out, List<u64>.asSlice(&liveIn)[next[successor] * width + word])
          successor = successor + usize.ONE
        }
        let slot = point * width + word
        let entry = u64.bitOr(u64.bitAnd(out, u64.bitNot(List<u64>.asSlice(&bound)[slot])), List<u64>.asSlice(&used)[slot])
        let mut outs = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut liveOut)
        outs[slot] = out
        if List<u64>.asSlice(&liveIn)[slot] != entry {
          let mut ins = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut liveIn)
          ins[slot] = entry
          changed = true
        }
        word = word + usize.ONE
      }
    }
  }
  return move liveOut
}

// Whether the exact path `written` contains where a holding holds its loan, so overwriting it
// discards the loan.
fn overwrites(walker: &Walker, written: usize, field: usize) -> bool {
  if written == usize.MAX || field == usize.MAX { return false }
  let paths = List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths)
  return pathContains(List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[written]), List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[field]))
}

fn heldLive(walker: &Walker, loan: usize, liveOut: &[u64], definitions: &[u64], width: usize, point: usize) -> bool {
  let all = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < all.length {
    // A point that binds the holder again ends its earlier definitions there: the holder's later
    // reads see the new value, and cleanup of the old one is observed before the binding.
    let rebound = point < points.length && points[point].defines == all[at].holder && all[at].point != point
    if all[at].loan == loan && !all[at].inherited && !rebound && reaches(definitions, width, point, at) && reaches(liveOut, width, point, at) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// A holder has one definition per binding/replacement. A definition copied from a holder read
// exists only if its source reached that read; overwriting or consuming the holder kills its
// earlier definitions. This includes back edges, whose local bindings create new definitions.
effect fn reachingHoldings(walker: &Walker, width: usize) -> Reach
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let all = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let mut entering = List<u64>.make()
  let mut leaving = List<u64>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length * width {
    run List<u64>.append(&mut entering, 0)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut leaving, 0)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut changed = true
  while changed {
    changed = false
    let mut point = usize.ZERO
    while point < points.length {
      let mut word = usize.ZERO
      while word < width {
        let mut outs = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut leaving)
        outs[point * width + word] = List<u64>.asSlice(&entering)[point * width + word]
        word = word + usize.ONE
      }
      let mut bit = usize.ZERO
      while bit < all.length {
        let slot = point * width + wordOf(bit)
        let mut outs = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut leaving)
        if points[point].defines == all[bit].holder {
          outs[slot] = u64.bitAnd(outs[slot], u64.bitNot(maskOf(bit)))
        }
        if all[bit].point == point
          && holdingSourceReaches(walker, all[bit], List<u64>.asSlice(&entering), width) {
          outs[slot] = u64.bitOr(outs[slot], maskOf(bit))
        }
        bit = bit + usize.ONE
      }
      let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
      let mut successor = usize.ZERO
      while successor < next.length {
        word = usize.ZERO
        while word < width {
          let slot = next[successor] * width + word
          let current = List<u64>.asSlice(&entering)[slot]
          let merged = u64.bitOr(current, List<u64>.asSlice(&leaving)[point * width + word])
          if merged != current {
            let mut ins = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut entering)
            ins[slot] = merged
            changed = true
          }
          word = word + usize.ONE
        }
        successor = successor + usize.ONE
      }
      point = point + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return Reach { entering: move entering, leaving: move leaving }
}

// Graph reachability, used at storage ends rather than treating sibling arms as one numeric
// interval. The ordinary conflict walk keeps its compact interval test.
effect fn pathReaches(walker: &Walker, from: usize, to: usize) -> bool
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator {
  if from == usize.MAX || to == usize.MAX {
    return false
  }
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut seen = List<bool>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length {
    run List<bool>.append(&mut seen, false)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut queue = List<usize>.make()
  run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, from)
  let mut visited = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut seen)
  visited[from] = true
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&queue) {
    let point = List<usize>.asSlice(&queue)[at]
    if point == to {
      return true
    }
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
    let mut index = usize.ZERO
    while index < next.length {
      let mut visited = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut seen)
      if
        !visited[next[index]] {
        visited[next[index]] = true
        run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, next[index])
      }
      index = index + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

effect fn flightEnds(
  walker: &Walker,
  loan: &Loan,
  point: usize,
  definitions: &[u64],
  width: usize
) -> bool
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator {
  let intervals = List<Interval>.asSlice(&loan.intervals)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < intervals.length {
    let interval = intervals[at]
    if interval.to != point && interval.from < point && point < interval.to
      && (interval.definition == usize.MAX
      || reaches(definitions, width, interval.read, interval.definition)) {
      let arrived = run pathReaches(walker, interval.from, point)
      if arrived && run pathReaches(walker, point, interval.to) {
        return true
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Report the first authentic required holder read beyond the storage end. A carried arm/return
// result instead reports its retention boundary, as LIFE-001 and BORROW-008 require. Points are
// numbered in creation order, so a read the end reaches only around a loop's back edge was created
// before it: the scan continues from the first point once the later ones are exhausted.
effect fn expiredUse(
  walker: &Walker,
  loan: usize,
  event: &Event,
  definitions: &[u64],
  definitionWidth: usize,
  localOnly: bool
) -> Location
  ! OutOfMemoryError
  ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let all = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let mut step = usize.ONE
  while step < points.length {
    let point = (event.point + step) % points.length
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < all.length {
      if all[at].loan == loan && points[point].uses == all[at].holder && !all[at].shadowed && !all[at].inherited
        && (!localOnly || all[at].holder < walker.localCount)
        && pathsOverlap(walker, points[point].read, all[at].field)
        && !overwrites(walker, points[point].written, all[at].field)
        && reaches(definitions, definitionWidth, point, at)
        && run pathReaches(walker, event.point, point) {
        return points[point].span
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    step = step + usize.ONE
  }
  return event.span
}

// A holding of `loan` a later read needs, whose value was read out of another holder after the
// storage end at `end`, on a path that neither borrows again nor binds that holder again: the holder
// still held the loan there, so the value carries storage that has ended (OWN0019). A shadowed
// holding's place is read no more by its holder's own reads, but a value read from the place still
// carries its loans.
effect fn staleHolding(walker: &Walker, loan: usize, end: usize, live: &[u64], definitions: &[u64], width: usize) -> usize ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let all = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let created = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)[loan].created
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < all.length {
    if all[at].loan == loan && !all[at].shadowed && reaches(live, width, all[at].point, at) {
      let sources = List<HoldingSource>.asSlice(&walker.holdingSources)
      let mut source = all[at].sources
      while source < all[at].sources + all[at].sourceCount {
        if reaches(definitions, width, sources[source].read, sources[source].definition)
          && run readKeeping(walker, end, sources[source].read, created, all[sources[source].definition].holder) { return at }
        source = source + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return usize.MAX
}

// Whether `to` is reachable from `from` on a path through neither `created` nor a point that binds
// `holder` again.
effect fn readKeeping(walker: &Walker, from: usize, to: usize, created: usize, holder: usize) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if from == usize.MAX || to == usize.MAX { return false }
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut seen = List<bool>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length {
    run List<bool>.append(&mut seen, false)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut pending = List<usize>.make()
  run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, from)
  while List<usize>.length(&pending) > usize.ZERO {
    let last = List<usize>.length(&pending) - usize.ONE
    let point = List<usize>.remove(&mut pending, last)
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
    let mut successor = usize.ZERO
    while successor < next.length {
      let target = next[successor]
      if target == to { return true }
      if !List<bool>.asSlice(&seen)[target] && target != created && points[target].defines != holder {
        let mut marked = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut seen)
        marked[target] = true
        run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, target)
      }
      successor = successor + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return false
}

// Where `holding` retains its loan: the binding that retains it, as the bootstrap reports a value
// that retains expired storage; otherwise the first read of its holder that reaches the loan after
// it is bound, or `fallback`.
effect fn holdingUse(walker: &Walker, holding: usize, fallback: Location, definitions: &[u64], width: usize) -> Location
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let held = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)[holding]
  let retained = points[held.point].span
  if retained.end > retained.start { return retained }
  let mut step = usize.ONE
  while step < points.length {
    let point = (held.point + step) % points.length
    if points[point].uses == held.holder && pathsOverlap(walker, points[point].read, held.field)
      && reaches(definitions, width, point, holding) && run pathReaches(walker, held.point, point) {
      return points[point].span
    }
    step = step + usize.ONE
  }
  return fallback
}

// Whether a write of `written` replaces all of `moved`: same root, and a prefix of its path that
// names no unknown element.
fn covers(written: &Place, moved: &Place) -> bool {
  if written.root != moved.root {
    return false
  }
  let first = List<Step>.asSlice(&written.steps)
  let second = List<Step>.asSlice(&moved.steps)
  if first.length > second.length {
    return false
  }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < first.length {
    if first[at].kind == StepKind.AnyElement || !sameStep(first[at], second[at]) {
      return false
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

fn isBackEdge(walker: &Walker, from: usize, to: usize) -> bool {
  let loops = List<Loop>.asSlice(&walker.loops)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < loops.length {
    if loops[at].header == to {
      let sources = List<usize>.asSlice(&loops[at].sources)
      let mut index = usize.ZERO
      while index < sources.length {
        if sources[index] == from {
          return true
        }
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Reaching moves along forward edges: bit `m` of `entering[p]` (and `leaving[p]`) is set when move
// event `moves[m]` reaches point `p` in the same loop iteration, on a path that neither rebinds nor
// replaces its place. Repetition is checked separately at each loop header.
struct Reach {
  entering: List<u64>
  leaving: List<u64>
}

effect fn reaching(walker: &Walker, moves: &[usize], width: usize) -> Reach ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let events = List<Event>.asSlice(&walker.events)
  let mut entering = List<u64>.make()
  let mut leaving = List<u64>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length * width {
    run List<u64>.append(&mut entering, 0)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut leaving, 0)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut changed = true
  while changed {
    changed = false
    let mut point = usize.ZERO
    while point < points.length {
      let mut word = usize.ZERO
      while word < width {
        let mut outs = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut leaving)
        outs[point * width + word] = List<u64>.asSlice(&entering)[point * width + word]
        word = word + usize.ONE
      }
      let recorded = points[point].event
      let mut bit = usize.ZERO
      while bit < moves.length {
        let moved = &events[moves[bit]].place
        let mut kill = points[point].initializes == moved.root
        if recorded != usize.MAX && events[recorded].kind == Kind.Write && covers(&events[recorded].place, moved) {
          kill = true
        }
        let slot = point * width + wordOf(bit)
        let mut outs = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut leaving)
        if kill {
          outs[slot] = u64.bitAnd(outs[slot], u64.bitNot(maskOf(bit)))
        }
        if recorded == moves[bit] {
          outs[slot] = u64.bitOr(outs[slot], maskOf(bit))
        }
        bit = bit + usize.ONE
      }
      let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
      let mut successor = usize.ZERO
      while successor < next.length {
        if !isBackEdge(walker, point, next[successor]) {
          word = usize.ZERO
          while word < width {
            let slot = next[successor] * width + word
            let current = List<u64>.asSlice(&entering)[slot]
            let merged = u64.bitOr(current, List<u64>.asSlice(&leaving)[point * width + word])
            if merged != current {
              let mut ins = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut entering)
              ins[slot] = merged
              changed = true
            }
            word = word + usize.ONE
          }
        }
        successor = successor + usize.ONE
      }
      point = point + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  return Reach {entering: move entering, leaving: move leaving}
}

// Whether `place` is moved in state `state` of point `point`: some reaching move names exactly it.
fn movedIn(events: &[Event], moves: &[usize], state: &[u64], width: usize, point: usize, place: &Place) -> bool {
  let mut bit = usize.ZERO
  while bit < moves.length {
    if reaches(state, width, point, bit) && samePlace(&events[moves[bit]].place, place) {
      return true
    }
    bit = bit + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

fn samePlace(left: &Place, right: &Place) -> bool {
  return left.root == right.root && overlap(left, right) == usize.ONE
    && List<Step>.length(&left.steps) == List<Step>.length(&right.steps)
}

// Whether `local` is bound inside the loop, so it has no owner state at the header.
fn boundInside(walker: &Walker, repeat: &Loop, local: usize) -> bool {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut point = repeat.header
  while point < repeat.end {
    if points[point].initializes == local {
      return true
    }
    point = point + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a loop repeats with every `match place` refinement it uses intact: a write in the body
// to the subject of a match outside the loop invalidates a binding the next iteration uses (the
// bootstrap's `OWN0005` otherwise).
effect fn refinementRepeats(walker: &Walker, events: &[Event], repeat: &Loop, reaches: &mut List<ReplacementReach>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut use = usize.ZERO
  while use < events.length {
    let used = &events[use]
    if used.refiner != usize.MAX && used.point >= repeat.header && used.point < repeat.end
      && used.kind != Kind.End && used.kind != Kind.Expire {
      let test = refinementTest(walker, used.refiner)
      if test != usize.MAX && (test < repeat.header || test >= repeat.end) {
        let mut source = usize.ZERO
        while source < events.length {
          let written = &events[source]
          if written.point >= repeat.header && written.point < repeat.end
            && replaces(written.kind)
            && coversRefined(&written.place, &used.place, used.refinedDepth)
            && run reachesAvoiding(walker, &mut reaches.*, written.point, used.point, test) {
            return false
          }
          source = source + usize.ONE
        }
      }
    }
    use = use + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Whether a loop repeats with the same moved places of its outer locals as it enters with
// (the bootstrap's `OWN0005` otherwise).
fn compatibleHeader(walker: &Walker, events: &[Event], moves: &[usize], reach: &Reach, width: usize, repeat: &Loop) -> bool {
  if repeat.before == usize.MAX {
    return true
  }
  let leaving = List<u64>.asSlice(&reach.leaving)
  let sources = List<usize>.asSlice(&repeat.sources)
  let mut bit = usize.ZERO
  while bit < moves.length {
    let place = &events[moves[bit]].place
    if !boundInside(walker, repeat, place.root) {
      let entered = movedIn(events, moves, leaving, width, repeat.before, place)
      let mut index = usize.ZERO
      while index < sources.length {
        if movedIn(events, moves, leaving, width, sources[index], place) != entered {
          return false
        }
        index = index + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    bit = bit + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

fn reaches(entering: &[u64], width: usize, point: usize, bit: usize) -> bool {
  return u64.bitAnd(entering[point * width + wordOf(bit)], maskOf(bit)) != 0
}

/// Checks the loans of one typed body.
///
/// # Details
///
/// `owner` is the body's declaration, `locals` and `nodes` its typed locals and nodes, and `root`
/// its root node. `supplied` lists the Supplied atoms of the body's own selected application (see
/// `regionDomain`). Conflicts and uses of moved places are reported in evaluation order; the first
/// one is returned.
pub effect fn check(owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>], locals: &[Local], nodes: &[Node], root: NodeId, pending: bool,
  obligations: &[SafetyObligation], premises: &[RegionBound], cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>) -> Verdict
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut requirements = List<RetentionEdge>.make()
  if pending { requirements = run localRetentionEdges(owner, obligations) }
  // Open relations enlarge the possible source-retention graph only. The separately supplied
  // declared `premises` remain the sole assumptions for the region proof. Retained capture
  // contents make this retention summary incomplete.
  let mut retentionRelations = List<ImpliedGroup>.make()
  let mut openContents = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut settled = true
  let mut obligation = usize.ZERO
  while obligation < obligations.length {
    match &obligations[obligation] {
      SafetyObligation.RegionRelation {offered, wanted, ..} => {
        let mut members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
        run appendAtoms(&mut members, &offered)
        let mut container = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
        run appendAtoms(&mut container, &wanted)
        run List<ImpliedGroup>.append(&mut retentionRelations, ImpliedGroup {container: move container, members: move members})
      }
      SafetyObligation.Contents {region, ..} => {
        settled = false
        run appendAtoms(&mut openContents, &region)
      }
      _ => ()
    }
    obligation = obligation + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut unrun = List<bool>.make()
  let mut declared = usize.ZERO
  while declared < locals.length {
    run List<bool>.append(&mut unrun, false)
    declared = declared + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut walker = Walker {
    callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>.make(),
    unrun: move unrun,
    points: List<Point>.make(),
    loans: List<Loan>.make(),
    events: List<Event>.make(),
    frames: List<Frame>.make(),
    loops: List<Loop>.make(),
    held: List<List<usize>>.make(),
    definitions: List<Holding>.make(), holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>.make(),
    scopes: List<Scope>.make(),
    localCount: locals.length,
    cleanup: move cleanup,
    loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>.make(),
    exit: usize.ZERO,
    entry: usize.ZERO,
    outside: false,
    reason: BorrowStatus.Regions,
    guarded: List<usize>.make(),
    guardConsumed: Option<Location>.none(),
    retention: Retention.None, requirements: move requirements,
    settled: settled,
    retentionRelations: move retentionRelations, wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>.make(),
    openContents: move openContents,
    unretained: List<usize>.make(), contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), storing: false, inherited: BorrowStatus.Checked, storable: List<usize>.make(),
    refinements: List<Refinement>.make(),
    lexicalHolders: List<usize>.make(),
    paths: List<List<Step>>.make(),
    stores: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    returns: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    sealed: List<Location>.make(),
    unheld: List<Location>.make(),
    escaping: List<usize>.make(),
    supplied: run copiedRegions(supplied),
  }
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, List<Step>.make())
  run List<Scope>.append(&mut walker.scopes, Scope {roots: List<usize>.make(), expiring: List<usize>.make(), statement: false})
  walker.exit = run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX)
  let entry = run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX)
  walker.entry = entry
  let mut initialized = entry
  let mut parameter = usize.ZERO
  while parameter < locals.length {
    let mut bound = false
    let mut node = usize.ZERO
    while node < nodes.length {
      match &nodes[node].kind {
        NodeKind.LocalBinding {local, ..} => { if local.index == parameter { bound = true } }
        NodeKind.MutableBinding {local, ..} => { if local.index == parameter { bound = true } }
        _ => {}
      }
      node = node + usize.ONE
    }
    if !bound {
      run registerRoot(&mut walker, parameter)
      // Parameters and capture aliases already own their storage on entry. Record that
      // initialization just like a binding, so a branch-local descriptor does not become
      // the lower bound of its owner's availability in the finite region proof.
      initialized = run newPoint(&mut walker, initialized)
      let mut points = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
      points[initialized].initializes = parameter
    }
    parameter = parameter + usize.ONE
  }
  let flow = run visit(nodes, locals, owner, &mut walker, root, initialized)
  // A guard may inspect its arm's bindings but not consume them: a later arm still receives the
  // unchanged payload when the guard is false (MATCH-002).
  if let Option<Location>.Some {value: consumed} = &walker.guardConsumed {
    return Verdict {outcome: Outcome.Conflict, status: BorrowStatus.Regions, code: RejectionCode.GuardConsumesPattern,
      access: consumed, earlier: Option<Location>.none(), reports: List<Report>.make()}
  }
  // A loan of storage this body owns cannot outlive the body, so a retained relation that requires
  // its region to outlive a universal region is refuted, reported at the borrow as the bootstrap
  // reports the unsatisfied region bound (SEM0212). The walk records every loan even where it leaves
  // the body unchecked, and this refutation reads only loans and relations, not their flow.
  let escaping = run escapingOwnedLoan(&walker, owner, obligations, false)
  if escaping != usize.MAX {
    let all = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
    return Verdict {outcome: Outcome.Conflict, status: BorrowStatus.Regions, code: RejectionCode.UnsatisfiedLifetimeBound,
      access: all[escaping].origin, earlier: Option<Location>.none(), reports: List<Report>.make()}
  }
  // A returned value is stored in the caller's result slot, so the same refutation holds for goals
  // admitted inside a `return`. It decides a body only where the walk itself finds no conflict: the
  // walk reports a loan of body storage a returned value holds where it escapes (OWN0019).
  let mut returnedEscape = usize.MAX
  if List<StoreWindow>.length(&walker.returns) > usize.ZERO {
    returnedEscape = run escapingOwnedLoan(&walker, owner, obligations, true)
  }
  if walker.outside {
    return refutedOr(&walker, returnedEscape, verdict(Outcome.NotChecked, walker.reason))
  }
  let released = run releaseScopes(&mut walker, usize.ZERO, nodes[root.index].origin.location, flow.at)
  if walker.outside { return refutedOr(&walker, returnedEscape, verdict(Outcome.NotChecked, walker.reason)) }
  if released != usize.MAX {
    // Body statements produce no implicit escaping value. Explicit returns consume their value
    // after scope release; this statement tail may coincide with the final End safely.
    cross(&mut walker, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried))
    run consume(&mut walker, List<Carry>.asSlice(&flow.carried), released)
  }
  let exit = walker.exit
  run edge(&mut walker, released, exit)
  let definitionWidth = (List<Holding>.length(&walker.definitions) + 63) / 64
  let mut definitions = Reach {entering: List<u64>.make(), leaving: List<u64>.make()}
  // Holdings a later read of their field needs, and holdings any later use of their holder keeps.
  let mut liveOut = List<u64>.make()
  let mut keptOut = List<u64>.make()
  if definitionWidth > usize.ZERO {
    definitions = run reachingHoldings(&walker, definitionWidth)
    liveOut = run liveness(&walker, definitionWidth, true)
    keptOut = run liveness(&walker, definitionWidth, false)
  }
  let callerSources = run callerHoldingSources(&walker, List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth)
  let independentEscapes = run retainCallerSources(&mut walker, List<CallerSource>.asSlice(&callerSources),
    List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth)
  let events = List<Event>.asSlice(&walker.events)
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut moves = List<usize>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < events.length {
    if events[at].kind == Kind.Move || events[at].kind == Kind.Drop {
      run List<usize>.append(&mut moves, at)
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let moved = List<usize>.asSlice(&moves)
  let moveWidth = (moved.length + 63) / 64
  let mut reach = Reach {entering: List<u64>.make(), leaving: List<u64>.make()}
  if moveWidth > usize.ZERO {
    reach = run reaching(&walker, moved, moveWidth)
  }
  let loops = List<Loop>.asSlice(&walker.loops)
  let mut replacementReaches = List<ReplacementReach>.make()
  let mut contested = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut chains = List<UnretainedChain>.make()
  let unretained = List<usize>.asSlice(&walker.unretained)
  let mut dropped = usize.ZERO
  while dropped < unretained.length {
    run List<UnretainedChain>.append(&mut chains, run unretainedChain(&walker, owner, unretained[dropped]))
    dropped = dropped + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut checkedLoops = usize.ZERO
  let mut unknown = false
  // The conflicts found so far, in the order found. After the first, the walk goes on to report the
  // other accesses that conflict with a live loan and the storage they leave expired, as the
  // bootstrap's loan and lifetime analyses report every one; any other kind of conflict found later
  // ends the walk unreported.
  let mut reports = List<Report>.make()
  let mut stopped = false
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at <= events.length {
    // A loop header is checked in evaluation order, before the first access after it.
    while checkedLoops < loops.length && (at == events.length || loops[checkedLoops].header < events[at].point) {
      let repeats = run refinementRepeats(&walker, events, &loops[checkedLoops], &mut replacementReaches)
      if (moveWidth > usize.ZERO && !compatibleHeader(&walker, events, moved, &reach, moveWidth, &loops[checkedLoops])) || !repeats {
        let span = loops[checkedLoops].span
        if List<Report>.length(&reports) == usize.ZERO {
          return Verdict {outcome: Outcome.Conflict, status: BorrowStatus.Regions, code: RejectionCode.IncompatibleLoopHeader, access: span, earlier: Option<Location>.none(), reports: List<Report>.make()}
        }
        stopped = true
        break
      }
      checkedLoops = checkedLoops + usize.ONE
    }
    if stopped || at == events.length {
      break
    }
    let event = &events[at]
    if event.consumesTarget == usize.ONE {
      if List<Report>.length(&reports) == usize.ZERO {
        return Verdict {outcome: Outcome.Conflict, status: BorrowStatus.Regions, code: RejectionCode.OverlappingAssignment, access: event.span,
          earlier: Option<Location>.none(), reports: List<Report>.make()}
      }
      break
    }
    if event.consumesTarget != usize.ZERO {
      unknown = true
    }
    let mut bit = usize.ZERO
    while event.kind != Kind.End && event.kind != Kind.Expire && bit < moved.length {
      let source = &events[moved[bit]]
      if reaches(List<u64>.asSlice(&reach.entering), moveWidth, event.point, bit) {
        let shared = overlap(&source.place, &event.place)
        if shared != usize.ZERO {
          // A replacement of the whole moved place reinitializes it, and a drop of an owner ends
          // the parts that remain after a part was moved out.
          let ends = event.kind == Kind.Drop && covers(&event.place, &source.place)
            && List<Step>.length(&event.place.steps) < List<Step>.length(&source.place.steps)
          if !ends && (event.kind != Kind.Write || !covers(&event.place, &source.place)) {
            // Inspecting the tag of an owner reads none of its moved parts.
            let partial = event.kind == Kind.Inspect && !covers(&source.place, &event.place)
            // A write behind a moved reference uses the reference to reach its referent.
            // A runtime index may name the moved element itself, so reading or writing through it
            // uses the moved place, as the bootstrap reports (OWN0001).
            let used = shared == usize.ONE && (event.kind != Kind.Write || behind(&source.place, &event.place)) && !partial
            if used || (shared == 2 && !partial && determined(&source.place)) {
              if List<Report>.length(&reports) == usize.ZERO {
                return Verdict {outcome: Outcome.Conflict, status: BorrowStatus.Regions, code: RejectionCode.UseAfterMove, access: event.span, earlier: Option<Location>.some(source.span), reports: List<Report>.make()}
              }
              stopped = true
              break
            }
            // A partial replacement of a moved place, or an overlap decided by an unknown index.
            if !partial {
              unknown = true
            }
          }
        }
      }
      bit = bit + usize.ONE
    }
    if stopped {
      break
    }
    // A `match place` binding names the payload its match selected. Once the subject place is
    // replaced, the binding no longer denotes a place of it, as the bootstrap reports (OWN0002).
    if event.refiner != usize.MAX && event.kind != Kind.End && event.kind != Kind.Expire {
      let test = refinementTest(&walker, event.refiner)
      let mut source = usize.ZERO
      while test != usize.MAX && source < events.length {
        let written = &events[source]
        if replaces(written.kind)
          && coversRefined(&written.place, &event.place, event.refinedDepth)
          && run reachesAvoiding(&walker, &mut replacementReaches, written.point, event.point, test) {
          // The same write also meets the subject's loans, which the bootstrap reports beside it.
          if List<Report>.length(&reports) == usize.ZERO {
            run List<Report>.append(&mut reports, Report {code: RejectionCode.ExtractionBoundary, requestedExclusive: false, existingExclusive: false, access: event.span,
              related: true, earlier: written.span})
          }
          break
        }
        source = source + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    let mut index = usize.ZERO
    while index < loans.length {
      // A loan kept only by a typing relation the return-slot refutation decides is reported there
      // (SEM0212), at its borrow, rather than where the walk finds it.
      let deferred = loans[index].bound && returnedEscape != usize.MAX
      if (event.kind == Kind.End || event.kind == Kind.Expire) && loans[index].local && !deferred && covers(&event.place, &loans[index].place) {
        let carried = run flightEnds(&walker, &loans[index], event.point, List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth)
        let mut held = definitionWidth > usize.ZERO
          && heldLive(&walker, index, List<u64>.asSlice(&liveOut), List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth, event.point)
        if !held && List<bool>.asSlice(&independentEscapes)[index] {
          held = run reachesAvoiding(&walker, &mut replacementReaches, loans[index].created, event.point, usize.MAX)
        }
        let caller = run callerRetentionAt(&walker, index, event.point, List<CallerSource>.asSlice(&callerSources),
          List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth, &mut replacementReaches)
        if caller == CallerSource.Actual { held = true }
        if !held && loans[index].until != usize.MAX {
          held = run liveUntil(&walker, &mut replacementReaches, &loans[index], event.point)
        }
        let mut stale = usize.MAX
        if !carried && !held && definitionWidth > usize.ZERO {
          stale = run staleHolding(&walker, index, event.point, List<u64>.asSlice(&liveOut), List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth)
        }
        if !carried && !held && stale == usize.MAX && caller == CallerSource.Unknown { unknown = true }
        if carried || held || stale != usize.MAX {
          if loans[index].precision == LoanPrecision.Alternatives || loans[index].precision == LoanPrecision.Unknown { unknown = true } else {
            // A temporary's view carried past its owner is reported where it is first used after
            // that, as the bootstrap reports a statement temporary, unless nothing uses it again.
            let mut required = event.span
            if stale != usize.MAX {
              required = run holdingUse(&walker, stale, event.span, List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth)
            } else if !carried || temporary(nodes, loans[index].place.root) {
              required = run expiredUse(&walker, index, event, List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth, false)
            }
            run addReport(&mut reports, Report {code: expiredCode(), access: required, related: true, earlier: loans[index].origin, requestedExclusive: false, existingExclusive: false})
          }
        }
      } else if index != event.loan && !deferred && !lentTo(&loans[index], &event.binders) {
        let code = conflictCode(event.kind, loans[index].exclusive)
        if let Option<RejectionCode>.Some {value} = move code {
          let mut shared = overlap(&loans[index].place, &event.place)
          // A runtime index may name the lent element itself, so the access conflicts with the
          // loan as the bootstrap reports it (OWN0011).
          let mut indexed = shared == 2
          if shared != usize.ZERO && behind(&event.place, &loans[index].place) {
            // Replacing a reference leaves the referent it lent untouched. Consuming a known
            // shared descriptor does too: `behind` authenticates this same local's dereference
            // boundary. The referent's own loans and source obligations remain independently live.
            indexed = false
            if event.kind == Kind.Write {
              shared = usize.ZERO
            } else if event.kind == Kind.Move || event.kind == Kind.Drop {
              shared = 2
              if loans[index].precision == LoanPrecision.Exact && sharedLocalDescriptor(locals, &event.place) {
                shared = usize.ZERO
              }
            }
          }
          if shared != usize.ZERO {
            let mut live = run inFlight(&walker, &loans[index], event.point, List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth)
            if !live && definitionWidth > usize.ZERO {
              live = heldLive(&walker, index, List<u64>.asSlice(&keptOut), List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth, event.point)
            }
            // Written/capture/opaque escape reasons retain their original global constraint.
            // A new concrete caller retention instead starts at the operation that retains it;
            // a sibling or returned arm cannot extend it onto an unrelated access path.
            if !live && List<bool>.asSlice(&independentEscapes)[index] {
              live = run reachesAvoiding(&walker, &mut replacementReaches, loans[index].created, event.point, usize.MAX)
            }
            let caller = run callerRetentionAt(&walker, index, event.point, List<CallerSource>.asSlice(&callerSources),
              List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth, &mut replacementReaches)
            if caller == CallerSource.Actual { live = true }
            // An unrun `effect` block's own capture is live from where it is taken to the block's
            // scope end.
            if !live && loans[index].until != usize.MAX {
              live = run liveUntil(&walker, &mut replacementReaches, &loans[index], event.point)
            }
            // A loan a dropped loan's proof grounds on is used, through the dropped loan, wherever
            // that loan's creation reaches.
            let grounding = List<UnretainedChain>.asSlice(&chains)
            let mut chain = usize.ZERO
            while !live && chain < grounding.length {
              if listsIndex(List<usize>.asSlice(&grounding[chain].loans), index)
                && run reachesAvoiding(&walker, &mut replacementReaches, loans[grounding[chain].dropped].created, event.point, usize.MAX) {
                run appendAllAtoms(&mut contested, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&grounding[chain].regions))
              }
              chain = chain + usize.ONE
            }
            if !live && caller == CallerSource.Unknown { unknown = true }
            if live {
              // An approximate loan's conflict is not a proof either way: the body answers
              // `imprecise`, which is unchecked, never `Checked`.
              if (shared == usize.ONE || indexed) && (loans[index].precision == LoanPrecision.Exact
                || (loans[index].precision == LoanPrecision.Stored && caller == CallerSource.Actual)) {
                run addReport(&mut reports, Report {code: value, access: event.target, related: true, earlier: loans[index].origin,
                  requestedExclusive: event.kind == Kind.ExclusiveBorrow, existingExclusive: loans[index].exclusive})
                // A write, move or drop of body storage leaves a view its borrow made expired, which
                // the view's next use reports (OWN0019), as the bootstrap's lifetime analysis
                // invalidates a borrow's origin. A match binding's loan is not such an origin.
                if (event.kind == Kind.Write || event.kind == Kind.Move || event.kind == Kind.Drop)
                  && loans[index].local && loans[index].binder == usize.MAX {
                  // Only a local that holds the view reads it again; a match's bindings view their
                  // subject's place, which the access itself reports.
                  let use = run expiredUse(&walker, index, event, List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth, true)
                  if use.start != event.span.start || use.end != event.span.end {
                    run addReport(&mut reports, Report {code: expiredCode(), access: use, related: true, earlier: loans[index].origin, requestedExclusive: false, existingExclusive: false})
                  }
                }
                break
              }
              unknown = true
            }
          }
        }
      }
      index = index + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if List<Report>.length(&reports) > usize.ZERO {
    let first = List<Report>.asSlice(&reports)[usize.ZERO]
    let listed = run bySpan(List<Report>.asSlice(&reports))
    let mut earlier = Option<Location>.none()
    if first.related { earlier = Option<Location>.some(first.earlier) }
    return Verdict {outcome: Outcome.Conflict, status: BorrowStatus.Regions, code: first.code, access: first.access, earlier: move earlier,
      reports: move listed}
  }
  if walker.storing {
    return refutedOr(&walker, returnedEscape, verdict(Outcome.NotChecked, BorrowStatus.StoredLoans))
  }
  if unknown {
    return refutedOr(&walker, returnedEscape, verdict(Outcome.NotChecked, BorrowStatus.Imprecise))
  }
  if walker.inherited != BorrowStatus.Checked {
    return refutedOr(&walker, returnedEscape, verdict(Outcome.NotChecked, walker.inherited))
  }
  walker.contested = move contested
  let mut symbolic = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  let crossingsProved = run crossedRegionsProved(&walker, owner, premises, &mut symbolic)
  let mut relationsProved = !pending && crossingsProved
  if !relationsProved {
    relationsProved = run localRelationsProved(&walker, owner, obligations, premises, &mut symbolic,
      List<u64>.asSlice(&liveOut), List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions.entering), definitionWidth, !crossingsProved)
  }
  if relationsProved && run regionClosed(owner, supplied, locals, nodes) {
    return refutedOr(&walker, returnedEscape, verdict(Outcome.Clear, BorrowStatus.Checked))
  }
  return refutedOr(&walker, returnedEscape, verdict(Outcome.Clear, BorrowStatus.Regions))
}

// A caller retains the value read into its operand, not its holder's historical type. Shadow
// definitions remain in the region proof, but cannot supply that value. A copied alias follows
// each paired source/read; a read before replacement therefore survives replacement of its source.
// Holdings only refer to previously recorded definitions. Unknown or unavailable provenance stays
// Unknown rather than becoming evidence that the loan is absent.
effect fn callerHoldingSources(walker: &Walker, definitions: &[u64], width: usize) -> List<CallerSource>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let holdings = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let sources = List<HoldingSource>.asSlice(&walker.holdingSources)
  let mut states = List<CallerSource>.make()
  if List<CallerRetention>.length(&walker.callerRetentions) == usize.ZERO { return move states }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < holdings.length {
    let holding = holdings[at]
    let mut state = CallerSource.Unknown
    if holding.field != usize.MAX {
      if holding.shadowed { state = CallerSource.Absent }
      else if holding.sourceCount == usize.ZERO { state = CallerSource.Actual }
      else if holding.sources <= sources.length && holding.sourceCount <= sources.length - holding.sources {
        state = CallerSource.Absent
        let mut each = holding.sources
        while each < holding.sources + holding.sourceCount {
          let source = sources[each]
          let selected = callerSource(walker, List<CallerSource>.asSlice(&states), definitions, width, source.definition, source.read)
          if selected == CallerSource.Actual { state = CallerSource.Actual }
          else if selected == CallerSource.Unknown && state != CallerSource.Actual { state = CallerSource.Unknown }
          each = each + usize.ONE
        }
      }
    }
    run List<CallerSource>.append(&mut states, state)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move states
}

fn callerSource(walker: &Walker, sources: &[CallerSource], definitions: &[u64], width: usize,
  definition: usize, read: usize) -> CallerSource {
  // Only a fresh borrow introduces this unconditional pair; every copy/transform preserves it
  // or replaces it with a recorded Holding/read pair.
  if definition == usize.MAX && read == usize.MAX { return CallerSource.Actual }
  if definition >= sources.length || width == usize.ZERO || read >= List<Point>.length(&walker.points) {
    return CallerSource.Unknown
  }
  if !reaches(definitions, width, read, definition) { return CallerSource.Absent }
  return sources[definition]
}

// Preserve independent escape reasons separately from location-qualified caller retention.
// The aggregate flag remains conservative for region availability/release proofs. Event conflicts
// use the returned independent reasons or callerRetentionAt, never that aggregate flag alone.
// No later overwrite can cancel a call that already retained a real source.
effect fn retainCallerSources(walker: &mut Walker, sources: &[CallerSource], definitions: &[u64], width: usize) -> List<bool>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut independent = List<bool>.make()
  let original = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < original.length {
    run List<bool>.append(&mut independent, original[at].escapes)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let retained = List<CallerRetention>.asSlice(&walker.callerRetentions)
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < retained.length {
    let source = &retained[at]
    if callerSource(&walker.*, sources, definitions, width, source.definition, source.read) != CallerSource.Absent {
      let mut loans = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
      loans[source.loan].escapes = true
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move independent
}

// Both Exact and Stored caller-retained conflicts need the operation to reach the access. The
// source definition is authenticated at the operand read: Move may consume it before the call.
// Unknown source evidence can require an unchecked result, never a concrete conflict by itself.
effect fn callerRetentionAt(walker: &Walker, loan: usize, point: usize, sources: &[CallerSource], definitions: &[u64], width: usize,
  replacements: &mut List<ReplacementReach>) -> CallerSource ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let retained = List<CallerRetention>.asSlice(&walker.callerRetentions)
  let mut result = CallerSource.Absent
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < retained.length {
    let source = &retained[at]
    if source.loan == loan && run reachesAvoiding(walker, &mut replacements.*, source.point, point, usize.MAX) {
      let selected = callerSource(walker, sources, definitions, width, source.definition, source.read)
      if selected == CallerSource.Actual { return CallerSource.Actual }
      if selected == CallerSource.Unknown { result = CallerSource.Unknown }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return result
}

// The SEM0212 refutation of the loan at `escaping` (`escapingOwnedLoan`), or `otherwise` when
// `escaping` is `usize.MAX`.
fn refutedOr(walker: &Walker, escaping: usize, otherwise: Verdict) -> Verdict {
  if escaping == usize.MAX { return move otherwise }
  let all = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  return Verdict {outcome: Outcome.Conflict, status: BorrowStatus.Regions, code: RejectionCode.UnsatisfiedLifetimeBound,
    access: all[escaping].origin, earlier: Option<Location>.none(), reports: List<Report>.make()}
}

// R3 uses the Walker's points and edges. Required sets over-approximate its exact loan flow;
// available sets under-approximate storage validity. A successful inclusion is a proof. A failed
// inclusion in this conservative slice stays pending: the exact End/access walk above owns
// OWN0019/conflict diagnostics. Unknown mappings cannot upgrade a body; a complete union of
// possible loans can prove safety only when every possible source satisfies the proof.
// `required` holds the region's own requirement and every point propagated into it; `incoming` only
// the points propagated from other regions. A local region's own requirement was checked loan by
// loan against that loan's validity; propagated points must lie where every loan of the region is
// valid.
struct RegionPoints {
  region: Shared<Lifetime>
  required: List<u64>
  incoming: List<u64>
  available: List<u64>
}

struct RegionEdge {
  shorter: usize
  longer: usize
}

impl Copy for RegionEdge {}

enum RegionDomain { Universal, Local, Unknown }

fn suppliedAtom(region: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> bool {
  return Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(region, fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> bool {
    return match &atom.* { Lifetime.Supplied {..} => true _ => false }
  })
}

// Whether `region` is a borrow region of `owner`'s body.
fn regionLocal(region: &Shared<Lifetime>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  return Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(region, fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> bool {
    if let Lifetime.Local {declaration, ..} = &atom.* { return DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner) }
    return false
  })
}

effect fn copiedRegions(regions: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> List<Shared<Lifetime>> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut copied = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < regions.length {
    run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut copied, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&regions[at]))
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move copied
}

// A Supplied atom is universal only when it is one of the body's own application regions: it then
// names a caller region valid for the whole invocation, as the parameter it binds does. Supplied
// atoms carry no owner, so one from any other numbering stays unknown; the caller passes none
// when the body may hold such an atom.
fn regionDomain(region: &Shared<Lifetime>, owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> RegionDomain {
  if suppliedAtom(region) {
    if proofContains(supplied, region) { return RegionDomain.Universal }
    return RegionDomain.Unknown
  }
  return Shared<Lifetime>.with<RegionDomain>(region, fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> RegionDomain {
    return match &atom.* {
      Lifetime.Static => RegionDomain.Universal
      Lifetime.Parameter {declaration, ..} => {
        let kind = DeclarationId.kind(&declaration)
        if DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner)
          || (DeclarationId.isPrefixOf(&declaration, owner) && kind != OwnerKind.Anonymous && kind != OwnerKind.EffectBlock) {
          return RegionDomain.Universal
        }
        return RegionDomain.Unknown
      }
      Lifetime.Local {declaration, ..} => {
        if DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner) { return RegionDomain.Local }
        return RegionDomain.Unknown
      }
      _ => RegionDomain.Unknown
    }
  })
}

// The enclosing Walker bounds construction, retention and escape of the capture. This witness
// covers only finite uses in the direct nested invocation; it is never a universal premise.
fn capturedFiniteSource(region: &Shared<Lifetime>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  let kind = DeclarationId.kind(owner)
  if kind != OwnerKind.Anonymous && kind != OwnerKind.EffectBlock { return false }
  return Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(region, fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> bool {
    if let Lifetime.Local {declaration, ..} = &atom.* {
      return DeclarationId.kind(&declaration) == OwnerKind.Function
        && DeclarationId.ownerCount(&declaration) + usize.ONE == DeclarationId.ownerCount(owner)
        && DeclarationId.isPrefixOf(&declaration, owner)
    }
    return false
  })
}

// Cache completed provenance proofs by their target. Cyclic graphs are grounded separately;
// a currently visited node is never installed here as an assumed proof or a failed result.
struct SymbolicRegion {
  offered: Shared<Lifetime>
  wanted: Shared<Lifetime>
  proved: bool
}

effect fn appendNewAtoms(target: &mut List<Shared<Lifetime>>, region: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> () ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let count = Lifetime.atomCount(region)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < count {
    let atom = Lifetime.atomAt(region, at)
    if !proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&target.*), &atom) {
      run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut target.*, move atom)
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// Walks a dropped loan's provenance as symbolicParentsProved does: from its own regions through
// every loan naming a non-universal walked region to that loan's parent, and through every source
// a retention relation lets into a walked region.
effect fn unretainedChain(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, dropped: usize) -> UnretainedChain
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let relations = List<ImpliedGroup>.asSlice(&walker.retentionRelations)
  let mut chain = UnretainedChain {dropped: dropped, loans: List<usize>.make(), regions: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()}
  run List<usize>.append(&mut chain.loans, dropped)
  let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loans[dropped].regions)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < named.length {
    run appendNewAtoms(&mut chain.regions, &named[at])
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut next = usize.ZERO
  while next < List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(&chain.regions) {
    let walked = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&chain.regions)
    let region = Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&walked[next])
    if regionDomain(&region, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied)) != RegionDomain.Universal {
      at = usize.ZERO
      while at < loans.length {
        if proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loans[at].regions), &region) {
          if !listsIndex(List<usize>.asSlice(&chain.loans), at) { run List<usize>.append(&mut chain.loans, at) }
          if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: parent} = &loans[at].parent { run appendNewAtoms(&mut chain.regions, &parent) }
        }
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
      at = usize.ZERO
      while at < relations.length {
        if proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&relations[at].container), &region) {
          let members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&relations[at].members)
          let mut member = usize.ZERO
          while member < members.length {
            run appendNewAtoms(&mut chain.regions, &members[member])
            member = member + usize.ONE
          }
        }
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    next = next + usize.ONE
  }
  return move chain
}

fn listsIndex(indices: &[usize], index: usize) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < indices.length {
    if indices[at] == index { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

fn proofContains(regions: &[Shared<Lifetime>], region: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < regions.length {
    if Lifetime.equalsShared(&regions[at], region) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether the caller's 2a check (`checkDeclaredRegions`) already proved a universal relation:
// one whose whole offered side is a single declared region. A constituent of a meet that also
// holds a local atom has had no such proof, and neither has a Supplied atom, which 2a leaves
// pending; those must pass `universalRegionProved`.
fn declaredRelationProved(offered: &Shared<Lifetime>, wanted: &Shared<Lifetime>, constituents: usize) -> bool {
  return constituents == usize.ONE && !suppliedAtom(offered) && !suppliedAtom(wanted)
}

// Only authenticated scalar universals participate here. Premises come from the header proof,
// never the retained obligation list. Meets and outside-owner atoms remain pending.
effect fn universalRegionProved(owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>], offered: &Shared<Lifetime>, wanted: &Shared<Lifetime>,
  premises: &[RegionBound]) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if regionDomain(offered, owner, supplied) != RegionDomain.Universal || regionDomain(wanted, owner, supplied) != RegionDomain.Universal { return false }
  if Lifetime.equalsShared(offered, wanted) { return true }
  if Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(offered, fn(value: &Lifetime) -> bool {
    return match &value.* { Lifetime.Static => true _ => false }
  }) { return true }
  let mut reached = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut reached, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(wanted))
  let mut next = usize.ZERO
  while next < List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(&reached) {
    let entries = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&reached)
    let current = Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&entries[next])
    if Lifetime.equalsShared(offered, &current) { return true }
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < premises.length {
      let premise = &premises[at]
      if regionDomain(&premise.longer, owner, supplied) == RegionDomain.Universal
        && regionDomain(&premise.shorter, owner, supplied) == RegionDomain.Universal
        && Lifetime.equalsShared(&premise.shorter, &current)
        && !proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&reached), &premise.longer) {
        run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut reached, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&premise.longer))
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    next = next + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

fn cachedSymbolicRegion(owner: &DeclarationId, offered: &Shared<Lifetime>, wanted: &Shared<Lifetime>,
  cache: &[SymbolicRegion]) -> Option<bool> {
  let shorterLocal = regionLocal(wanted, owner)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < cache.length {
    let sameTarget = Lifetime.equalsShared(&cache[at].wanted, wanted)
      || (shorterLocal && regionLocal(&cache[at].wanted, owner))
    if sameTarget && Lifetime.equalsShared(&cache[at].offered, offered) { return Option<bool>.some(cache[at].proved) }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return Option<bool>.none()
}

// A node in an authenticated actual-parent graph; grounding alone grants no point validity.
struct SymbolicRoot {
  region: Shared<Lifetime>
  parents: List<usize>
  grounded: bool
}

effect fn symbolicRootIndex(roots: &mut List<SymbolicRoot>, region: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let entries = List<SymbolicRoot>.asSlice(&roots.*)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < entries.length {
    if Lifetime.equalsShared(&entries[at].region, region) { return at }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let selected = List<SymbolicRoot>.length(&roots.*)
  run List<SymbolicRoot>.append(&mut roots.*, SymbolicRoot {
    region: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(region), parents: List<usize>.make(), grounded: false,
  })
  return selected
}

// All parent paths must stay inside this complete provenance graph or end at a sufficient
// universal. Each reachable component must also reach a real root; a root elsewhere in the graph
// cannot justify an ungrounded sibling cycle. Static cycles from reassigning a reborrow may be
// grounded by the original reference, without assuming the cycle itself is a source of validity.
effect fn symbolicParentsProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, offered: &Shared<Lifetime>,
  wanted: &Shared<Lifetime>, premises: &[RegionBound], cache: &mut List<SymbolicRegion>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut roots = List<SymbolicRoot>.make()
  drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, offered)
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut next = usize.ZERO
  while next < List<SymbolicRoot>.length(&roots) {
    let entries = List<SymbolicRoot>.asSlice(&roots)
    let region = Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&entries[next].region)
    // A contested region is used past the body by a loan the walk dropped, after a conflicting
    // access: it outlives no universal region.
    if regionDomain(wanted, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied)) == RegionDomain.Universal
      && proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.contested), &region) { return false }
    let mut parents = List<usize>.make()
    let mut grounded = false
    let mut found = false
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < loans.length {
      let loan = &loans[at]
      if proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions), &region) {
        found = true
        if loan.local || !provable(loan.precision) { return false }
        if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
          if !Lifetime.equalsShared(&borrowed, &region) { return false }
        } else { return false }
        if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: bound} = &loan.parent {
          // A reborrow through several descriptors is bounded by their meet: every atom must
          // reach the target, and any one sufficient atom grounds this storage.
          let count = Lifetime.atomCount(&bound)
          if count == usize.ZERO { return false }
          let mut atom = usize.ZERO
          while atom < count {
            let parent = Lifetime.atomAt(&bound, atom)
            let domain = regionDomain(&parent, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied))
            if domain == RegionDomain.Universal {
              if regionDomain(wanted, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied)) == RegionDomain.Universal
                && !run universalRegionProved(owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), &parent, wanted, premises) { return false }
              grounded = true
            } else if domain == RegionDomain.Local {
              let known = cachedSymbolicRegion(owner, &parent, wanted, List<SymbolicRegion>.asSlice(&cache.*))
              if let Option<bool>.Some {value} = move known {
                if !value { return false }
                grounded = true
              } else {
                let index = run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, &parent)
                run List<usize>.append(&mut parents, index)
              }
            } else { return false }
            atom = atom + usize.ONE
          }
        } else { return false }
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    if !found { return false }
    // An open contents bound lets values of unknown regions into this region.
    if proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.openContents), &region) { return false }
    // A value can also enter this region without a loan, through a region relation such as a
    // passed reference meeting a fresh borrow in one call region. Each such source must itself
    // reach the target; it never grounds this region, so its own loans must still be found.
    let relations = List<ImpliedGroup>.asSlice(&walker.retentionRelations)
    let mut relation = usize.ZERO
    while relation < relations.length {
      if proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&relations[relation].container), &region) {
        let members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&relations[relation].members)
        let mut member = usize.ZERO
        while member < members.length {
          let source = &members[member]
          if !Lifetime.equalsShared(source, &region) {
            let domain = regionDomain(source, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied))
            if domain == RegionDomain.Universal {
              if regionDomain(wanted, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied)) == RegionDomain.Universal
                && !run universalRegionProved(owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), source, wanted, premises) { return false }
            } else if domain == RegionDomain.Local {
              let known = cachedSymbolicRegion(owner, source, wanted, List<SymbolicRegion>.asSlice(&cache.*))
              if let Option<bool>.Some {value} = move known {
                if !value { return false }
              } else {
                drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, source)
              }
            } else { return false }
          }
          member = member + usize.ONE
        }
      }
      relation = relation + usize.ONE
    }
    let mut recorded = List<SymbolicRoot>.asMutSlice(&mut roots)
    recorded[next].parents = move parents
    recorded[next].grounded = grounded
    next = next + usize.ONE
  }
  if !groundRegionParents(&mut roots) { return false }
  let entries = List<SymbolicRoot>.asSlice(&roots)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < entries.length {
    run List<SymbolicRegion>.append(&mut cache.*, SymbolicRegion {
      offered: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&entries[at].region), wanted: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(wanted), proved: true,
    })
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

fn groundRegionParents(roots: &mut List<SymbolicRoot>) -> bool {
  let mut changed = true
  while changed {
    changed = false
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < List<SymbolicRoot>.length(&roots.*) {
      let entries = List<SymbolicRoot>.asSlice(&roots.*)
      let mut grounded = entries[at].grounded
      if !grounded {
        let parents = List<usize>.asSlice(&entries[at].parents)
        let mut parent = usize.ZERO
        while parent < parents.length {
          if entries[parents[parent]].grounded { grounded = true }
          parent = parent + usize.ONE
        }
        if grounded {
          let mut recorded = List<SymbolicRoot>.asMutSlice(&mut roots.*)
          recorded[at].grounded = true
          changed = true
        }
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  let entries = List<SymbolicRoot>.asSlice(&roots.*)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < entries.length {
    if !entries[at].grounded { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// A local target asks only for a source valid throughout the finite body. A universal target
// retains its exact identity. Inner retained atoms never stand in for outer storage provenance.
effect fn symbolicRegionProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId,
  offered: &Shared<Lifetime>, wanted: &Shared<Lifetime>, premises: &[RegionBound], cache: &mut List<SymbolicRegion>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let longer = regionDomain(offered, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied))
  let shorter = regionDomain(wanted, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied))
  if longer == RegionDomain.Unknown || shorter == RegionDomain.Unknown { return false }
  if longer == RegionDomain.Universal {
    if shorter == RegionDomain.Local { return true }
    return run universalRegionProved(owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), offered, wanted, premises)
  }
  if let Option<bool>.Some {value} = move cachedSymbolicRegion(owner, offered, wanted, List<SymbolicRegion>.asSlice(&cache.*)) {
    return value
  }
  let proved = run symbolicParentsProved(walker, owner, offered, wanted, premises, &mut cache.*)
  if !proved {
    run List<SymbolicRegion>.append(&mut cache.*, SymbolicRegion {
      offered: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(offered), wanted: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(wanted), proved: false,
    })
  }
  return proved
}

// The actual parent bounds this loan's chosen outer lifetime. Such an external source is
// valid throughout the body independently of when its descriptor or this loan was created.
effect fn loanParentBoundProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, loan: &Loan,
  premises: &[RegionBound], cache: &mut List<SymbolicRegion>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if loan.local || !provable(loan.precision) { return false }
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
    if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: parent} = &loan.parent {
      // A meet of descriptor lifetimes offers the borrow only while each of them does.
      let count = Lifetime.atomCount(&parent)
      if count == usize.ZERO { return false }
      let mut atom = usize.ZERO
      while atom < count {
        let member = Lifetime.atomAt(&parent, atom)
        if !run symbolicRegionProved(walker, owner, &member, &borrowed, premises, &mut cache.*) { return false }
        atom = atom + usize.ONE
      }
      return true
    }
  }
  return false
}

effect fn crossedRegionsProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, premises: &[RegionBound],
  cache: &mut List<SymbolicRegion>) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < loans.length {
    let loan = &loans[at]
    if loan.crossed && !run loanParentBoundProved(walker, owner, loan, premises, &mut cache.*) { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Finite crossings may end at owned storage, but every actual parent path must be accounted
// for and grounded. These edges become point-set requirements, never symbolic premises or a
// universal-source cache entry. A type's inner atom cannot identify its outer source loan.
effect fn finiteParentRoots(loans: &[Loan], owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>], roots: &mut List<SymbolicRoot>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut next = usize.ZERO
  while next < List<SymbolicRoot>.length(&roots.*) {
    let entries = List<SymbolicRoot>.asSlice(&roots.*)
    let region = Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&entries[next].region)
    if !regionLocal(&region, owner) { return false }
    let mut parents = List<usize>.make()
    let mut grounded = false
    let mut found = false
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < loans.length {
      let loan = &loans[at]
      if regionsCarry(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions), &region, owner, supplied) {
        found = true
        if !provable(loan.precision) { return false }
        if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
          if !carriesRegion(&borrowed, &region, owner, supplied) { return false }
        } else { return false }
        if loan.local {
          if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {..} = &loan.parent { return false }
          grounded = true
        } else if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: bound} = &loan.parent {
          let count = Lifetime.atomCount(&bound)
          if count == usize.ZERO { return false }
          let mut atom = usize.ZERO
          while atom < count {
            let parent = Lifetime.atomAt(&bound, atom)
            let domain = regionDomain(&parent, owner, supplied)
            if domain == RegionDomain.Universal {
              grounded = true
            } else if domain == RegionDomain.Local {
              let index = run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots.*, &parent)
              run List<usize>.append(&mut parents, index)
            } else { return false }
            atom = atom + usize.ONE
          }
        } else { return false }
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    if !found { return false }
    let mut recorded = List<SymbolicRoot>.asMutSlice(&mut roots.*)
    recorded[next].parents = move parents
    recorded[next].grounded = grounded
    next = next + usize.ONE
  }
  return groundRegionParents(&mut roots.*)
}

effect fn finiteCrossingsProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, premises: &[RegionBound],
  symbolic: &mut List<SymbolicRegion>, liveOut: &[u64],
  definitions: &[u64], definitionWidth: usize, regions: &mut List<RegionPoints>, edges: &mut List<RegionEdge>, flow: &mut IntervalFlow, storage: &mut RegionAvailability) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut roots = List<SymbolicRoot>.make()
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < loans.length {
    let loan = &loans[at]
    if loan.crossed && !run loanParentBoundProved(walker, owner, loan, premises, &mut symbolic.*) {
      if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
        if localMeet(&borrowed, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied)) {
          // The meet's local constituents carry its finite requirements; its universal ones
          // outlive the body.
          let mut atom = usize.ZERO
          while atom < Lifetime.atomCount(&borrowed) {
            let member = Lifetime.atomAt(&borrowed, atom)
            if regionLocal(&member, owner) { drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, &member) }
            atom = atom + usize.ONE
          }
        } else {
          drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, &borrowed)
        }
      } else { return false }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if !run finiteParentRoots(loans, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), &mut roots) { return false }
  let entries = List<SymbolicRoot>.asSlice(&roots)
  // Record only the complete, grounded parent graph. Every edge is installed below before
  // solving; these finite facts never enter the universal-source cache.
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < entries.length {
    run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut storage.finiteParents, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&entries[at].region))
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut indices = List<usize>.make()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < entries.length {
    let index = run regionPoints(walker, owner, &entries[at].region, liveOut,
      definitions, definitionWidth, &mut regions.*, premises, &mut symbolic.*, &mut flow.*, &mut storage.*)
    if index == usize.MAX { return false }
    run List<usize>.append(&mut indices, index)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mapped = List<usize>.asSlice(&indices)
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < entries.length {
    let parents = List<usize>.asSlice(&entries[at].parents)
    let mut parent = usize.ZERO
    while parent < parents.length {
      let source = mapped[at]
      let target = mapped[parents[parent]]
      if source == target {
        // Ordinary identity goals need no propagation. An actual reborrow parent sharing its
        // atom is different: require all own points in the shared availability intersection.
        // Later incoming points already receive that check in the ordinary worklist.
        requireSharedParentPoints(&mut regions.*, source)
      } else {
        run List<RegionEdge>.append(&mut edges.*, RegionEdge {shorter: source, longer: target})
      }
      parent = parent + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

fn requireSharedParentPoints(regions: &mut List<RegionPoints>, index: usize) -> () {
  let mut entries = List<RegionPoints>.asMutSlice(&mut regions.*)
  let count = List<u64>.length(&entries[index].required)
  let mut word = usize.ZERO
  while word < count {
    let needed = List<u64>.asSlice(&entries[index].required)
    let value = needed[word]
    let mut propagated = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut entries[index].incoming)
    propagated[word] = u64.bitOr(propagated[word], value)
    word = word + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

fn includeRegionPoint(bits: &mut List<u64>, point: usize) -> bool {
  let words = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut bits.*)
  let word = wordOf(point)
  let before = words[word]
  words[word] = u64.bitOr(before, maskOf(point))
  return before != words[word]
}

fn excludeRegionPoint(bits: &mut List<u64>, point: usize) -> bool {
  let words = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut bits.*)
  let word = wordOf(point)
  let before = words[word]
  words[word] = u64.bitAnd(before, u64.bitNot(maskOf(point)))
  return before != words[word]
}

// Availability is a storage-validity must fact, separate from the actual loan's activity.
// An authenticated universal parent or complete finite parent graph can establish validity
// independently of this descriptor. Finite parent edges still bound every required point by
// the actual storage. Without either witness, creation remains the conservative lower bound on
// every path from entry; a point no path from creation reaches is available (`unreachableAvailable`).
// Real referent ends, writes, moves and drops still propagate exclusions along the CFG; neither
// the symbolic escape proof nor the Walker's conflict/liveness checks are bypassed.
effect fn localAvailable(walker: &Walker, index: usize, loan: &Loan, sourceBound: bool, ownedStart: bool,
  definitions: &[u64], definitionWidth: usize, available: &mut List<u64>) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut entered = List<usize>.make()
  // check() creates exit at zero and entry at one; neither is a separate region graph.
  if !sourceBound && !ownedStart && loan.created != usize.ONE && excludeRegionPoint(&mut available.*, usize.ONE) {
    run List<usize>.append(&mut entered, usize.ONE)
  }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&entered) {
    let point = List<usize>.asSlice(&entered)[at]
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
    let mut edge = usize.ZERO
    while edge < next.length {
      if next[edge] != loan.created && excludeRegionPoint(&mut available.*, next[edge]) {
        run List<usize>.append(&mut entered, next[edge])
      }
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut queue = List<usize>.make()
  let events = List<Event>.asSlice(&walker.events)
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < events.length {
    let event = &events[at]
    let ends = event.kind == Kind.End || event.kind == Kind.Expire || event.kind == Kind.Write
      || event.kind == Kind.Move || event.kind == Kind.Drop
    // Ending or replacing the descriptor does not end an independently bounded referent, and
    // ending a descriptor's storage never ends what it refers to: a reborrow through a reference
    // a scope or statement ends stays bounded by the loan that reference carries. Actual referent
    // events still invalidate availability, and Walker conflicts are unchanged.
    let storageEnds = event.kind == Kind.End || event.kind == Kind.Expire
    let descriptorOnly = (event.kind == Kind.Write || storageEnds || sourceBound) && behind(&event.place, &loan.place)
    if ends && !descriptorOnly && event.point != loan.created && overlap(&event.place, &loan.place) != usize.ZERO
      && excludeRegionPoint(&mut available.*, event.point) {
      run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, event.point)
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  // A referent event invalidates the loan only along paths that still hold it: each invalidated point
  // carries the holdings that still hold the loan on some path from the event. A holding ends where
  // its holder is bound again; a copy of a carried holding, or a binding of the loan while it is in
  // flight, joins them. Past a point where none is left and no value carrying the loan is in flight,
  // nothing on that path can hold it again without its creation, so no later requirement on that
  // path depends on this storage.
  let width = definitionWidth
  if width == usize.ZERO || loan.escapes || loan.until != usize.MAX {
    at = usize.ZERO
    while at < List<usize>.length(&queue) {
      let point = List<usize>.asSlice(&queue)[at]
      let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
      let mut edge = usize.ZERO
      while edge < next.length {
        if next[edge] != loan.created && excludeRegionPoint(&mut available.*, next[edge]) {
          run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, next[edge])
        }
        edge = edge + usize.ONE
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    return ()
  }
  let all = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let mut carried = List<u64>.make()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length * width { run List<u64>.append(&mut carried, 0) at = at + usize.ONE }
  // Seed each event with the holdings of this loan that reach it.
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&queue) {
    let point = List<usize>.asSlice(&queue)[at]
    let mut held = usize.ZERO
    while held < all.length {
      if all[held].loan == index && reaches(definitions, width, point, held) {
        let mut words = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut carried)
        let slot = point * width + wordOf(held)
        words[slot] = u64.bitOr(words[slot], maskOf(held))
      }
      held = held + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&queue) {
    let point = List<usize>.asSlice(&queue)[at]
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
    let flowing = withinInterval(loan, point)
    let mut edge = usize.ZERO
    while edge < next.length {
      let target = next[edge]
      if target != loan.created {
        let landing = withinInterval(loan, target)
        let mut grew = false
        let mut holds = false
        let mut held = usize.ZERO
        while held < all.length {
          let incoming = u64.bitAnd(List<u64>.asSlice(&carried)[point * width + wordOf(held)], maskOf(held)) != 0
          let rebound = points[target].defines == all[held].holder && all[held].point != target
          let mut copied = false
          if all[held].loan == index && all[held].point == target {
            copied = all[held].sourceCount == usize.ZERO && (flowing || landing)
            let sources = List<HoldingSource>.asSlice(&walker.holdingSources)
            let mut source = all[held].sources
            while source < all[held].sources + all[held].sourceCount {
              let origin = sources[source].definition
              if reaches(definitions, width, sources[source].read, origin)
                && u64.bitAnd(List<u64>.asSlice(&carried)[point * width + wordOf(origin)], maskOf(origin)) != 0 { copied = true }
              source = source + usize.ONE
            }
          }
          if (incoming && !rebound) || copied {
            holds = true
            let slot = target * width + wordOf(held)
            let before = List<u64>.asSlice(&carried)[slot]
            let mut words = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut carried)
            words[slot] = u64.bitOr(before, maskOf(held))
            if words[slot] != before { grew = true }
          }
          held = held + usize.ONE
        }
        if holds || landing {
          let excluded = excludeRegionPoint(&mut available.*, target)
          if excluded || grew { run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, target) }
        }
      }
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// Whether a value carrying `loan` may be in flight at `point`: within one of its intervals.
fn withinInterval(loan: &Loan, point: usize) -> bool {
  let intervals = List<Interval>.asSlice(&loan.intervals)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < intervals.length {
    if intervals[at].from <= point && point <= intervals[at].to { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// A loan is live only at points its creation reaches, so a point no path from its creation reaches
// places no validity requirement on it: such a point is available to the loan, whatever region
// requirement arrives there.
effect fn unreachableAvailable(walker: &Walker, created: usize, available: &mut List<u64>) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut reached = List<u64>.make()
  let mut word = usize.ZERO
  while word < List<u64>.length(&available.*) {
    run List<u64>.append(&mut reached, 0)
    word = word + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut queue = List<usize>.make()
  drop includeRegionPoint(&mut reached, created)
  run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, created)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&queue) {
    let point = List<usize>.asSlice(&queue)[at]
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
    let mut edge = usize.ZERO
    while edge < next.length {
      if includeRegionPoint(&mut reached, next[edge]) { run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, next[edge]) }
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let reachedWords = List<u64>.asSlice(&reached)
  let mut words = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut available.*)
  word = usize.ZERO
  while word < words.length {
    words[word] = u64.bitOr(words[word], u64.bitNot(reachedWords[word]))
    word = word + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// One lazy reverse CFG and one cached point set per consuming endpoint, scoped to this
// body's region proof. Traversal includes all edges, including back edges; numeric source
// ordering never decides whether a branch can reach its consumer.
struct IntervalFlow {
  offsets: List<usize>
  predecessors: List<usize>
  endpoints: List<usize>
  reaching: List<List<u64>>
}

fn emptyIntervalFlow() -> IntervalFlow {
  return IntervalFlow {offsets: List<usize>.make(), predecessors: List<usize>.make(),
    endpoints: List<usize>.make(), reaching: List<List<u64>>.make()}
}

effect fn intervalPredecessors(walker: &Walker, flow: &mut IntervalFlow) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if List<usize>.length(&flow.offsets) > usize.ZERO { return () }
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at <= points.length { run List<usize>.append(&mut flow.offsets, usize.ZERO) at = at + usize.ONE }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length {
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[at].next)
    let mut edge = usize.ZERO
    while edge < next.length {
      let mut offsets = List<usize>.asMutSlice(&mut flow.offsets)
      offsets[next[edge] + usize.ONE] = offsets[next[edge] + usize.ONE] + usize.ONE
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  at = usize.ONE
  while at <= points.length {
    let mut offsets = List<usize>.asMutSlice(&mut flow.offsets)
    offsets[at] = offsets[at] + offsets[at - usize.ONE]
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let offsets = List<usize>.asSlice(&flow.offsets)
  let edgeCount = offsets[points.length]
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < edgeCount { run List<usize>.append(&mut flow.predecessors, usize.ZERO) at = at + usize.ONE }
  let mut cursor = List<usize>.make()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length { run List<usize>.append(&mut cursor, offsets[at]) at = at + usize.ONE }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length {
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[at].next)
    let mut edge = usize.ZERO
    while edge < next.length {
      let mut positions = List<usize>.asMutSlice(&mut cursor)
      let index = positions[next[edge]]
      positions[next[edge]] = index + usize.ONE
      let mut predecessors = List<usize>.asMutSlice(&mut flow.predecessors)
      predecessors[index] = at
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

effect fn intervalEndpoint(walker: &Walker, endpoint: usize, flow: &mut IntervalFlow) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let ends = List<usize>.asSlice(&flow.endpoints)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < ends.length { if ends[at] == endpoint { return at } at = at + usize.ONE }
  run intervalPredecessors(walker, &mut flow.*)
  let mut reached = List<u64>.make()
  let words = (List<Point>.length(&walker.points) + 63) / 64
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < words { run List<u64>.append(&mut reached, 0) at = at + usize.ONE }
  drop includeRegionPoint(&mut reached, endpoint)
  let mut pending = List<usize>.make()
  run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, endpoint)
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&pending) {
    let point = List<usize>.asSlice(&pending)[at]
    let offsets = List<usize>.asSlice(&flow.offsets)
    let predecessors = List<usize>.asSlice(&flow.predecessors)
    let mut edge = offsets[point]
    while edge < offsets[point + usize.ONE] {
      let previous = predecessors[edge]
      if includeRegionPoint(&mut reached, previous) { run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, previous) }
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let index = List<usize>.length(&flow.endpoints)
  run List<usize>.append(&mut flow.endpoints, endpoint)
  run List<List<u64>>.append(&mut flow.reaching, move reached)
  return index
}

// An owned place can exist before a fresh loan is taken. Keep this storage fact separate from
// actual loan activity and from the universal-source proof. Each cached mask is a must fact:
// any entry path avoiding the root's initialization excludes every point it reaches.
struct RegionAvailability {
  roots: List<usize>
  masks: List<List<u64>>
  finiteParents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
  // Authenticated body-scoped choices have no storage source of their own. Every later
  // relation still constrains them through the same graph as actual source regions.
  choices: List<Shared<Lifetime>>
}

fn emptyRegionAvailability() -> RegionAvailability {
  return RegionAvailability {roots: List<usize>.make(), masks: List<List<u64>>.make(),
    finiteParents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), choices: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()}
}

effect fn initializedOwnedRegion(walker: &Walker, loan: &Loan, region: &Shared<Lifetime>,
  storage: &mut RegionAvailability, flow: &mut IntervalFlow) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  if !loan.local || !provable(loan.precision) { return usize.MAX }
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {..} = &loan.parent { return usize.MAX }
  // A direct borrow can be shortened to a meet. Each actual constituent still names this
  // same initialized storage; an unrelated nested lifetime does not. Authenticate membership
  // in both the sole retained lifetime and the borrow itself before using the root's must-mask.
  let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
  if named.length != usize.ONE || (!Lifetime.equalsShared(&named[0], region) && !meetMember(&named[0], region)) { return usize.MAX }
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loan.borrowed {
    if !Lifetime.equalsShared(&borrowed, region) && !meetMember(&borrowed, region) { return usize.MAX }
  } else { return usize.MAX }
  let roots = List<usize>.asSlice(&storage.roots)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < roots.length { if roots[at] == loan.place.root { return at } at = at + usize.ONE }
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let mut initialized = usize.MAX
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length {
    if points[at].initializes == loan.place.root {
      if initialized != usize.MAX { return usize.MAX }
      initialized = at
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if initialized == usize.MAX { return usize.MAX }
  // This proof authenticates one storage instance. A root rebound around a CFG cycle keeps
  // the creation lower bound; a new iteration must not revive an earlier escaped loan.
  let endpoint = run intervalEndpoint(walker, initialized, &mut flow.*)
  let reached = List<List<u64>>.asSlice(&flow.reaching)
  let paths = List<u64>.asSlice(&reached[endpoint])
  let successors = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[initialized].next)
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < successors.length {
    if u64.bitAnd(paths[wordOf(successors[at])], maskOf(successors[at])) != 0 { return usize.MAX }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut available = List<u64>.make()
  let words = (points.length + 63) / 64
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < words { run List<u64>.append(&mut available, u64.bitNot(0)) at = at + usize.ONE }
  let mut pending = List<usize>.make()
  if initialized != walker.entry && excludeRegionPoint(&mut available, walker.entry) {
    run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, walker.entry)
  }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < List<usize>.length(&pending) {
    let point = List<usize>.asSlice(&pending)[at]
    let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[point].next)
    let mut edge = usize.ZERO
    while edge < next.length {
      if next[edge] != initialized && excludeRegionPoint(&mut available, next[edge]) {
        run List<usize>.append(&mut pending, next[edge])
      }
      edge = edge + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let index = List<usize>.length(&storage.roots)
  run List<usize>.append(&mut storage.roots, loan.place.root)
  run List<List<u64>>.append(&mut storage.masks, move available)
  return index
}

// Points after this particular owned loan has ceased to inhabit any value on every path
// that created it. Paths that never created the loan impose no source-instance requirement at
// a join with a released path. A later creation or carrier reactivates the source. This is not
// storage availability: the loan's own uses must first pass the unmodified storage proof.
// Unknown sources, outward retention and parent dependencies cannot use this local release fact.
effect fn releasedLoanPoints(walker: &Walker, index: usize, definitions: &[u64], width: usize,
  needed: &[u64]) -> List<u64> ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let points = List<Point>.asSlice(&walker.points)
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let loan = &loans[index]
  let mut released = List<u64>.make()
  let words = (points.length + 63) / 64
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < words { run List<u64>.append(&mut released, 0) at = at + usize.ONE }
  if !ownedStorageLoan(loan) || loan.escapes || loan.until != usize.MAX { return move released }
  // A parent can still be needed through a child whose carrier has a different loan identity.
  // Keep its full availability constraint unless all such dependencies are accounted for.
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < loans.length {
    if at != index {
      if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: parent} = &loans[at].parent {
        let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
        let mut each = usize.ZERO
        while each < named.length {
          let mut atom = usize.ZERO
          while atom < Lifetime.atomCount(&named[each]) {
            if meetMember(&parent, &Lifetime.atomAt(&named[each], atom)) { return move released }
            atom = atom + usize.ONE
          }
          each = each + usize.ONE
        }
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let held = List<Holding>.asSlice(&walker.definitions)
  let mut occupied = List<bool>.make()
  let mut ends = List<bool>.make()
  let intervals = List<Interval>.asSlice(&loan.intervals)
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length {
    let mut carries = at == loan.created || u64.bitAnd(needed[wordOf(at)], maskOf(at)) != 0
    let mut survives = false
    let mut ended = false
    let mut each = usize.ZERO
    while each < held.length {
      if held[each].loan == index && !held[each].shadowed {
        // Incoming definitions protect the value until its overwrite; a newly bound definition
        // protects it from that point onward. Inherited values remain independent real carriers.
        let enters = width != usize.ZERO && reaches(definitions, width, at, each)
        let binds = held[each].point == at && holdingSourceReaches(walker, held[each], definitions, width)
        if enters || binds { carries = true }
        if (enters && points[at].defines != held[each].holder) || binds { survives = true }
        if enters && points[at].defines == held[each].holder && !binds { ended = true }
      }
      each = each + usize.ONE
    }
    each = usize.ZERO
    while each < intervals.length {
      let interval = intervals[each]
      if interval.to == at && interval.from <= interval.to
        && (interval.definition == usize.MAX || (width != usize.ZERO && reaches(definitions, width, interval.read, interval.definition))) { ended = true }
      each = each + usize.ONE
    }
    run List<bool>.append(&mut occupied, carries)
    run List<bool>.append(&mut ends, ended && !survives)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  // Bit 1: this path has not created the loan; bit 2: it still carries the source;
  // bit 4: it created and released the source. Joins keep every incoming possibility.
  let mut states = List<u64>.make()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length { run List<u64>.append(&mut states, 0) at = at + usize.ONE }
  let mut initial = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut states)
  initial[walker.entry] = 1
  let mut changed = true
  while changed {
    changed = false
    at = usize.ZERO
    while at < points.length {
      let incoming = List<u64>.asSlice(&states)[at]
      if incoming != 0 {
        let mut outgoing = incoming
        if at == loan.created { outgoing = 2 }
        else if List<bool>.asSlice(&occupied)[at] {
          outgoing = u64.bitOr(u64.bitAnd(incoming, 1), 2)
        }
        // Only a recorded consumption or replacement can terminate an instance. Mere absence
        // of a carrier is not release evidence, including on a cycle before initialization.
        if List<bool>.asSlice(&ends)[at] && u64.bitAnd(outgoing, 2) != 0 {
          outgoing = u64.bitOr(u64.bitAnd(outgoing, 1), 4)
        }
        let next = List<usize>.asSlice(&points[at].next)
        let mut edge = usize.ZERO
        while edge < next.length {
          let mut entries = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut states)
          let before = entries[next[edge]]
          entries[next[edge]] = u64.bitOr(before, outgoing)
          if entries[next[edge]] != before { changed = true }
          edge = edge + usize.ONE
        }
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < points.length {
    let state = List<u64>.asSlice(&states)[at]
    // A concrete release must reach the point; absence before any source was created is not
    // evidence that initialization, a write, or a storage end can be ignored.
    if !List<bool>.asSlice(&occupied)[at] && u64.bitAnd(state, 4) != 0 && u64.bitAnd(state, 2) == 0 {
      drop includeRegionPoint(&mut released, at)
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move released
}

// A local atom names the loans typing gave it: usually one borrow, but every fresh borrow of one call
// shares the call's region, and a borrow of a value retains the regions its type names. The atom
// checks each loan's own requirement against that loan's availability. Its required set is their
// union; incoming requirements must fit their availability intersection. An atom no
// loan names remains pending unless typing authenticated it as an unconstrained call-prefix
// choice. A loan typed under a `localMeet` names each of the meet's local constituents. Outside-owner,
// invocation and supplied terms and unknown mappings remain pending.
effect fn regionPoints(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, region: &Shared<Lifetime>,
  liveOut: &[u64], definitions: &[u64], definitionWidth: usize,
  regions: &mut List<RegionPoints>, premises: &[RegionBound], symbolic: &mut List<SymbolicRegion>, flow: &mut IntervalFlow, storage: &mut RegionAvailability) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let existing = List<RegionPoints>.asSlice(&regions.*)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < existing.length {
    if Lifetime.equalsShared(&existing[at].region, region) { return at }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let domain = regionDomain(region, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied))
  if domain == RegionDomain.Unknown { return usize.MAX }
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut selected = List<usize>.make()
  if domain == RegionDomain.Local {
    at = usize.ZERO
    while at < loans.length {
      if regionsCarry(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loans[at].regions), region, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied)) {
        if !provable(loans[at].precision) { return usize.MAX }
        run List<usize>.append(&mut selected, at)
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    if List<usize>.length(&selected) == usize.ZERO
      && !proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&storage.choices), region) { return usize.MAX }
  }
  let pointCount = List<Point>.length(&walker.points)
  let words = (pointCount + 63) / 64
  let mut required = List<u64>.make()
  let mut available = List<u64>.make()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < words {
    let mut initial: u64 = 0
    if domain == RegionDomain.Universal { initial = u64.bitNot(0) }
    run List<u64>.append(&mut required, initial)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut available, u64.bitNot(0))
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let chosen = List<usize>.asSlice(&selected)
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < chosen.length {
    let loan = &loans[chosen[index]]
    if loan.created >= pointCount { return usize.MAX }
    // Each loan's requirement must lie within its own validity. Its exclusions propagate on their
    // own set: a point another loan of the atom already excluded must not stop this loan's
    // propagation before its own creation point.
    let mut own = List<u64>.make()
    let mut needed = List<u64>.make()
    at = usize.ZERO
    while at < words {
      run List<u64>.append(&mut own, u64.bitNot(0))
      run List<u64>.append(&mut needed, 0)
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    let universalBound = run loanParentBoundProved(walker, owner, loan, premises, &mut symbolic.*)
    // Each nonlocal member of this graph has authenticated outer provenance. Its finite
    // parent edges constrain all incoming and own requirements to the actual source storage.
    let finiteBound = !loan.local && proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&storage.finiteParents), region)
    let sourceBound = universalBound || finiteBound
    let initialized = run initializedOwnedRegion(walker, loan, region, &mut storage.*, &mut flow.*)
    run localAvailable(walker, chosen[index], loan, sourceBound, initialized != usize.MAX, definitions, definitionWidth, &mut own)
    if initialized != usize.MAX {
      let masks = List<List<u64>>.asSlice(&storage.masks)
      let valid = List<u64>.asSlice(&masks[initialized])
      let mut ownWords = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut own)
      let mut word = usize.ZERO
      while word < words { ownWords[word] = u64.bitAnd(ownWords[word], valid[word]) word = word + usize.ONE }
    }
    drop includeRegionPoint(&mut needed, loan.created)
    let intervals = List<Interval>.asSlice(&loan.intervals)
    at = usize.ZERO
    while at < intervals.length {
      let interval = intervals[at]
      if interval.from >= pointCount || interval.to >= pointCount { return usize.MAX }
      if interval.definition == usize.MAX || reaches(definitions, definitionWidth, interval.read, interval.definition) {
        // An abandoned branch cannot carry this interval to its consumer. Cleanup observers
        // have their own intervals, and heldLive below still supplies loop-carried requirements.
        if interval.from <= interval.to {
          let endpoint = run intervalEndpoint(walker, interval.to, &mut flow.*)
          let reached = List<List<u64>>.asSlice(&flow.reaching)
          let paths = List<u64>.asSlice(&reached[endpoint])
          let mut point = interval.from
          while point <= interval.to {
            if u64.bitAnd(paths[wordOf(point)], maskOf(point)) != 0 { drop includeRegionPoint(&mut needed, point) }
            point = point + usize.ONE
          }
        }
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    if definitionWidth > usize.ZERO {
      at = usize.ZERO
      while at < pointCount {
        if heldLive(walker, chosen[index], liveOut, definitions, definitionWidth, at) {
          drop includeRegionPoint(&mut needed, at)
        }
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    run unreachableAvailable(walker, loan.created, &mut own)
    let ownWords = List<u64>.asSlice(&own)
    let neededWords = List<u64>.asSlice(&needed)
    let mut word = usize.ZERO
    while word < words {
      if u64.bitAnd(neededWords[word], u64.bitNot(ownWords[word])) != 0 { return usize.MAX }
      word = word + usize.ONE
    }
    // Incoming graph requirements can outlast this particular source instance. They constrain
    // its storage only while that instance can still inhabit a value; concrete release on every
    // creating path makes the source irrelevant there. Own uses were checked above, and the
    // release mask excludes their points, surviving holdings, parents and open-ended retention.
    // Keep every relation edge and requirement: other live sources still restrict the intersection.
    let released = run releasedLoanPoints(walker, chosen[index], definitions, definitionWidth, neededWords)
    let releasedWords = List<u64>.asSlice(&released)
    let mut all = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut available)
    let mut gathered = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut required)
    word = usize.ZERO
    while word < words {
      all[word] = u64.bitAnd(all[word], u64.bitOr(ownWords[word], releasedWords[word]))
      gathered[word] = u64.bitOr(gathered[word], neededWords[word])
      word = word + usize.ONE
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut propagated = List<u64>.make()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < words {
    run List<u64>.append(&mut propagated, 0)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let position = List<RegionPoints>.length(&regions.*)
  run List<RegionPoints>.append(&mut regions.*, RegionPoints {region: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(region),
    required: move required, incoming: move propagated, available: move available})
  return position
}

// Whether `loan` is an exact loan of storage the body owns: rooted in a local or a temporary's
// hidden owner, which ends with its statement, with no reference step and no parent region, so no
// reborrow of storage reached through a reference. A field store keeps its carriers exact
// (`LoanPrecision.Stored`), and what it borrows is unchanged.
fn ownedStorageLoan(loan: &Loan) -> bool {
  if !loan.local || (loan.precision != LoanPrecision.Exact && loan.precision != LoanPrecision.Stored) { return false }
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {..} = &loan.parent { return false }
  let steps = List<Step>.asSlice(&loan.place.steps)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < steps.length {
    if steps[at].kind == StepKind.Referent { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Records a write, through a reference or into the local `holder`, whose target's type names a
// lifetime parameter of the body or a named enclosing declaration.
effect fn recordStore(walker: &mut Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, written: &Shared<Type>, span: Location, holder: usize) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  if let Option<StoreWindow>.Some {value} = move run storeWindow(owner, written, span, holder) {
    run List<StoreWindow>.append(&mut walker.stores, move value)
  }
  return ()
}

// The window of a write at `span` whose target's type is `written`: the universal lifetime
// parameters that type names, or none when it names none.
effect fn storeWindow(owner: &DeclarationId, written: &Shared<Type>, span: Location, holder: usize) -> Option<StoreWindow>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut atoms = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run Type.regionAtoms(written, &mut atoms)
  let mut regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&atoms)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < named.length {
    let parameter = Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(&named[at], fn(value: &Lifetime) -> bool {
      return match &value.* { Lifetime.Parameter {..} => true _ => false }
    })
    if parameter && regionDomain(&named[at], owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&regions)) == RegionDomain.Universal && !proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&regions), &named[at]) {
      run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut regions, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&named[at]))
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(&regions) == usize.ZERO { return Option<StoreWindow>.none() }
  return Option<StoreWindow>.some(StoreWindow {span: span, regions: move regions, holder: holder})
}

// The operand a `move` takes, or `id` itself.
fn movedOperand(nodes: &[Node], id: NodeId) -> NodeId {
  if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Move {value, ..}, ..} = &nodes[id.index].kind { return movedOperand(nodes, value) }
  return id
}

// Whether `listed` holds `local`.
fn listsLocal(listed: &[usize], local: usize) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < listed.length {
    if listed[at] == local { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether a goal into `wanted`, admitted at `site`, belongs to a recorded write whose target's type
// names `wanted`: a write through a reference, or one into a local whose value a write through a
// reference stores; with `returned`, also a value a `return` stores in the caller's result slot. A local has one region, so every value written into it must outlive what the
// stored value must.
fn storedGoal(walker: &Walker, wanted: &Shared<Lifetime>, site: Location, returned: bool) -> bool {
  if returned && windowGoal(walker, List<StoreWindow>.asSlice(&walker.returns), wanted, site)
    && !sealedSite(walker, List<StoreWindow>.asSlice(&walker.returns), site) { return true }
  return windowGoal(walker, List<StoreWindow>.asSlice(&walker.stores), wanted, site)
}

// Whether `site` lies in the operand of a call inside a returned value whose result can retain no
// region: what reaches that call, such as a borrow passed to an inner call whose region typing
// relates to the caller's but whose value only a length or a count reads, never reaches the
// returned value, so a goal admitted there is no requirement of the result slot. Only the innermost
// `return` holding the site decides: a `return` nested in the call's operand returns its own value,
// which the call's result never receives.
fn sealedSite(walker: &Walker, windows: &[StoreWindow], site: Location) -> bool {
  let mut inner = usize.MAX
  let mut window = usize.ZERO
  while window < windows.length {
    if site.start >= windows[window].span.start && site.end <= windows[window].span.end
      && (inner == usize.MAX || (windows[window].span.start >= windows[inner].span.start
        && windows[window].span.end <= windows[inner].span.end)) {
      inner = window
    }
    window = window + usize.ONE
  }
  if inner == usize.MAX { return false }
  let returned = windows[inner].span
  let sealed = List<Location>.asSlice(&walker.sealed)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < sealed.length {
    if site.start >= sealed[at].start && site.end <= sealed[at].end
      && sealed[at].start >= returned.start && sealed[at].end <= returned.end { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether one of `windows` admits a goal into `wanted` at `site` (`storedGoal`).
fn windowGoal(walker: &Walker, windows: &[StoreWindow], wanted: &Shared<Lifetime>, site: Location) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < windows.length {
    if site.start >= windows[at].span.start && site.end <= windows[at].span.end
      && proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&windows[at].regions), wanted)
      && (windows[at].holder == usize.MAX || listsLocal(List<usize>.asSlice(&walker.escaping), windows[at].holder)) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// The first loan of storage this body owns whose region the retained relations require to outlive
// a lifetime parameter of the body or a named enclosing declaration, or `usize.MAX`. The relations
// are the body's region goals: each offered region must outlive its wanted one. A seed is a goal
// admitted inside a write whose target's type names its single wanted parameter (`storedGoal`), or,
// with `returned`, inside a `return`: the value is stored in caller storage typed at that parameter,
// directly, as the caller's result, or through a local whose value is, so every atom of its offered side must outlive it. A goal into a single atom so required passes the requirement on to
// its offered atoms. Other goals are not seeds: a call's region binding need not be minimal, so a
// goal it admits into a universal region may be longer than any solution needs, and a goal into
// 'static may be an Effect environment that a run in this body uses only finitely. A goal into a
// meet requires only the meet, so it passes nothing on, and a provisional goal waiting on an
// inferred 'static is no requirement yet. A goal admitted inside an operand its call's result cannot
// hold (`unheldSite`) relates the operand only to the call's binder, which the callee's signature
// keeps apart from its result, so it is neither a seed nor passes a requirement on; a loan made
// there may be typed at that binder, so the result's requirements are none of its own. Owned storage
// ends with the body at the latest, so a loan of it so required is never valid.
effect fn escapingOwnedLoan(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, obligations: &[SafetyObligation], returned: bool) -> usize
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut required = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  let mut changed = true
  while changed {
    changed = false
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while at < obligations.length {
      if let SafetyObligation.RegionRelation {origin, offered, wanted, inferredStatic} = &obligations[at] {
        let provisional = match &inferredStatic { Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {..} => true _ => false }
        if !provisional && !unheldSite(walker, origin.location) && Lifetime.atomCount(&wanted) == usize.ONE
          && (storedGoal(walker, &wanted, origin.location, returned) || proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&required), &wanted)) {
          let count = Lifetime.atomCount(&offered)
          let mut atom = usize.ZERO
          while atom < count {
            let member = Lifetime.atomAt(&offered, atom)
            if regionLocal(&member, owner) && !proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&required), &member) {
              run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut required, move member)
              changed = true
            }
            atom = atom + usize.ONE
          }
        }
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  let held = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&required)
  if held.length == usize.ZERO { return usize.MAX }
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut index = usize.ZERO
  while index < loans.length {
    if ownedStorageLoan(&loans[index]) && !unheldSite(walker, loans[index].origin) {
      let regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loans[index].regions)
      let mut at = usize.ZERO
      while at < regions.length {
        if proofContains(held, &regions[at]) { return index }
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    index = index + usize.ONE
  }
  return usize.MAX
}

// Worklist edges point shorter -> longer (§4.3). Keeping a boundary's edge active everywhere
// over-approximates its location-sensitive requirements. Failed inclusions therefore stay pending
// until that finer proof exists; successful inclusions discharge the complete original relation.
effect fn localRelationsProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, obligations: &[SafetyObligation],
  premises: &[RegionBound], symbolic: &mut List<SymbolicRegion>,
  liveOut: &[u64], definitions: &[u64], definitionWidth: usize, finiteCrossings: bool) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let loans = List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < loans.length {
    if !provable(loans[at].precision) { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut regions = List<RegionPoints>.make()
  let mut edges = List<RegionEdge>.make()
  let mut flow = emptyIntervalFlow()
  let mut storage = emptyRegionAvailability()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < obligations.length {
    if let SafetyObligation.RegionChoice {origin, region} = &obligations[at] {
      if !Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(&region, fn(value: &Lifetime) -> bool {
        return match &value.* {
          Lifetime.Local {declaration, ordinal} => DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner) && ordinal == origin.node
          _ => false
        }
      }) { return false }
      if !proofContains(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&storage.choices), &region) {
        run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut storage.choices, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&region))
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if finiteCrossings && !run finiteCrossingsProved(walker, owner, premises, &mut symbolic.*, liveOut,
    definitions, definitionWidth, &mut regions, &mut edges, &mut flow, &mut storage) { return false }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < obligations.length {
    match &obligations[at] {
      SafetyObligation.RegionRelation {offered, wanted, inferredStatic, ..} => {
        if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {..} = &inferredStatic { return false }
        // A meet offers a lifetime only while every constituent offers it. Decompose only
        // this offered side; every constituent still needs its own provenance and finite proof.
        let count = Lifetime.atomCount(&offered)
        if count == usize.ZERO { return false }
        let mut atom = usize.ZERO
        while atom < count {
          let member = Lifetime.atomAt(&offered, atom)
          let longer = regionDomain(&member, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied))
          // A region outlives a meet when it outlives one constituent: one it is itself, or, for an
          // authenticated universal, a region local to this body.
          if Lifetime.atomCount(&wanted) > usize.ONE
            && (meetMember(&wanted, &member) || (longer == RegionDomain.Universal && meetHoldsLocal(&wanted, owner))) {
            atom = atom + usize.ONE
            continue
          }
          let shorter = regionDomain(&wanted, owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied))
          // A caller boundary needs real storage provenance, not the identical finite point sets
          // of two distinct universal lifetimes. Every outer loan must reach a sufficient parent.
          if longer == RegionDomain.Local && shorter == RegionDomain.Universal {
            if !run symbolicRegionProved(walker, owner, &member, &wanted, premises, &mut symbolic.*) { return false }
          } else if shorter == RegionDomain.Local
            && (longer == RegionDomain.Universal
              || (longer == RegionDomain.Unknown && capturedFiniteSource(&member, owner))) {
            // An authenticated universal, or a captured local of the directly enclosing function,
            // covers finite uses in this invocation. The enclosing Walker bounds the capture's
            // construction, retention and escape; this Walker still checks conflicts and ends.
            // Captured locals stay Unknown in regionDomain: this fact must never bypass a
            // captured-local-to-parameter/static goal as a universal-to-universal relation.
          } else if longer == RegionDomain.Universal && shorter == RegionDomain.Universal {
            if !declaredRelationProved(&member, &wanted, count)
              && !run universalRegionProved(owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), &member, &wanted, premises) { return false }
          } else {
            let source = run regionPoints(walker, owner, &wanted, liveOut, definitions, definitionWidth, &mut regions, premises, &mut symbolic.*, &mut flow, &mut storage)
            let target = run regionPoints(walker, owner, &member, liveOut, definitions, definitionWidth, &mut regions, premises, &mut symbolic.*, &mut flow, &mut storage)
            if source == usize.MAX || target == usize.MAX { return false }
            run List<RegionEdge>.append(&mut edges, RegionEdge {shorter: source, longer: target})
          }
          atom = atom + usize.ONE
        }
      }
      SafetyObligation.Contents {origin, subject, region} => {
        if !finiteCaptureContents(owner, origin, &subject, &region) { return false }
      }
      SafetyObligation.UnprovedImpliedBound => { return false }
      _ => ()
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return run solveRegionRequirements(&mut regions, List<RegionEdge>.asSlice(&edges))
}

// A type chosen before this invocation cannot contain a region created inside it. This proves
// only the recorded finite capture use, never a declared Contents premise or an outward bound.
fn finiteCaptureContents(owner: &DeclarationId, origin: Origin, subject: &Shared<Type>, region: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> bool {
  let local = Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(region, fn(value: &Lifetime) -> bool {
    return match &value.* {
      Lifetime.Local {declaration, ordinal} => DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner) && ordinal == origin.node
      _ => false
    }
  })
  if !local { return false }
  return Shared<Type>.with<bool>(subject, fn(value: &Type) -> bool {
    return match &value.* {
      Type.Parameter {declaration, ..} => DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner) || namedEnclosing(&declaration, owner)
      _ => false
    }
  })
}

effect fn solveRegionRequirements(regions: &mut List<RegionPoints>, links: &[RegionEdge]) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  // Each region's own requirement reaches every region that must outlive it. One that returns to its
  // origin through a cycle of relations, as two regions related both ways do, was already checked
  // loan by loan there; checking it again against every loan of the origin would refuse a loan
  // whose own validity ends before another loan of the same region is still needed.
  let count = List<RegionPoints>.length(&regions.*)
  let mut own = List<List<u64>>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < count {
    let entries = List<RegionPoints>.asSlice(&regions.*)
    let mut words = List<u64>.make()
    let required = List<u64>.asSlice(&entries[at].required)
    let mut word = usize.ZERO
    while word < required.length { run List<u64>.append(&mut words, required[word]) word = word + usize.ONE }
    run List<List<u64>>.append(&mut own, move words)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut origin = usize.ZERO
  while origin < count {
    let mut reached = List<bool>.make()
    at = usize.ZERO
    while at < count { run List<bool>.append(&mut reached, at == origin) at = at + usize.ONE }
    let mut queue = List<usize>.make()
    run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, origin)
    let mut next = usize.ZERO
    while next < List<usize>.length(&queue) {
      let source = List<usize>.asSlice(&queue)[next]
      let mut edge = usize.ZERO
      while edge < links.length {
        let link = links[edge]
        if link.shorter == source && link.longer < count && !List<bool>.asSlice(&reached)[link.longer] {
          let mut marked = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut reached)
          marked[link.longer] = true
          run List<usize>.append(&mut queue, link.longer)
        }
        edge = edge + usize.ONE
      }
      next = next + usize.ONE
    }
    let sourceWords = List<u64>.asSlice(&List<List<u64>>.asSlice(&own)[origin])
    let flags = List<bool>.asSlice(&reached)
    at = usize.ZERO
    while at < count {
      if at != origin && flags[at] {
        let mut entries = List<RegionPoints>.asMutSlice(&mut regions.*)
        let mut word = usize.ZERO
        while word < sourceWords.length {
          let mut words = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut entries[at].required)
          words[word] = u64.bitOr(words[word], sourceWords[word])
          let mut arrived = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut entries[at].incoming)
          arrived[word] = u64.bitOr(arrived[word], sourceWords[word])
          word = word + usize.ONE
        }
      }
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
    origin = origin + usize.ONE
  }
  let solved = List<RegionPoints>.asSlice(&regions.*)
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < solved.length {
    let arrivedWords = List<u64>.asSlice(&solved[at].incoming)
    let available = List<u64>.asSlice(&solved[at].available)
    let mut word = usize.ZERO
    while word < arrivedWords.length {
      if u64.bitAnd(arrivedWords[word], u64.bitNot(available[word])) != 0 { return false }
      word = word + usize.ONE
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

/// Whether every region a body's locals and values name is closed for this body: `'static`, a
/// universal region chosen before the body runs, or a loan region of the body itself, so its loans
/// and their scopes are the whole region proof.
///
/// # Details
///
/// Storage-end events prove local validity on every outgoing path. Reaching definitions and
/// backward liveness decide which holder loans are required; in-flight joins and cleanup use the
/// graph's actual paths. A referent loan crossing a boundary remains external to this local proof.
/// Universal regions are the lifetime parameters of this declaration and of every named declaration
/// enclosing it (an impl's parameters in a method, an enclosing function's in an anonymous body),
/// and an anonymous body's invocation binders. A local region of an enclosing named body is a capture
/// dependency: the enclosing body bounds its formation and retention with its own points, and
/// this body proves only its own uses (R3 amendment 4). Owned body storage cannot outlive the
/// body. An inferred region can satisfy a universal bound only through the separate symbolic
/// source proof; classifying its atoms here does not prove that bound. A callable contract's
/// invocation binders describe future calls, so a nested callable's own parameters are closed
/// wherever its value is held, as in an Effect application that carries it, and an invocation
/// region is closed where it occurs only inside the callables a type holds. A parent's binder in
/// an escaped child's contract is not the child's own and stays open. Exact callable lifetime and
/// row application arguments are selection metadata; Type.bodyRegionAtoms still checks their
/// contracts, captures and type evidence. A Supplied atom is closed only when it is one of
/// `supplied`, the body's own selected application regions; any other remains open. Callee
/// contracts and outside-body type parameters cannot smuggle in a fresh body-local region.
pub effect fn regionClosed(owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>], locals: &[Local], nodes: &[Node]) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < locals.length {
    if !run typeRegionClosed(&locals[at].ty, owner, supplied) {
      return false
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < nodes.length {
    if let NodeKind.Expression {ty, ..} = &nodes[at].kind {
      if !run typeRegionClosed(&ty, owner, supplied) {
        return false
      }
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Whether `declaration` is a named declaration enclosing `owner`: an impl around a method, or the
// function around an anonymous body. An enclosing anonymous body's own binders and locals stay open,
// so a literal nested in another literal proves nothing about its enclosing literal.
fn namedEnclosing(declaration: &DeclarationId, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  let kind = DeclarationId.kind(declaration)
  return kind != OwnerKind.Anonymous && kind != OwnerKind.EffectBlock && DeclarationId.isPrefixOf(declaration, owner)
}

// Where a call can keep a loan one operand carries: `Local` also when the operand holds none of it.
fn keptSink(paths: &[List<Step>], loan: &Loan, owner: &DeclarationId, carry: Carry, sink: &OperandSink, located: &mut bool) -> CallSink {
  let origin = loan.origin
  // An operand whose type names only `'static` holds no loan of the body unless typing gave that
  // loan a `'static` region; one the walk carries into it otherwise is not part of its value.
  let regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
  if !sink.holds && (regions.length == usize.ZERO || !staticRegions(&loan.regions)) { return CallSink.Local }
  let mut kept = sink.whole
  let mut approximate = sink.wholeApproximate
  let mut own = origin.start == sink.span.start && origin.end == sink.span.end
  if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: region} = &sink.view {
    let typed = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&loan.regions)
    let mut at = usize.ZERO
    while !own && at < typed.length {
      own = Lifetime.equalsShared(&typed[at], &region)
      at = at + usize.ONE
    }
  }
  let mut positioned = false
  if own {
    kept = sink.outer
    approximate = sink.outerApproximate
  } else {
    positioned = narrowSlots(paths, carry, loan, sink, &mut kept, &mut approximate)
  }
  // A structural slot is the actual destination of this carried value after coercion. Without
  // that correspondence, local region names alone cannot establish a universal retention path.
  if !own && !positioned && kept == CallSink.Universal && typedLocally(&loan.regions, owner) { kept = CallSink.Unknown }
  // An approximate channel's universal region may be longer than any binding needs: only a loan
  // typing gave a universal region is held to it, and any other leaves the body unchecked.
  if kept != CallSink.Universal && approximate == CallSink.Universal {
    if universalRegions(&loan.regions, owner) {
      kept = CallSink.Universal
    } else {
      kept = CallSink.Unknown
    }
  } else if kept == CallSink.Local && approximate == CallSink.Unknown {
    kept = CallSink.Unknown
  }
  located.* = positioned || (own && carry.direct && carry.field == usize.ZERO)
  return kept
}

// Completed classifications and their actual-slot witnesses share carry order. Parent
// closure may promote a sink, but never manufactures a structural-slot witness.
struct RetainedSinks {
  sinks: List<CallSink>
  located: List<bool>
}

// Classifies operand retention without mutating loans. A reborrow keeps its parent's storage
// borrowed while it lives, so a loan of body storage
// that the parent regions of an escaping loan reach among those its operand carries escapes with
// it, wherever typing placed it. Any other loan that reaches a call this walk cannot describe keeps
// the body from being Checked; the walk goes on, so a definite conflict among exact loans, such as
// an escaping loan of body storage that ends, still rejects it. Each carry is judged by
// `sinks[only]`, or by its own operand's sink when `only` is `usize.MAX`; a carry with no sink is
// kept nowhere.
effect fn retainedSinks(loans: &[Loan], paths: &[List<Step>], owner: &DeclarationId, carries: &[Carry], sinks: &[OperandSink], only: usize) -> RetainedSinks
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut kept = List<CallSink>.make()
  let mut escaping = List<usize>.make()
  let mut located = List<bool>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carries.length {
    let mut operand = only
    if operand == usize.MAX { operand = carries[at].operand }
    let mut decided = CallSink.Local
    let mut exactSlot = false
    if operand < sinks.length { decided = keptSink(paths, &loans[carries[at].loan], owner, carries[at], &sinks[operand], &mut exactSlot) }
    run List<bool>.append(&mut located, exactSlot)
    run List<CallSink>.append(&mut kept, decided)
    if decided == CallSink.Universal { run List<usize>.append(&mut escaping, at) }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut reached = List<bool>.make()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carries.length {
    run List<bool>.append(&mut reached, List<CallSink>.asSlice(&kept)[at] == CallSink.Universal)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut next = usize.ZERO
  while next < List<usize>.length(&escaping) {
    let child = List<usize>.asSlice(&escaping)[next]
    if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: parent} = &loans[carries[child].loan].parent {
      at = usize.ZERO
      while at < carries.length {
        let seen = List<bool>.asSlice(&reached)[at]
        if !seen && (only != usize.MAX || carries[at].operand == carries[child].operand) {
          if let Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.Some {value: borrowed} = &loans[carries[at].loan].borrowed {
            if meetMember(&parent, &borrowed) {
              let mut marked = List<bool>.asMutSlice(&mut reached)
              marked[at] = true
              run List<usize>.append(&mut escaping, at)
              // Storage this body owns cannot outlive it. A reborrow through a reference keeps its
              // own judgment: the region proof bounds the caller storage it reaches.
              if loans[carries[at].loan].local {
                let mut decisions = List<CallSink>.asMutSlice(&mut kept)
                decisions[at] = CallSink.Universal
              }
            }
          }
        }
        at = at + usize.ONE
      }
    }
    next = next + usize.ONE
  }
  return RetainedSinks {sinks: move kept, located: move located}
}

// Apply the completed retention decision at the original call point, before result
// consumption/classification. Parent closure observes the pre-effect loan state; precise
// caller sources are validated later against the operand read's reaching definitions.
effect fn keepCarried(walker: &mut Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, carries: &[Carry], sinks: &[OperandSink], only: usize, point: usize) -> ()
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let kept = run retainedSinks(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), List<List<Step>>.asSlice(&walker.paths), owner, carries, sinks, only)
  let decisions = List<CallSink>.asSlice(&kept.sinks)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < carries.length {
    if decisions[at] == CallSink.Universal {
      let mut all = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
      // Stored preserves exact source flow, but only a known actual signature slot authenticates
      // its retention beyond this point. Alternatives and Unknown never gain this evidence.
      if List<bool>.asSlice(&kept.located)[at] && carries[at].field != usize.MAX && point != usize.MAX
        && (all[carries[at].loan].precision == LoanPrecision.Exact || all[carries[at].loan].precision == LoanPrecision.Stored) {
        run List<CallerRetention>.append(&mut walker.callerRetentions, CallerRetention {
          loan: carries[at].loan, point: point, definition: carries[at].definition, read: carries[at].read})
      } else {
        all[carries[at].loan].escapes = true
      }
    } else if decisions[at] == CallSink.Unknown {
      walker.storing = true
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

// A known value path identifies the slot carrying a loan even after region shortening or
// projection changes its referent type. Unknown paths retain the whole-operand judgment unless
// the reference's own type rules out a slot; opaque contents never establish an exact position.
fn narrowSlots(paths: &[List<Step>], carry: Carry, loan: &Loan, sink: &OperandSink, kept: &mut CallSink, approximate: &mut CallSink) -> bool {
  let slots = List<SlotSink>.asSlice(&sink.slots)
  if sink.undescribed || slots.length == usize.ZERO { return false }
  let mut occupied = false
  let mut positioned = false
  let mut uncertain = false
  let mut precise = CallSink.Local
  let mut wider = CallSink.Local
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < slots.length {
    let mut matched = SlotPath.Unknown
    if carry.field != usize.MAX {
      matched = transferSlotPath(List<Step>.asSlice(&paths[carry.field]), List<KeptStep>.asSlice(&slots[at].path), slots[at].view)
    }
    let mut fits = matched == SlotPath.Same
    if matched == SlotPath.Unknown {
      if !carry.direct { return false }
      if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value: referent} = &loan.referent {
        fits = Type.mayHoldLoan(slots[at].view, &slots[at].referent, slots[at].exclusive, &referent, loan.exclusive)
      }
    }
    if fits {
      occupied = true
      if matched == SlotPath.Same && slots[at].view { positioned = true }
      if matched == SlotPath.Unknown || !slots[at].view { uncertain = true }
      let mut slotKept = slots[at].kept
      let mut slotApproximate = slots[at].approximate
      if !slots[at].view {
        slotKept = sink.whole
        slotApproximate = sink.wholeApproximate
      }
      precise = joinSinks(precise, slotKept)
      wider = joinSinks(wider, slotApproximate)
    }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  if !occupied { return false }
  kept.* = precise
  approximate.* = wider
  return positioned && !uncertain
}

// The longer of two sinks: unknown over universal over local.
fn joinSinks(left: CallSink, right: CallSink) -> CallSink {
  if left == CallSink.Unknown || right == CallSink.Unknown { return CallSink.Unknown }
  if left == CallSink.Universal || right == CallSink.Universal { return CallSink.Universal }
  return CallSink.Local
}

// Whether a region atom is chosen before the body runs and outlives it: `'static`, or a lifetime
// parameter of the body or of a named declaration enclosing it.
fn universalAtom(region: &Lifetime, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  return match &region.* {
    Lifetime.Static => true
    Lifetime.Parameter {declaration, ..} => DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner) || namedEnclosing(&declaration, owner)
    _ => false
  }
}

// Whether any of `regions` outlives the body: an intersection does only when every member does.
fn universalRegions(regions: &List<Shared<Lifetime>>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(regions)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < named.length {
    if Lifetime.allAtoms(&named[at], fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> bool { return universalAtom(atom, owner) }) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether `value` names regions and every one of them is a lifetime parameter that outlives the
// body. A value typed at 'static keeps only what is valid for 'static, which a body loan never is.
effect fn universallyTyped(value: &Shared<Type>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let mut atoms = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run Type.regionAtoms(value, &mut atoms)
  let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&atoms)
  if named.length == usize.ZERO { return false }
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < named.length {
    let parameter = Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(&named[at], fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> bool {
      return match &atom.* { Lifetime.Parameter {..} => universalAtom(atom, owner) _ => false }
    })
    if !parameter { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Whether typing gave a loan regions, none of which outlives the body.
fn typedLocally(regions: &List<Shared<Lifetime>>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  return List<Shared<Lifetime>>.length(regions) != usize.ZERO && !universalRegions(regions, owner)
}

// Whether every one of `regions` is `'static`.
fn staticRegions(regions: &List<Shared<Lifetime>>) -> bool {
  let named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(regions)
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < named.length {
    if !Lifetime.allAtoms(&named[at], fn(atom: &Lifetime) -> bool { return match &atom.* { Lifetime.Static => true _ => false } }) { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}

// Where a call can keep an operand once it returns: in storage that outlives the caller's body, only
// within it, or somewhere this walk has no record to tell.
enum CallSink { Local, Universal, Unknown }

// What a call can keep of one operand (R3 amendment 4). `whole` answers for loans the operand
// carries in; `outer` answers for the loan the operand's own borrow creates, which the callee holds
// only as the reference it receives.
struct OperandSink {
  outer: CallSink
  whole: CallSink
  // Where a channel the analysis only approximates can also keep the operand (KeptRegions).
  outerApproximate: CallSink
  wholeApproximate: CallSink
  span: Location
  // Whether the operand's type can hold a loan of the body: it names a region other than `'static`
  // or a type parameter, or typing recorded none.
  holds: bool
  // The operand's own region when it is a view: a carried loan typed at it is the view's own borrow,
  // made earlier as when a call returns a view of its argument, so it is judged as `outer`.
  view: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>
  // Where the callee can keep a loan by where it lies in the operand (`KeptSlot`), or none.
  slots: List<SlotSink>
  // Whether the call could not describe the operand at all.
  undescribed: bool
}

// One `KeptSlot` of an operand: whether a loan can lie there and where the callee keeps it then. An
// opaque slot keeps a loan wherever the whole operand does.
struct SlotSink {
  path: List<KeptStep>
  view: bool
  referent: Shared<Type>
  exclusive: bool
  kept: CallSink
  approximate: CallSink
}

// An approximate channel's sink: unknown where the call could not describe the operand at all.
fn approximateSink(regions: &List<Shared<Lifetime>>, undescribed: bool, owner: &DeclarationId) -> CallSink {
  if undescribed { return CallSink.Unknown }
  return regionSink(regions, owner)
}

fn regionSink(regions: &List<Shared<Lifetime>>, owner: &DeclarationId) -> CallSink {
  if universalRegions(regions, owner) { return CallSink.Universal }
  return CallSink.Local
}

// What a call recorded it can keep of its operands, or none for a call this walk cannot see into.
// An immediate run walks as the call it executes.
fn callKept(nodes: &[Node], call: NodeId) -> Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>> {
  return match &nodes[call.index].kind {
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Run {value, access}, ..} => {
      if access == RunAccess.Immediate { return callKept(nodes, value) }
      return Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.none()
    }
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.StagedCallable {retention, ..}, ..} => Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.some(Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.clone(&retention.kept))
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.DirectCall {kept, ..}, ..} => Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.some(Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.clone(&kept))
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.InterfaceCall {kept, ..}, ..} => Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.some(Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.clone(&kept))
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.CallableCall {kept, ..}, ..} => Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.some(Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.clone(&kept))
    NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Aggregate {section, ..}, ..} => match &section {
      Option<SectionRetention>.Some {value} => Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.some(Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.clone(&value.kept))
      Option<SectionRetention>.None => Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.none()
    }
    _ => Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.none()
  }
}

effect fn operandSinks(nodes: &[Node], call: NodeId, arguments: &[NodeId], owner: &DeclarationId) -> List<OperandSink>
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut sinks = List<OperandSink>.make()
  let recorded = callKept(nodes, call)
  // A call with no record, an intrinsic or foreign one, can keep an operand only in storage
  // another operand reaches, so it is undescribed only when some operand names a universal region
  // where it can store; a callable operand stores only where its contract's parameters reach. Its signature is fixed, and a loan of the body never has the body's type
  // parameter as its type.
  let mut reaches = false
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < arguments.length {
    let mut stored = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
    if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, arguments[at]) {
      run Type.callableStoredRegions(&value, &mut stored)
    }
    if universalRegions(&stored, owner) { reaches = true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut unrecorded = CallSink.Local
  if reaches { unrecorded = CallSink.Unknown }
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < arguments.length {
    // A stage captures a suffix of its selected signature. The base callable occupies value 0,
    // but is not a parameter of that signature and has no corresponding entry.
    let mut position = at
    if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.StagedCallable {retention, ..}, ..} = &nodes[call.index].kind {
      position = usize.MAX
      if at != usize.ZERO { position = retention.first + at - usize.ONE }
    }
    if let NodeKind.Expression {form: Expression.Aggregate {section, ..}, ..} = &nodes[call.index].kind {
      if let Option<SectionRetention>.Some {value} = &section { position = value.first + at }
    }
    let span = nodes[arguments[at].index].origin.location
    let mut holds = true
    let mut view = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
    if let Option<Shared<Type>>.Some {value} = move expressionType(nodes, arguments[at]) {
      view = Type.viewRegion(&value)
      let mut named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
      run Type.regionAtoms(&value, &mut named)
      let generic = run Type.namesTypeParameter(&value)
      holds = generic || !staticRegions(&named)
    }
    let mut sink = OperandSink {outer: unrecorded, whole: unrecorded, outerApproximate: unrecorded, wholeApproximate: unrecorded,
      span: span, holds: holds, view: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none(), slots: List<SlotSink>.make(), undescribed: false}
    if let Option<Shared<List<KeptRegions>>>.Some {value: kept} = &recorded {
      let listed = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<usize>(&kept, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> usize { return List<KeptRegions>.length(values) })
      if position < listed {
        sink = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<OperandSink>(&kept, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> OperandSink {
          let entries = List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)
          return OperandSink {outer: regionSink(&entries[position].outer, owner), whole: regionSink(&entries[position].whole, owner),
            outerApproximate: approximateSink(&entries[position].outerApproximate, entries[position].undescribed, owner),
            wholeApproximate: approximateSink(&entries[position].wholeApproximate, entries[position].undescribed, owner),
            span: span, holds: holds, view: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none(), slots: List<SlotSink>.make(),
            undescribed: entries[position].undescribed}
        })
        let count = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<usize>(&kept, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> usize {
          let entries = List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)
          return List<KeptSlot>.length(&entries[position].slots)
        })
        let mut index = usize.ZERO
        while index < count {
          let mut slot = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<SlotSink>(&kept, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> SlotSink {
            let entries = List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)
            let listed = List<KeptSlot>.asSlice(&entries[position].slots)
            return SlotSink {path: List<KeptStep>.make(), view: listed[index].view, referent: Shared<Type>.clone(&listed[index].referent), exclusive: listed[index].exclusive,
              kept: regionSink(&listed[index].kept, owner), approximate: approximateSink(&listed[index].keptApproximate, entries[position].undescribed, owner)}
          })
          let length = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<usize>(&kept, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> usize {
            return List<KeptStep>.length(&List<KeptSlot>.asSlice(&List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)[position].slots)[index].path)
          })
          let mut step = usize.ZERO
          while step < length {
            let value = Shared<List<KeptRegions>>.with<KeptStep>(&kept, fn(values: &List<KeptRegions>) -> KeptStep {
              return List<KeptStep>.asSlice(&List<KeptSlot>.asSlice(&List<KeptRegions>.asSlice(values)[position].slots)[index].path)[step]
            })
            run List<KeptStep>.append(&mut slot.path, value)
            step = step + usize.ONE
          }
          run List<SlotSink>.append(&mut sink.slots, move slot)
          index = index + usize.ONE
        }
      }
    }
    sink.view = move view
    run List<OperandSink>.append(&mut sinks, move sink)
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return move sinks
}

// Whether any of `atoms` is an invocation region.
fn anyInvocationAtom(atoms: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < atoms.length {
    if Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(&atoms[at], fn(region: &Lifetime) -> bool { return match &region.* { Lifetime.Invocation {..} => true _ => false } }) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

// Whether `declaration` is one of the callable values a type holds (`Type.appendCallableTargets`).
fn namesTarget(targets: &[DeclarationId], declaration: &DeclarationId) -> bool {
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < targets.length {
    if DeclarationId.equals(&targets[at], declaration) { return true }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return false
}

effect fn typeRegionClosed(ty: &Shared<Type>, owner: &DeclarationId, supplied: &[Shared<Lifetime>]) -> bool ! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut atoms = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run Type.bodyRegionAtoms(ty, &mut atoms)
  let listed = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&atoms)
  let kind = DeclarationId.kind(owner)
  let anonymous = kind == OwnerKind.Anonymous || kind == OwnerKind.EffectBlock
  let callable = Shared<Type>.with<bool>(ty, callableValue)
  let mut nested = List<DeclarationId>.make()
  run Type.appendCallableTargets(ty, &mut nested)
  let targets = List<DeclarationId>.asSlice(&nested)
  // An invocation region describes a callable's future calls only inside that callable: one the type
  // names outside every callable it holds is open.
  let mut outside = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run Type.regionAtomsOutsideCallables(ty, &mut outside)
  let invocationOutside = anyInvocationAtom(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&outside))
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < listed.length {
    if suppliedAtom(&listed[at]) {
      if !proofContains(supplied, &listed[at]) { return false }
      at = at + usize.ONE
      continue
    }
    let closed = Shared<Lifetime>.with<bool>(&listed[at], fn(region: &Lifetime) -> bool {
      return match &region.* {
        Lifetime.Static => true
        Lifetime.Local {declaration, ..} => DeclarationId.equals(&declaration, owner) || namedEnclosing(&declaration, owner)
        Lifetime.Parameter {declaration, ..} => DeclarationId.isPrefixOf(&declaration, owner)
          || (callable && DeclarationId.isPrefixOf(owner, &declaration))
          || (DeclarationId.isPrefixOf(owner, &declaration) && namesTarget(targets, &declaration))
        Lifetime.Invocation {..} => anonymous || callable || !invocationOutside
        _ => false
      }
    })
    if !closed { return false }
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return true
}


test effect fn regionWorklistPropagatesThroughCycles() -> () ! OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run regionWorklistClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn regionWorklistClaims() -> () ! OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut regions = List<RegionPoints>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 3 {
    let mut required = List<u64>.make()
    let mut available = List<u64>.make()
    let mut seed: u64 = 0
    let mut permitted: u64 = 2
    if at == 2 { seed = 2 }
    if at == usize.ZERO { permitted = 0 }
    let mut propagated = List<u64>.make()
    run List<u64>.append(&mut required, seed)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut propagated, 0)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut available, permitted)
    // The set solver uses opaque region indices; domain authentication is tested by source Cases.
    run List<RegionPoints>.append(&mut regions, RegionPoints {
      region: run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Invocation {ordinal: at}), required: move required, incoming: move propagated,
      available: move available})
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut edges = List<RegionEdge>.make()
  run List<RegionEdge>.append(&mut edges, RegionEdge {shorter: 1, longer: 0})
  run List<RegionEdge>.append(&mut edges, RegionEdge {shorter: 2, longer: 1})
  run List<RegionEdge>.append(&mut edges, RegionEdge {shorter: 1, longer: 2})
  let impossible = run solveRegionRequirements(&mut regions, List<RegionEdge>.asSlice(&edges))
  run Testing.expect(!impossible, "a required point reaches an unavailable region through a transitive cycle")
  let solved = List<RegionPoints>.asSlice(&regions)
  let first = List<u64>.asSlice(&solved[usize.ZERO].required)
  let required = first[usize.ZERO]
  run Testing.expect(required == 2, "requirements propagate from shorter to longer even after its first queue visit")
  let mut entries = List<RegionPoints>.asMutSlice(&mut regions)
  let mut permitted = List<u64>.asMutSlice(&mut entries[usize.ZERO].available)
  permitted[usize.ZERO] = 2
  let possible = run solveRegionRequirements(&mut regions, List<RegionEdge>.asSlice(&edges))
  run Testing.expect(possible, "the same obligations are proved when all propagated points are available")

  // A's own seed was checked loan by loan: returning through A <-> B must not
  // check it against A's aggregate availability. A foreign seed still must fit.
  // Each solve mutates required/incoming, so the two controls start from fresh state.
  let mut foreign = usize.ZERO
  while foreign < 2 {
    let mut cycle = List<RegionPoints>.make()
    let mut region = usize.ZERO
    while region < 2 {
      let mut seed: u64 = 2
      let mut permitted: u64 = 0
      if region == usize.ONE {
        seed = 0
        if foreign == usize.ONE { seed = 4 }
        permitted = 2
      }
      let mut required = List<u64>.make()
      let mut incoming = List<u64>.make()
      let mut available = List<u64>.make()
      run List<u64>.append(&mut required, seed)
      run List<u64>.append(&mut incoming, 0)
      run List<u64>.append(&mut available, permitted)
      run List<RegionPoints>.append(&mut cycle, RegionPoints {
        region: run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Invocation {ordinal: region}),
        required: move required, incoming: move incoming, available: move available})
      region = region + usize.ONE
    }
    let mut relations = List<RegionEdge>.make()
    run List<RegionEdge>.append(&mut relations, RegionEdge {shorter: 0, longer: 1})
    run List<RegionEdge>.append(&mut relations, RegionEdge {shorter: 1, longer: 0})
    let proved = run solveRegionRequirements(&mut cycle, List<RegionEdge>.asSlice(&relations))
    if foreign == usize.ZERO {
      run Testing.expect(proved, "a region's own requirement cannot invalidate it by returning through a cycle")
    } else {
      run Testing.expect(!proved, "a foreign requirement still fails when the cycle reaches an unavailable point")
    }
    foreign = foreign + usize.ONE
  }
  return ()
}

test effect fn regionWrappedIntervalRequiresLiveHolderPoints() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run wrappedRegionClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn wrappedRegionClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let module = run ModuleId.make(b"test", b"r3", b"loop.silk")
  let owner = run DeclarationId.fromParts(move module, List<OwnerStep>.make())
  let region = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let mut walker = Walker {
    callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>.make(),
    unrun: List<bool>.make(), points: List<Point>.make(), loans: List<Loan>.make(), events: List<Event>.make(),
    frames: List<Frame>.make(), loops: List<Loop>.make(), held: List<List<usize>>.make(),
    definitions: List<Holding>.make(), holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>.make(), scopes: List<Scope>.make(), localCount: 1,
    cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>.make(), loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>.make(), exit: 0, entry: 1,
    outside: false, reason: BorrowStatus.Regions, guarded: List<usize>.make(),
    guardConsumed: Option<Location>.none(), retention: Retention.None, requirements: List<RetentionEdge>.make(),
    settled: true, retentionRelations: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>.make(), openContents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), unretained: List<usize>.make(), contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), storing: false, inherited: BorrowStatus.Checked, storable: List<usize>.make(),
    refinements: List<Refinement>.make(), lexicalHolders: List<usize>.make(),
    paths: List<List<Step>>.make(),
    stores: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    returns: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    sealed: List<Location>.make(),
    unheld: List<Location>.make(),
    escaping: List<usize>.make(),
    supplied: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(),
  }
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, List<Step>.make())
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 5 { drop run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX) at = at + 1 }
  run edge(&mut walker, 1, 2)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 3)
  run edge(&mut walker, 3, 4)
  run edge(&mut walker, 4, 2)
  run edge(&mut walker, 4, 0)
  let mut intervals = List<Interval>.make()
  run List<Interval>.append(&mut intervals, Interval {from: 4, to: 2, definition: 0, read: 2, cleanup: false})
  let mut named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut named, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&region))
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, Loan {
    place: Place {root: 0, steps: List<Step>.make()}, exclusive: false,
    origin: Location.make(0, 1), intervals: move intervals, precision: LoanPrecision.Exact,
    regions: move named, local: true, borrowed: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&region)),
    parent: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none(), crossed: false, created: 1, escapes: false, binder: usize.MAX, block: usize.MAX, until: usize.MAX,
    referent: Option<Shared<Type>>.none(), bound: false,
  })
  run List<Holding>.append(&mut walker.definitions, Holding {loan: 0, holder: 0, point: 4, sources: usize.ZERO, sourceCount: usize.ZERO, field: usize.MAX, direct: false,
    shadowed: false, inherited: false})
  // A definition created at the bottom of the loop reaches the next header read. There is no
  // numeric interior in [4, 2]; only heldLive supplies points 2 and 3 to the region requirement.
  let mut definitions = List<u64>.make()
  let mut live = List<u64>.make()
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 5 {
    let mut present: u64 = 0
    if at == 2 || at == 3 { present = 1 }
    run List<u64>.append(&mut definitions, present)
    run List<u64>.append(&mut live, present)
    at = at + 1
  }
  let mut regions = List<RegionPoints>.make()
  let premises = List<RegionBound>.make()
  let mut symbolic = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  let mut flow = emptyIntervalFlow()
  let mut storage = emptyRegionAvailability()
  let found = run regionPoints(&walker, &owner, &region, 
    List<u64>.asSlice(&live), List<u64>.asSlice(&definitions), 1, &mut regions,
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic, &mut flow, &mut storage)
  run Testing.expect(found != usize.MAX, "the exact loop holder has available storage")
  let entries = List<RegionPoints>.asSlice(&regions)
  let required = List<u64>.asSlice(&entries[found].required)
  run Testing.expect(u64.bitAnd(required[0], 12) == 12,
    "wrapped intervals retain their back-edge holder points; removing heldLive loses this requirement")
  return ()
}

test effect fn symbolicRegionRootsRequireEveryParent() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run symbolicRootClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn symbolicTestLoan(region: &Shared<Lifetime>, parent: &Shared<Lifetime>, local: bool) -> Loan
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let mut regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut regions, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(region))
  return Loan {place: Place {root: 0, steps: List<Step>.make()}, exclusive: false,
    origin: Location.make(0, 1), intervals: List<Interval>.make(), precision: LoanPrecision.Exact,
    regions: move regions, local: local, borrowed: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(region)),
    parent: Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(parent)), crossed: true, created: 1, escapes: false, binder: usize.MAX, block: usize.MAX, until: usize.MAX,
    referent: Option<Shared<Type>>.none(), bound: false}
}

effect fn symbolicRootClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let module = run ModuleId.make(b"test", b"r3", b"symbolic.silk")
  let mut owners = List<OwnerStep>.make()
  run List<OwnerStep>.append(&mut owners, OwnerStep {kind: OwnerKind.Function,
    name: Option<Bytes>.some(run Bytes.copy(b"caller")), occurrence: 0})
  let owner = run DeclarationId.fromParts(move module, move owners)
  let first = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let second = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let a = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let b = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let mut walker = Walker {
    callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>.make(),
    unrun: List<bool>.make(), points: List<Point>.make(), loans: List<Loan>.make(), events: List<Event>.make(),
    frames: List<Frame>.make(), loops: List<Loop>.make(), held: List<List<usize>>.make(),
    definitions: List<Holding>.make(), holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>.make(), scopes: List<Scope>.make(), localCount: 1,
    cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>.make(), loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>.make(), exit: 0, entry: 1,
    outside: false, reason: BorrowStatus.Regions, guarded: List<usize>.make(),
    guardConsumed: Option<Location>.none(), retention: Retention.None, requirements: List<RetentionEdge>.make(),
    settled: true, retentionRelations: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>.make(), openContents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), unretained: List<usize>.make(), contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), storing: false, inherited: BorrowStatus.Checked, storable: List<usize>.make(),
    refinements: List<Refinement>.make(), lexicalHolders: List<usize>.make(),
    paths: List<List<Step>>.make(),
    stores: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    returns: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    sealed: List<Location>.make(),
    unheld: List<Location>.make(),
    escaping: List<usize>.make(),
    supplied: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(),
  }
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, List<Step>.make())
  let premises = List<RegionBound>.make()
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&first, &second, false))
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&second, &first, false))
  let mut cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(!run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &a, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "an ungrounded reborrow cycle cannot establish a caller lifetime")
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&second, &a, false))
  cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &a, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "a reborrow cycle is proved when every branch stays grounded in the matching universal parent")
  let mut alternatives = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  alternatives[2].precision = LoanPrecision.Alternatives
  cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &a, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "a complete possible-source union proves a bound only through all of its roots")
  let mut unresolved = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  unresolved[2].precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown
  cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(!run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &a, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "unknown retention cannot acquire a proof from another complete branch")
  let mut exact = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  exact[2].precision = LoanPrecision.Exact
  cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(!run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &b, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "a cached proof for one universal does not prove another universal")
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&first, &b, false))
  cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(!run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &a, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "every loan sharing an inference region must have a sufficient parent")
  let mut changed = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  changed[3].parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&a))
  cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &a, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "a shared region is proved when every one of its parents reaches the requested universal")
  let mut owned = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  owned[3].local = true
  cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(!run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &a, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "owned storage cannot acquire a universal validity bound from a named parent")
  let mut restored = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  restored[3].local = false
  let third = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 2})
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&first, &third, false))
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&third, &third, false))
  cache = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(!run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &first, &a, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut cache),
    "a grounded branch cannot justify another branch that ends in an ungrounded cycle")
  return ()
}


test effect fn retainedParentClosureUsesActualBorrowProvenance() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run retainedParentClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn retainedParentClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let module = run ModuleId.make(b"test", b"r3", b"retained-parent.silk")
  let mut owners = List<OwnerStep>.make()
  run List<OwnerStep>.append(&mut owners, OwnerStep {kind: OwnerKind.Function,
    name: Option<Bytes>.some(run Bytes.copy(b"caller")), occurrence: 0})
  let owner = run DeclarationId.fromParts(move module, move owners)
  let a = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let b = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let c = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 2})
  let universal = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let mut loans = List<Loan>.make()
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&a, &universal, false))
  let mut shelf = run symbolicTestLoan(&b, &universal, true)
  shelf.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut shelf.regions, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&a))
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut loans, move shelf)
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&c, &a, false))
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&a, &universal, false))
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 4 {
    run List<Carry>.append(&mut carried, Carry {loan: at, since: 0, operand: at,
      definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, field: usize.MAX, direct: false})
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  let mut result = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut result, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&b))
  let owned = run retainedParents(List<Loan>.asSlice(&loans), List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried),
    List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&result))
  let included = List<bool>.asSlice(&owned)
  run Testing.expect(!included[0] && included[1] && !included[2] && !included[3],
    "an owned outer borrow's retained inner atom is not an actual parent edge (Shelf guard)")
  result = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut result, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&c))
  let child = run retainedParents(List<Loan>.asSlice(&loans), List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried),
    List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&result))
  let ancestors = List<bool>.asSlice(&child)
  run Testing.expect(ancestors[0] && !ancestors[1] && ancestors[2] && ancestors[3],
    "every carried source sharing the actual parent atom remains in the possible-source union")
  return ()
}


test effect fn capturedFiniteSourcesAuthenticateExactDirectOwners() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run capturedFiniteOwnerClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn capturedTestOwner(path: &[u8], depth: usize) -> DeclarationId
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let module = run ModuleId.make(b"test", b"r3", path)
  let mut owners = List<OwnerStep>.make()
  run List<OwnerStep>.append(&mut owners, OwnerStep {kind: OwnerKind.Function,
    name: Option<Bytes>.some(run Bytes.copy(b"sameName")), occurrence: usize.ZERO})
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < depth {
    run List<OwnerStep>.append(&mut owners, OwnerStep {kind: OwnerKind.Anonymous,
      name: Option<Bytes>.none(), occurrence: usize.ZERO})
    at = at + usize.ONE
  }
  return run DeclarationId.fromParts(move module, move owners)
}

effect fn capturedFiniteOwnerClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"capture.silk", usize.ZERO)
  let child = run capturedTestOwner(b"capture.silk", usize.ONE)
  let grandchild = run capturedTestOwner(b"capture.silk", 2)
  let foreign = run capturedTestOwner(b"other.silk", usize.ZERO)
  let local = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let unrelated = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: move foreign, ordinal: 0})
  let nested = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&child), ordinal: 0})
  run Testing.expect(capturedFiniteSource(&local, &child),
    "the direct enclosing named function authenticates its captured local")
  run Testing.expect(!capturedFiniteSource(&unrelated, &child),
    "a same-spelled function and local ordinal in another module are not the captured source")
  run Testing.expect(!capturedFiniteSource(&local, &grandchild) && !capturedFiniteSource(&nested, &grandchild),
    "unsupported anonymous-in-anonymous nesting cannot inherit a finite-source witness")
  run Testing.expect(regionDomain(&local, &child, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make())) == RegionDomain.Unknown,
    "finite capture coverage is directional and never a universal lifetime classification")
  return ()
}

test effect fn suppliedRegionsAreUniversalOnlyWhenTheBodysOwn() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run suppliedRegionClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn suppliedRegionClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"supplied.silk", usize.ZERO)
  let own = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Supplied {ordinal: 0})
  let other = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Supplied {ordinal: 1})
  let declared = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let alsoDeclared = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let forever = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Static)
  let mut supplied = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut supplied, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&own))
  let listed = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&supplied)
  let none = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run Testing.expect(regionDomain(&own, &owner, listed) == RegionDomain.Universal
    && regionDomain(&other, &owner, listed) == RegionDomain.Unknown
    && regionDomain(&own, &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&none)) == RegionDomain.Unknown,
    "only a Supplied atom of the body's own application is universal; any other numbering stays unknown")
  run Testing.expect(declaredRelationProved(&declared, &alsoDeclared, usize.ONE)
    && !declaredRelationProved(&own, &declared, usize.ONE) && !declaredRelationProved(&declared, &own, usize.ONE)
    && !declaredRelationProved(&declared, &alsoDeclared, 2),
    "the declared-region check proves neither a Supplied side nor a meet constituent")
  let mut both = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut both, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&own))
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut both, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&other))
  let bothListed = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&both)
  let mut premises = List<RegionBound>.make()
  run List<RegionBound>.append(&mut premises, RegionBound {longer: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&declared), shorter: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&alsoDeclared)})
  let bounds = List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises)
  let itself = run universalRegionProved(&owner, bothListed, &own, &own, bounds)
  let fromStatic = run universalRegionProved(&owner, bothListed, &forever, &own, bounds)
  let toOther = run universalRegionProved(&owner, bothListed, &own, &other, bounds)
  let toStatic = run universalRegionProved(&owner, bothListed, &own, &forever, bounds)
  let toDeclared = run universalRegionProved(&owner, bothListed, &own, &declared, bounds)
  run Testing.expect(itself && fromStatic && !toOther && !toStatic && !toDeclared,
    "a Supplied region outlives only itself: no premise relates it to another Supplied, 'static or a declared region")
  return ()
}

test effect fn requiredRetentionKeepsNamespacesAndOuterLoansDistinct() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run requiredRetentionClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn requiredRetentionClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let module = run ModuleId.make(b"test", b"r3", b"requirements.silk")
  let owner = run DeclarationId.fromParts(move module, List<OwnerStep>.make())
  let otherModule = run ModuleId.make(b"test", b"r3", b"other-requirements.silk")
  let other = run DeclarationId.fromParts(move otherModule, List<OwnerStep>.make())
  let source = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let extent = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let foreign = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&other), ordinal: 0})
  let universal = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  run Testing.expect(retentionOrdinal(&foreign, &owner) == usize.MAX, "a matching ordinal in a different owner is not a local requirement")
  run Testing.expect(retentionOrdinal(&universal, &owner) == usize.MAX, "a parameter is not a local requirement")
  let mut obligations = List<SafetyObligation>.make()
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, retentionTestRelation(&source, &extent, false))
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, retentionTestRelation(&foreign, &extent, false))
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, retentionTestRelation(&source, &universal, false))
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, retentionTestRelation(&source, &extent, true))
  let admitted = run localRetentionEdges(&owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&obligations))
  run Testing.expect(List<RetentionEdge>.length(&admitted) == 1,
    "foreign, outward and unresolved inferred-static relations cannot supply finite retention edges")
  let mut required = List<usize>.make()
  run List<usize>.append(&mut required, 0)
  let mut outer = run symbolicTestLoan(&extent, &universal, false)
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut outer.regions, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&source))
  run Testing.expect(!requiredLoan(&outer, &owner, List<usize>.asSlice(&required)),
    "an inner retained atom does not turn its outer storage loan into the required source")
  let actual = run symbolicTestLoan(&source, &universal, false)
  run Testing.expect(requiredLoan(&actual, &owner, List<usize>.asSlice(&required)), "the actual outer source remains required")
  let mut unknown = run symbolicTestLoan(&source, &universal, false)
  unknown.regions = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run Testing.expect(!requiredLoan(&unknown, &owner, List<usize>.asSlice(&required)), "an empty region mapping supplies no retention evidence")
  let mut loans = List<Loan>.make()
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut loans, move actual)
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  run List<Carry>.append(&mut carried, Carry {loan: 0, since: 1, operand: 0, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, field: usize.MAX, direct: false})
  let mut named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut named, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&extent))
  let mut edges = List<RetentionEdge>.make()
  run List<RetentionEdge>.append(&mut edges, RetentionEdge {source: 0, extent: 1})
  run List<RetentionEdge>.append(&mut edges, RetentionEdge {source: 1, extent: 0})
  let closure = run requiredRetainedRegions(List<Loan>.asSlice(&loans), List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried),
    List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), &owner, List<RetentionEdge>.asSlice(&edges))
  run Testing.expect(retentionListed(List<usize>.asSlice(&closure), 0), "a local validity cycle retains the source without proving availability")
  return ()
}

fn retentionTestRelation(source: &Shared<Lifetime>, extent: &Shared<Lifetime>, unresolved: bool) -> SafetyObligation {
  let mut inferred = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  if unresolved { inferred = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(source)) }
  return SafetyObligation.RegionRelation {origin: Origin {node: 0, location: Location.make(0, 1)},
    offered: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(source), wanted: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(extent), inferredStatic: move inferred}
}

test effect fn finiteContentsAuthenticateSubjectAndCaptureSite() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  let mut typeTable = TypeTable.make()
  return run finiteContentsClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Types>(&mut typeTable) |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn finiteContentsClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator | &mut Types {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"contents.silk", 0)
  let child = run capturedTestOwner(b"contents.silk", 1)
  let nested = run capturedTestOwner(b"contents.silk", 2)
  let foreign = run capturedTestOwner(b"other-contents.silk", 0)
  let parameter = run Types.intern(Type.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let unrelated = run Types.intern(Type.Parameter {declaration: move foreign, ordinal: 0})
  let anonymous = run Types.intern(Type.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&child), ordinal: 0})
  let concrete = run Types.intern(Type.Unit)
  let local = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 3})
  let captured = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&child), ordinal: 3})
  let nestedLocal = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&nested), ordinal: 3})
  let fixed = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Static)
  let origin = Origin {node: 3, location: Location.make(0, 1)}
  let otherSite = Origin {node: 4, location: Location.make(0, 1)}
  run Testing.expect(finiteCaptureContents(&owner, origin, &parameter, &local), "the invocation's parameter covers its finite capture use")
  run Testing.expect(finiteCaptureContents(&child, origin, &parameter, &captured), "a named enclosing function's type parameter remains available in the anonymous invocation")
  run Testing.expect(!finiteCaptureContents(&owner, origin, &unrelated, &local), "a same-ordinal foreign type parameter supplies no evidence")
  run Testing.expect(!finiteCaptureContents(&owner, otherSite, &parameter, &local), "a different capture origin is not this finite obligation")
  run Testing.expect(!finiteCaptureContents(&owner, origin, &parameter, &captured), "the target must belong to the checked body")
  run Testing.expect(!finiteCaptureContents(&owner, origin, &parameter, &fixed), "finite availability never proves T:static")
  run Testing.expect(!finiteCaptureContents(&owner, origin, &concrete, &local), "arbitrary concrete contents require their separate loan proof")
  run Testing.expect(!finiteCaptureContents(&nested, origin, &anonymous, &nestedLocal), "an enclosing anonymous owner's parameters do not gain a nested-body rule")
  return ()
}

test effect fn descriptorReleaseRequiresCompleteExactSources() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run descriptorSourceClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn descriptorSourceClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"descriptor.silk", 0)
  let other = run capturedTestOwner(b"other-descriptor.silk", 0)
  let inner = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let outer = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let foreign = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: move other, ordinal: 1})
  let mut descriptor = run symbolicTestLoan(&outer, &inner, true)
  descriptor.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  let mut named = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut named, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&inner))
  let mut required = List<usize>.make()
  run Testing.expect(unneededOwnedLoan(&descriptor, &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), List<usize>.asSlice(&required), false),
    "an exact unmatched descriptor is eligible only after a separate complete-source proof")
  run Testing.expect(!unneededOwnedLoan(&descriptor, &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), List<usize>.asSlice(&required), true),
    "an actual ancestor of a retained source cannot be released")
  run List<usize>.append(&mut required, 1)
  run Testing.expect(!unneededOwnedLoan(&descriptor, &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), List<usize>.asSlice(&required), false),
    "a source required by an outer-to-inner goal remains retained")
  required = List<usize>.make()
  descriptor.precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown
  run Testing.expect(!unneededOwnedLoan(&descriptor, &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), List<usize>.asSlice(&required), false), "prior Unknown is never repaired by descriptor release")
  descriptor.precision = LoanPrecision.Alternatives
  run Testing.expect(!unneededOwnedLoan(&descriptor, &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), List<usize>.asSlice(&required), false), "prior Alternatives remains a possible source")
  let mut unrelated = run symbolicTestLoan(&foreign, &inner, true)
  unrelated.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  run Testing.expect(!unneededOwnedLoan(&unrelated, &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), List<usize>.asSlice(&required), false), "a foreign owner with the same ordinal supplies no local descriptor proof")
  let mut loans = List<Loan>.make()
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&inner, &inner, true))
  let mut carried = List<Carry>.make()
  run List<Carry>.append(&mut carried, Carry {loan: 0, since: 1, operand: 0, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, field: usize.MAX, direct: false})
  run Testing.expect(completeLocalResultSources(List<Loan>.asSlice(&loans), List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried), List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make())), "the exact actual source covers this local result")
  let mut listed = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut loans)
  listed[0].precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown
  run Testing.expect(!completeLocalResultSources(List<Loan>.asSlice(&loans), List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried), List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make())), "an unknown source cannot make result provenance complete")
  let mut exact = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut loans)
  exact[0].precision = LoanPrecision.Exact
  exact[0].borrowed = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&outer))
  run Testing.expect(!completeLocalResultSources(List<Loan>.asSlice(&loans), List<Carry>.asSlice(&carried), List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&named), &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make())), "a retained inner atom alone does not identify the actual source loan")
  return ()
}

test effect fn finiteParentsRequireGroundingAndLiveStorage() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run finiteParentClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn finiteParentClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"finite-parents.silk", 0)
  let foreignOwner = run capturedTestOwner(b"foreign-parents.silk", 0)
  let first = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let second = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let third = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 2})
  let foreign = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: move foreignOwner, ordinal: 0})
  let universal = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let mut walker = Walker {
    callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>.make(),
    unrun: List<bool>.make(), points: List<Point>.make(), loans: List<Loan>.make(), events: List<Event>.make(),
    frames: List<Frame>.make(), loops: List<Loop>.make(), held: List<List<usize>>.make(),
    definitions: List<Holding>.make(), holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>.make(), scopes: List<Scope>.make(), localCount: 2,
    cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>.make(), loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>.make(), exit: 0, entry: 1,
    outside: false, reason: BorrowStatus.Regions, guarded: List<usize>.make(),
    guardConsumed: Option<Location>.none(), retention: Retention.None, requirements: List<RetentionEdge>.make(),
    settled: true, retentionRelations: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>.make(), openContents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), unretained: List<usize>.make(), contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), storing: false, inherited: BorrowStatus.Checked, storable: List<usize>.make(),
    refinements: List<Refinement>.make(), lexicalHolders: List<usize>.make(),
    paths: List<List<Step>>.make(),
    stores: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    returns: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    sealed: List<Location>.make(),
    unheld: List<Location>.make(),
    escaping: List<usize>.make(),
    supplied: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(),
  }
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, List<Step>.make())
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 5 { drop run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX) at = at + usize.ONE }
  run edge(&mut walker, 1, 2)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 3)
  run edge(&mut walker, 3, 4)
  run edge(&mut walker, 4, 0)
  let mut root = run symbolicTestLoan(&first, &universal, true)
  root.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  root.crossed = false
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move root)
  let mut child = run symbolicTestLoan(&second, &first, false)
  child.place.root = 1
  run List<Step>.append(&mut child.place.steps, referent())
  child.created = 2
  run List<Interval>.append(&mut child.intervals, Interval {from: 2, to: 3, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, cleanup: false})
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move child)
  run List<Event>.append(&mut walker.events, Event {point: 3, place: Place {root: 0, steps: List<Step>.make()},
    kind: Kind.End, span: Location.make(0, 1), target: Location.make(0, 1), loan: usize.MAX, consumesTarget: 0,
    refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: 0, binders: List<usize>.make()})
  let emptyGoals = List<SafetyObligation>.make()
  let premises = List<RegionBound>.make()
  let words = List<u64>.make()
  let mut symbolic = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  run Testing.expect(!run localRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&emptyGoals),
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic,  List<u64>.asSlice(&words),
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, true),
    "a crossed child's required point must fit its owned parent's availability even with no typing goals")
  let mut descriptor = List<Event>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.events)
  descriptor[0].place.root = 1
  run Testing.expect(run localRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&emptyGoals),
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic,  List<u64>.asSlice(&words),
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, true),
    "ending a temporary descriptor preserves a finite child whose actual owned source stays alive")
  let mut referentEnd = List<Event>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.events)
  run List<Step>.append(&mut referentEnd[0].place.steps, referent())
  run Testing.expect(!run localRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&emptyGoals),
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic,  List<u64>.asSlice(&words),
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, true),
    "a finite parent proof never ignores an actual referent end")
  List<Event>.clear(&mut walker.events)
  run Testing.expect(run localRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&emptyGoals),
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic,  List<u64>.asSlice(&words),
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, true),
    "the finite crossing is proved when the actual owned parent remains valid")
  run Testing.expect(!run symbolicRegionProved(&walker, &owner, &second, &universal,
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic),
    "finite success never installs a universal-source proof for owned storage")
  let mut shared = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  shared[1].borrowed = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&first))
  let mut names = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asMutSlice(&mut shared[1].regions)
  names[0] = Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&first)
  run Testing.expect(run localRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&emptyGoals),
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic,  List<u64>.asSlice(&words),
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, true),
    "a shared parent atom remains grounded in its live owned source before the reborrow is created")
  run List<Event>.append(&mut walker.events, Event {point: 3, place: Place {root: 0, steps: List<Step>.make()},
    kind: Kind.End, span: Location.make(0, 1), target: Location.make(0, 1), loan: usize.MAX, consumesTarget: 0,
    refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: 0, binders: List<usize>.make()})
  run Testing.expect(!run localRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&emptyGoals),
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic,  List<u64>.asSlice(&words),
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, true),
    "a shared parent atom cannot erase the requirement to check every source's availability")
  List<Event>.clear(&mut walker.events)
  let mut restored = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  restored[1].borrowed = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&second))
  let mut original = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asMutSlice(&mut restored[1].regions)
  original[0] = Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&second)
  // Duplicate child regions retain every actual parent path, including an ungrounded sibling.
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&second, &third, false))
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, run symbolicTestLoan(&third, &third, false))
  let mut roots = List<SymbolicRoot>.make()
  drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, &second)
  run Testing.expect(!run finiteParentRoots(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), &mut roots),
    "a grounded branch cannot justify another source trapped in an ungrounded cycle")
  let mut grounded = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  grounded[3].local = true
  grounded[3].parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  roots = List<SymbolicRoot>.make()
  drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, &second)
  run Testing.expect(run finiteParentRoots(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), &mut roots),
    "all actual parents of a duplicated region can be grounded separately")
  let mut uncertain = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  uncertain[3].precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown
  roots = List<SymbolicRoot>.make()
  drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, &second)
  run Testing.expect(!run finiteParentRoots(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), &mut roots),
    "one Unknown actual source blocks the complete finite parent proof")
  let mut changed = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  changed[3].precision = LoanPrecision.Exact
  changed[2].parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&foreign))
  roots = List<SymbolicRoot>.make()
  drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, &second)
  run Testing.expect(!run finiteParentRoots(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), &mut roots),
    "an equal ordinal in a foreign owner is not a local parent")
  let mut innerOnly = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  innerOnly[2].parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&first))
  innerOnly[2].borrowed = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&third))
  roots = List<SymbolicRoot>.make()
  drop run symbolicRootIndex(&mut roots, &second)
  run Testing.expect(!run finiteParentRoots(List<Loan>.asSlice(&walker.loans), &owner, List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&walker.supplied), &mut roots),
    "a stored inner atom alone cannot supply actual outer loan identity")
  return ()
}


test effect fn intervalRequirementsKeepReachableEndsAndCleanup() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run intervalRequirementClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn intervalTestProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, region: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let words = List<u64>.make()
  let premises = List<RegionBound>.make()
  let mut regions = List<RegionPoints>.make()
  let mut symbolic = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  let mut flow = emptyIntervalFlow()
  let mut storage = emptyRegionAvailability()
  let found = run regionPoints(walker, owner, region, 
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, &mut regions,
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic, &mut flow, &mut storage)
  return found != usize.MAX
}

effect fn intervalRequirementClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"interval-paths.silk", 0)
  let region = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let universal = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let mut walker = Walker {
    callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>.make(),
    unrun: List<bool>.make(), points: List<Point>.make(), loans: List<Loan>.make(), events: List<Event>.make(),
    frames: List<Frame>.make(), loops: List<Loop>.make(), held: List<List<usize>>.make(),
    definitions: List<Holding>.make(), holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>.make(), scopes: List<Scope>.make(), localCount: 1,
    cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>.make(), loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>.make(), exit: 0, entry: 1,
    outside: false, reason: BorrowStatus.Regions, guarded: List<usize>.make(),
    guardConsumed: Option<Location>.none(), retention: Retention.None, requirements: List<RetentionEdge>.make(),
    settled: true, retentionRelations: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>.make(), openContents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), unretained: List<usize>.make(), contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), storing: false, inherited: BorrowStatus.Checked, storable: List<usize>.make(),
    refinements: List<Refinement>.make(), lexicalHolders: List<usize>.make(),
    paths: List<List<Step>>.make(),
    stores: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    returns: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    sealed: List<Location>.make(),
    unheld: List<Location>.make(),
    escaping: List<usize>.make(),
    supplied: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(),
  }
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, List<Step>.make())
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 5 { drop run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX) at = at + usize.ONE }
  run edge(&mut walker, 1, 2)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 0)
  run edge(&mut walker, 1, 3)
  run edge(&mut walker, 3, 4)
  run edge(&mut walker, 4, 0)
  let mut loan = run symbolicTestLoan(&region, &universal, true)
  loan.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  loan.crossed = false
  run List<Interval>.append(&mut loan.intervals, Interval {from: 1, to: 4, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, cleanup: false})
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move loan)
  run List<Event>.append(&mut walker.events, Event {point: 2, place: Place {root: 0, steps: List<Step>.make()},
    kind: Kind.End, span: Location.make(0, 1), target: Location.make(0, 1), loan: usize.MAX, consumesTarget: 0,
    refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: 0, binders: List<usize>.make()})
  run Testing.expect(run intervalTestProved(&walker, &owner, &region),
    "an early-exit storage end cannot reach this interval's consumer and is not its requirement")
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 3)
  run Testing.expect(!run intervalTestProved(&walker, &owner, &region),
    "the same storage end remains required when its branch reaches the consuming point")
  let mut direct = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  List<usize>.clear(&mut direct[2].next)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 0)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 1)
  run Testing.expect(!run intervalTestProved(&walker, &owner, &region),
    "a back edge that reaches the consumer cannot be pruned as an abandoned branch")
  let mut restored = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  List<usize>.clear(&mut restored[2].next)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 0)
  let mut observed = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  run List<Interval>.append(&mut observed[0].intervals, Interval {from: 2, to: 2, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, cleanup: true})
  run Testing.expect(!run intervalTestProved(&walker, &owner, &region),
    "an abandoned call does not erase a cleanup observer's independent requirement")
  return ()
}

test effect fn ownedInitializationRequiresEveryPathAndPreservesEnds() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run ownedInitializationClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn initializedRelationProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId,
  shorter: &Shared<Lifetime>, longer: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let words = List<u64>.make()
  let premises = List<RegionBound>.make()
  let mut regions = List<RegionPoints>.make()
  let mut symbolic = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  let mut flow = emptyIntervalFlow()
  let mut storage = emptyRegionAvailability()
  let first = run regionPoints(walker, owner, shorter, 
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, &mut regions,
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic, &mut flow, &mut storage)
  let second = run regionPoints(walker, owner, longer, 
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, &mut regions,
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic, &mut flow, &mut storage)
  if first == usize.MAX || second == usize.MAX { return false }
  let mut edges = List<RegionEdge>.make()
  run List<RegionEdge>.append(&mut edges, RegionEdge {shorter: first, longer: second})
  return run solveRegionRequirements(&mut regions, List<RegionEdge>.asSlice(&edges))
}

effect fn ownedInitializationClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"owned-initialization.silk", 0)
  let shorter = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let longer = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let mut walker = Walker {
    callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>.make(),
    unrun: List<bool>.make(), points: List<Point>.make(), loans: List<Loan>.make(), events: List<Event>.make(),
    frames: List<Frame>.make(), loops: List<Loop>.make(), held: List<List<usize>>.make(),
    definitions: List<Holding>.make(), holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>.make(), scopes: List<Scope>.make(), localCount: 2,
    cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>.make(), loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>.make(), exit: 0, entry: 1,
    outside: false, reason: BorrowStatus.Regions, guarded: List<usize>.make(),
    guardConsumed: Option<Location>.none(), retention: Retention.None, requirements: List<RetentionEdge>.make(),
    settled: true, retentionRelations: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>.make(), openContents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), unretained: List<usize>.make(), contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), storing: false, inherited: BorrowStatus.Checked, storable: List<usize>.make(),
    refinements: List<Refinement>.make(), lexicalHolders: List<usize>.make(),
    paths: List<List<Step>>.make(),
    stores: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    returns: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    sealed: List<Location>.make(),
    unheld: List<Location>.make(),
    escaping: List<usize>.make(),
    supplied: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(),
  }
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, List<Step>.make())
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 6 { drop run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX) at = at + usize.ONE }
  at = usize.ONE
  while at < 5 { run edge(&mut walker, at, at + usize.ONE) at = at + usize.ONE }
  run edge(&mut walker, 5, 0)
  let mut first = run symbolicTestLoan(&shorter, &shorter, true)
  first.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  first.crossed = false
  first.created = 2
  let mut second = run symbolicTestLoan(&longer, &longer, true)
  second.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  second.crossed = false
  second.created = 4
  second.place.root = 1
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move first)
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move second)
  let mut initialized = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  initialized[1].initializes = 1
  run Testing.expect(run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "an initialized owned source covers an earlier argument before its fresh borrow")
  let mut alternatives = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  alternatives[1].precision = LoanPrecision.Alternatives
  run Testing.expect(run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "an explicitly known alternative retains its actual initialized storage mask")
  let mut third = run symbolicTestLoan(&longer, &longer, true)
  third.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  third.crossed = false
  third.precision = LoanPrecision.Alternatives
  third.created = 4
  third.place.root = 2
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move third)
  let mut thirdStorage = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  thirdStorage[2].initializes = 2
  let mut uses = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  run List<Interval>.append(&mut uses[0].intervals, Interval {from: 2, to: 5, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, cleanup: false})
  run Testing.expect(run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "every known alternative contributes its own initialized storage mask")
  run List<Event>.append(&mut walker.events, Event {point: 5,
    place: Place {root: 2, steps: List<Step>.make()}, kind: Kind.End,
    span: Location.make(0, 1), target: Location.make(0, 1), loan: usize.MAX, consumesTarget: 0,
    refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: 0, binders: List<usize>.make()})
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "ending one alternative rejects an incoming requirement even while the other remains alive")
  List<Event>.clear(&mut walker.events)
  drop List<Loan>.pop(&mut walker.loans)
  let mut originalUses = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  List<Interval>.clear(&mut originalUses[0].intervals)
  let mut originalStorage = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  originalStorage[2].initializes = usize.MAX
  let mut unknown = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  unknown[1].precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "Unknown provenance cannot acquire availability from a matching initialization")
  let mut restoredPrecision = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  restoredPrecision[1].precision = LoanPrecision.Exact
  let mut delayed = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  delayed[1].initializes = usize.MAX
  delayed[3].initializes = 1
  // The later borrow at 4 cannot be live at the earlier loan's points 2 and 3, which its creation
  // never reaches: a value of a region observed at a point carries only loans whose creation
  // reaches that point, so those points place no validity requirement on its storage.
  run Testing.expect(run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "a requirement at points the later borrow's creation never reaches needs no storage there")
  run edge(&mut walker, 5, 2)
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "storage is not available before its initialization where the later borrow's creation reaches")
  let mut looped = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  drop List<usize>.pop(&mut looped[5].next)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 4)
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "one path bypassing initialization also excludes the later borrow's own required point")
  let mut restored = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  restored[1].initializes = 1
  restored[3].initializes = usize.MAX
  run List<Event>.append(&mut walker.events, Event {point: 2,
    place: Place {root: 1, steps: List<Step>.make()}, kind: Kind.End,
    span: Location.make(0, 1), target: Location.make(0, 1), loan: usize.MAX, consumesTarget: 0,
    refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: 0, binders: List<usize>.make()})
  run Testing.expect(run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "a storage end the later borrow's creation never reaches places no requirement on that borrow")
  run edge(&mut walker, 5, 2)
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "initialization does not erase an actual storage end the later fresh borrow's creation reaches")
  let mut ended = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  drop List<usize>.pop(&mut ended[5].next)
  List<Event>.clear(&mut walker.events)
  let mut cycling = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  cycling[1].initializes = usize.MAX
  cycling[3].initializes = 1
  List<usize>.clear(&mut cycling[1].next)
  run edge(&mut walker, 1, 3)
  run edge(&mut walker, 3, 2)
  run Testing.expect(run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "a rebinding on a CFG cycle the later borrow's creation never reaches places no requirement on that borrow")
  run edge(&mut walker, 5, 2)
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "a root rebound on a CFG cycle the later borrow's creation reaches cannot revive storage for an earlier loan")
  // Meet constituents keep the same owned-storage must proof. An incoming requirement at
  // the join also covers the path that never created this fresh borrow.
  List<Point>.clear(&mut walker.points)
  List<Loan>.clear(&mut walker.loans)
  List<Event>.clear(&mut walker.events)
  walker.localCount = 3
  at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 6 { drop run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX) at = at + usize.ONE }
  at = usize.ONE
  while at < 5 { run edge(&mut walker, at, at + usize.ONE) at = at + usize.ONE }
  run edge(&mut walker, 5, 0)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 5)
  let extra = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 2})
  let mut members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut members, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&longer))
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut members, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&extra))
  let meet = run Lifetime.meet(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&members))
  let mut demand = run symbolicTestLoan(&shorter, &shorter, true)
  demand.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  demand.created = 2
  run List<Interval>.append(&mut demand.intervals, Interval {from: 2, to: 5, definition: usize.MAX, read: usize.MAX, cleanup: false})
  let mut member = run symbolicTestLoan(&meet, &meet, true)
  member.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  member.created = 4
  member.place.root = 1
  let mut companion = run symbolicTestLoan(&longer, &longer, true)
  companion.parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  companion.created = 4
  companion.place.root = 2
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move demand)
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move member)
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move companion)
  let mut beforeSplit = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  beforeSplit[1].initializes = 1
  beforeSplit[2].initializes = 2
  run Testing.expect(run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "an actual meet member uses its owned storage initialized before the branch")
  let mut onlyBranch = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  onlyBranch[1].initializes = usize.MAX
  onlyBranch[3].initializes = 1
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "one contributing meet member still excludes an incoming join use on the path bypassing initialization")
  let mut allPaths = List<Point>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.points)
  allPaths[1].initializes = 1
  allPaths[3].initializes = usize.MAX
  let mut unrelatedBorrow = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  unrelatedBorrow[1].borrowed = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&extra))
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "membership in retained lifetimes alone cannot authenticate a different borrowed atom")
  let mut actualBorrow = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  actualBorrow[1].borrowed = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.some(Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&meet))
  run List<Event>.append(&mut walker.events, Event {point: 5,
    place: Place {root: 1, steps: List<Step>.make()}, kind: Kind.End,
    span: Location.make(0, 1), target: Location.make(0, 1), loan: usize.MAX, consumesTarget: 0,
    refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: 0, binders: List<usize>.make()})
  run Testing.expect(!run initializedRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &shorter, &longer),
    "a contributing meet member's End still rejects incoming use while the other source remains alive")

  return ()
}


test effect fn offeredMeetRequiresEverySource() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run offeredMeetClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn offeredMeetRelationProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId,
  offered: &Shared<Lifetime>, wanted: &Shared<Lifetime>) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let words = List<u64>.make()
  let premises = List<RegionBound>.make()
  let mut symbolic = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  let mut obligations = List<SafetyObligation>.make()
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, retentionTestRelation(offered, wanted, false))
  return run localRelationsProved(walker, owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&obligations),
    List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises), &mut symbolic, 
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, false)
}

effect fn offeredMeetClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"offered-meet.silk", 0)
  let first = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let second = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let wanted = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 2})
  let universal = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let mut walker = Walker {
    callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>.make(),
    unrun: List<bool>.make(), points: List<Point>.make(), loans: List<Loan>.make(), events: List<Event>.make(),
    frames: List<Frame>.make(), loops: List<Loop>.make(), held: List<List<usize>>.make(),
    definitions: List<Holding>.make(), holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>.make(), scopes: List<Scope>.make(), localCount: 3,
    cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>.make(), loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>.make(), exit: 0, entry: 1,
    outside: false, reason: BorrowStatus.Regions, guarded: List<usize>.make(),
    guardConsumed: Option<Location>.none(), retention: Retention.None, requirements: List<RetentionEdge>.make(),
    settled: true, retentionRelations: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>.make(), openContents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), unretained: List<usize>.make(), contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), storing: false, inherited: BorrowStatus.Checked, storable: List<usize>.make(),
    refinements: List<Refinement>.make(), lexicalHolders: List<usize>.make(),
    paths: List<List<Step>>.make(),
    stores: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    returns: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    sealed: List<Location>.make(),
    unheld: List<Location>.make(),
    escaping: List<usize>.make(),
    supplied: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(),
  }
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, List<Step>.make())
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 4 { drop run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX) at = at + usize.ONE }
  run edge(&mut walker, 1, 2)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 3)
  run edge(&mut walker, 3, 0)
  let mut one = run symbolicTestLoan(&first, &universal, false)
  one.created = 1
  let mut two = run symbolicTestLoan(&second, &universal, false)
  two.created = 1
  two.place.root = 1
  let mut consumer = run symbolicTestLoan(&wanted, &universal, false)
  consumer.created = 3
  consumer.place.root = 2
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move one)
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move two)
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move consumer)
  let mut members = List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make()
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut members, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&first))
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut members, Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&second))
  let offered = run Lifetime.meet(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&members))
  run Testing.expect(run offeredMeetRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &offered, &wanted),
    "both known source regions cover the finite consumer of their meet")
  run List<Event>.append(&mut walker.events, Event {point: 2,
    place: Place {root: 1, steps: List<Step>.make()}, kind: Kind.End,
    span: Location.make(0, 1), target: Location.make(0, 1), loan: usize.MAX, consumesTarget: 0,
    refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: 0, binders: List<usize>.make()})
  run Testing.expect(!run offeredMeetRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &offered, &wanted),
    "one ended source prevents the meet from covering a later consumer")
  List<Event>.clear(&mut walker.events)
  let missing = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 3})
  run List<Shared<Lifetime>>.append(&mut members, move missing)
  let incomplete = run Lifetime.meet(List<Shared<Lifetime>>.asSlice(&members))
  run Testing.expect(!run offeredMeetRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &incomplete, &wanted),
    "a known member never hides another member with no authenticated loan mapping")
  let mut restored = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  restored[1].precision = LoanPrecision.Unknown
  run Testing.expect(!run offeredMeetRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &offered, &wanted),
    "a known member never hides another member's unknown loan mapping")
  let mut exact = List<Loan>.asMutSlice(&mut walker.loans)
  exact[1].precision = LoanPrecision.Exact
  exact[1].parent = Option<Shared<Lifetime>>.none()
  exact[1].local = true
  run Testing.expect(!run offeredMeetRelationProved(&walker, &owner, &offered, &universal),
    "one function-local constituent cannot acquire the other member's universal parent")
  return ()
}


test effect fn regionChoicesKeepEverySourceConstraint() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> {
  let mut allocator = Allocator.systemAllocatorProvider()
  return run regionChoiceClaims() |> Effect.provideMut<Allocator>(&mut allocator)
}

effect fn choiceRelationsProved(walker: &Walker, owner: &DeclarationId, obligations: &[SafetyObligation]) -> bool
! OutOfMemoryError ? &mut Allocator {
  let words = List<u64>.make()
  let premises = List<RegionBound>.make()
  let mut symbolic = List<SymbolicRegion>.make()
  return run localRelationsProved(walker, owner, obligations, List<RegionBound>.asSlice(&premises),
    &mut symbolic,  List<u64>.asSlice(&words),
    List<u64>.asSlice(&words), 0, false)
}

effect fn regionChoiceClaims() -> ()
! InvalidModulePath | OutOfMemoryError | AssertionError<'static> ? &mut Allocator {
  let owner = run capturedTestOwner(b"region-choices.silk", 0)
  let source = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let choice = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 1})
  let useRegion = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Local {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 2})
  let universal = run Shared<Lifetime>.make(Lifetime.Parameter {declaration: DeclarationId.copy(&owner), ordinal: 0})
  let mut walker = Walker {
    callerRetentions: List<CallerRetention>.make(),
    unrun: List<bool>.make(), points: List<Point>.make(), loans: List<Loan>.make(), events: List<Event>.make(),
    frames: List<Frame>.make(), loops: List<Loop>.make(), held: List<List<usize>>.make(),
    definitions: List<Holding>.make(), holdingSources: List<HoldingSource>.make(), scopes: List<Scope>.make(), localCount: 3,
    cleanup: List<LoanCleanup>.make(), loopCleanup: List<LoopCleanup>.make(), exit: 0, entry: 1,
    outside: false, reason: BorrowStatus.Regions, guarded: List<usize>.make(),
    guardConsumed: Option<Location>.none(), retention: Retention.None, requirements: List<RetentionEdge>.make(),
    settled: true, retentionRelations: List<ImpliedGroup>.make(), wholeHolds: List<WholeHold>.make(), openContents: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), unretained: List<usize>.make(), contested: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(), storing: false, inherited: BorrowStatus.Checked, storable: List<usize>.make(),
    refinements: List<Refinement>.make(), lexicalHolders: List<usize>.make(),
    paths: List<List<Step>>.make(),
    stores: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    returns: List<StoreWindow>.make(),
    sealed: List<Location>.make(),
    unheld: List<Location>.make(),
    escaping: List<usize>.make(),
    supplied: List<Shared<Lifetime>>.make(),
  }
  run List<List<Step>>.append(&mut walker.paths, List<Step>.make())
  let mut at = usize.ZERO
  while at < 4 { drop run newPoint(&mut walker, usize.MAX) at = at + usize.ONE }
  run edge(&mut walker, 1, 2)
  run edge(&mut walker, 2, 3)
  run edge(&mut walker, 3, 0)
  let mut producer = run symbolicTestLoan(&source, &universal, false)
  producer.created = 1
  let mut consumer = run symbolicTestLoan(&useRegion, &universal, false)
  consumer.created = 3
  consumer.place.root = 1
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move producer)
  run List<Loan>.append(&mut walker.loans, move consumer)
  let mut obligations = List<SafetyObligation>.make()
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, retentionTestRelation(&choice, &useRegion, false))
  run Testing.expect(!run choiceRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&obligations)),
    "an unmapped local atom remains unproved without a typing witness")
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, SafetyObligation.RegionChoice {
    origin: Origin {node: 1, location: Location.make(0, 1)}, region: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&choice)})
  run Testing.expect(run choiceRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&obligations)),
    "an authenticated unconstrained choice can cover this finite consumer")
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, retentionTestRelation(&source, &choice, false))
  run Testing.expect(run choiceRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&obligations)),
    "a later source relation constrains the same choice")
  run List<Event>.append(&mut walker.events, Event {point: 2,
    place: Place {root: 0, steps: List<Step>.make()}, kind: Kind.End,
    span: Location.make(0, 1), target: Location.make(0, 1), loan: usize.MAX, consumesTarget: 0,
    refiner: usize.MAX, refinedDepth: 0, binders: List<usize>.make()})
  run Testing.expect(!run choiceRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&obligations)),
    "consumer requirements cross the choice and still fail beyond its actual source's end")
  List<Event>.clear(&mut walker.events)
  List<SafetyObligation>.truncate(&mut obligations, 1)
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, SafetyObligation.RegionChoice {
    origin: Origin {node: 0, location: Location.make(0, 1)}, region: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&choice)})
  run Testing.expect(!run choiceRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&obligations)),
    "the choice witness must name its actual origin")
  List<SafetyObligation>.clear(&mut obligations)
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, SafetyObligation.RegionChoice {
    origin: Origin {node: 1, location: Location.make(0, 1)}, region: Shared<Lifetime>.clone(&choice)})
  run List<SafetyObligation>.append(&mut obligations, retentionTestRelation(&choice, &universal, false))
  run Testing.expect(!run choiceRelationsProved(&walker, &owner, List<SafetyObligation>.asSlice(&obligations)),
    "a body-scoped choice is never a universal premise")
  return ()
}
